meter","If there is a fire alarm system, a report from the alarm company is required (per the online application form)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received 10 or more business days before settlement","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received 7 business days before settlement (source wording)","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received fewer than 4 business days before settlement","amount":"$161.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://forms.gle/oWLh33S1kuggYuRQ8$t$, $t$http://www.bridgetonfire.com/uniform-fire-code$t$, $j$[{"url":"http://www.bridgetonfire.com/uniform-fire-code","label":"Official source (bridgetonfire.com)"},{"url":"https://static1.squarespace.com/static/51cc4632e4b06e55251db119/t/691f23865714647f5f7c666a/1763648390990/Occupancy+%26+Smoke+Certificates.pdf","label":"Official source (static1.squarespace.com)"},{"url":"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd9PvQCoB-cH5v1UqIaPvFMeDzejV1zzNEnuFMw0yH7LAaFng/viewform","label":"Official source (docs.google.com)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.historicgreenwichnj.org/planning-documents/","label":"Official source (historicgreenwichnj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.historicgreenwichnj.org/municipal-directory/","label":"Official source (historicgreenwichnj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.historicgreenwichnj.org/fire-rescue/","label":"Official source (historicgreenwichnj.org)"},{"url":"http://www.bridgetonfire.com/department","label":"Official source (bridgetonfire.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The City of Bridgeton Fire Department is the local enforcing agency who is responsible for the enforcement of the Uniform Fire Safety Act within the City of Bridgeton, Hopewell Township, Greenwich Township, Stow Creek Township, Shiloh Borough, Fairfield Township, Downe Township, and Alloway Township.$t$, $t$c68236ac80f780462a18b518cc9457b6baa986c60d2a21ddc73656373fbd079f$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":24,"q_ok":22,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0606.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0606.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0607$t$, $t$Hopewell Township$t$, $t$CUMBERLAND$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$official_process_found$t$, $t$Resale / Continued Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Not required for sales, per Hopewell Township. Confirm with the office if the buyer's lender or title company asks.","Contact: Dave Elwell, Housing, Code Enforcement and Property Maintenance · (856) 455-1230 x- 117 · zoninghousing@hopewelltwp-nj.com","How to apply: No Township Certificate of Occupancy is needed for a sale since January 1, 2026. The seller still needs the smoke / CO / 911 house numbering inspection from the City of Bridgeton Fire Department (see fire section) and County Health Department water and septic certifications, all at least 10 days before closing.","Also: Water and septic certifications: Drinking water quality and septic certifications from the Cumberland County Health Department are required before closing; records must reach the Health Department at least 10 days before closing.","Also: 911 house numbering: Checked with the smoke/CO inspection before closing."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://hopewelltwp-nj.com/government/departments/housing-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://hopewelltwp-nj.com/buying-or-selling-your-home-in-hopewell/","label":"Official source (hopewelltwp-nj.com)"},{"url":"https://hopewelltwp-nj.com/government/departments/housing-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (hopewelltwp-nj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Please be advised that, effective January 1, 2026 , Hopewell Township, Cumberland County will no longer require local Certificate of Occupancy (CO) or Smoke Certification inspections in connection with the sale of residential properties.$t$, $t$3761ab27d32c14870c3c6033473d94b0213f755589a6471d95b073ca0963caff$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":18,"q_ok":18,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0607.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0607.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0607$t$, $t$Hopewell Township$t$, $t$CUMBERLAND$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: City of Bridgeton Fire Department, Bureau of Fire Prevention (town fire bureau)","Contact: Jack Justice Jr., Fire Official and Chief of Department · 856-451-0091 · justicej@cityofbridgeton.com","Apply: Submit the request 2 to 3 weeks before settlement; the lowest fee applies when the request is received 10 or more business days before settlement.","How to apply: Fill out the online 'CO and Smoke Certification Application' (Google Form) linked from the Bridgeton Fire Department's Uniform Fire Code page, picking Hopewell Township as the municipality. Payment is due at the time of the inspection by check or money order payable to the City of Bridgeton Fire Department (the form says an online payment link will be on the invoice). Re-inspection for a failed or no-show inspection costs the same as the first inspection. The certificate is emailed to the address given and is valid for 90 days. Questions: firedepartment@cityofbridgeton.com or 856-451-0090 / 856-451-0091.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 4/30/2026: Jack Justice, Jr. · (856) 451-0091 · firedepartment@cityofbridgeton.com","Hopewell adds a 911 house numbering check to the Bridgeton smoke/CO inspection; inspections must be scheduled and passed at least 10 days before the closing date","Smoke alarms (UL listed) on every level; battery-only alarms must be the 10-year sealed battery type, and hardwired alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","Basement smoke alarm at the bottom of the stairwell, on the ceiling (not between joists)","A 10-year sealed smoke alarm in every bedroom","Smoke alarms and CO alarms must be less than 10 years old and working","Carbon monoxide alarm in the hallway within 10 feet of all bedrooms","House numbers at least 4 inches high, contrasting color, permanently fixed and visible from the street","Homes with solar panels, a backup generator or battery storage need a permanent printed 'Caution: Multiple Sources of Power' label at the main electrical panel and the electric meter","If there is a fire alarm system, a report from the alarm company is required (per the online application form)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received 10 or more business days before settlement","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received 7 business days before settlement (source wording)","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received fewer than 4 business days before settlement","amount":"$161.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://forms.gle/oWLh33S1kuggYuRQ8$t$, $t$http://www.bridgetonfire.com/uniform-fire-code$t$, $j$[{"url":"http://www.bridgetonfire.com/uniform-fire-code","label":"Official source (bridgetonfire.com)"},{"url":"https://static1.squarespace.com/static/51cc4632e4b06e55251db119/t/691f23865714647f5f7c666a/1763648390990/Occupancy+%26+Smoke+Certificates.pdf","label":"Official source (static1.squarespace.com)"},{"url":"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd9PvQCoB-cH5v1UqIaPvFMeDzejV1zzNEnuFMw0yH7LAaFng/viewform","label":"Official source (docs.google.com)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://hopewelltwp-nj.com/buying-or-selling-your-home-in-hopewell/","label":"Official source (hopewelltwp-nj.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The City of Bridgeton Fire Department is the local enforcing agency who is responsible for the enforcement of the Uniform Fire Safety Act within the City of Bridgeton, Hopewell Township, Greenwich Township, Stow Creek Township, Shiloh Borough, Fairfield Township, Downe Township, and Alloway Township.$t$, $t$368f6aab586617e9c51255d5abaa2c6f4861ec234947577be31859e65bb96340$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":18,"q_ok":18,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0607.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0607.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0611$t$, $t$Shiloh Borough$t$, $t$CUMBERLAND$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy for a new occupant of an existing building (zoning permit first)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Shiloh (Housing Code Official: Upper Deerfield Township; zoning permit from the Borough Zoning Officer)","Contact: Teresa Warburton, Housing Code Official (Upper Deerfield Township, serving Shiloh) · 856-455-9591 · twarburton@upperdeerfield.com","How to apply: No resale application is posted. The 1999 ordinance says a zoning permit from the Zoning Officer must be issued before a certificate of occupancy goes to a new occupant of an existing building; the Borough's zoning permit form is at https://shilohborough.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/SHL_ZONING_PERMIT.pdf. Contact the Housing Code Official (Teresa Warburton, Upper Deerfield Township, 856-455-9591) or the Borough office (856-455-3054, clerk@shilohborough.com) to arrange the certificate of occupancy.","Also: Zoning permit before the certificate of occupancy: The 1999 ordinance requires a zoning permit from the Zoning Officer before a certificate of occupancy is issued to a new occupant ($10 in 1999)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of occupancy, per dwelling unit (1999 Development Ordinance; certified check or bank money order payable to the Borough of Shiloh)","amount":"$25"},{"label":"Zoning permit, which must be issued before a certificate of occupancy for a new occupant (1999 Development Ordinance)","amount":"$10"}]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://shilohborough.com/government/other-officials/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://shilohborough.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Shiloh-Development-Ord-As-Amended-1999.pdf","label":"Official source (shilohborough.com)"},{"url":"https://shilohborough.com/government/other-officials/","label":"Official source (shilohborough.com)"},{"url":"https://shilohborough.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/SHL_REORG2025Agenda.pdf","label":"Official source (shilohborough.com)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/administration/construction-code/","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$B. Requirement for Issuance of Zoning Permit Prior to Other Permits. A zoning permit shall be issued by the Zoning Officer before the issuance of either a certificate of occupancy to a new occupant of an existing building or portion of an existing building or portion of an existing building, or before the issuance of a building permit.$t$, $t$a8b29dbdf049a7fd7bfd5ca2f05abc989c9994002d2532c0d384b883d97bde3f$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":12,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0611.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0611.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0611$t$, $t$Shiloh Borough$t$, $t$CUMBERLAND$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: City of Bridgeton Fire Department, Bureau of Fire Prevention (town fire bureau)","Contact: Jack Justice Jr., Fire Official and Chief of Department, City of Bridgeton Fire Department · 856-451-0091 · firedepartment@cityofbridgeton.com","Apply: Submit the request 2 to 3 weeks before settlement; the lowest fee applies when the request is received 10 or more business days before settlement","How to apply: Fill out the online 'CO and Smoke Certification Application' (Google Form) linked from the Bridgeton Fire Department's Uniform Fire Code page and pick Shiloh Borough as the municipality. Payment is by check or money order payable to the City of Bridgeton Fire Department (the form says an online payment link will be on the invoice). The certificate is valid for 90 days. Questions: firedepartment@cityofbridgeton.com or 856-451-0090 (guideline sheet) / (856) 451-0091 (Bureau of Fire Prevention).","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 4/30/2026: Jack Justice, Jr. · (856) 451-0091 · firedepartment@cityofbridgeton.com","Smoke alarms (UL listed) on every level; battery-only alarms must be the 10-year sealed battery type, and hardwired alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","Basement smoke alarm at the bottom of the stairwell, on the ceiling (not between joists)","A 10-year sealed smoke alarm in every bedroom","Smoke alarms and CO alarms must be less than 10 years old and working","Carbon monoxide alarm in the hallway within 10 feet of all bedrooms","House numbers at least 4 inches high, contrasting color, permanently fixed and visible from the street","Homes with solar panels, a backup generator or battery storage need a permanent printed 'Caution: Multiple Sources of Power' label at the main electrical panel and the electric meter","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received 10 or more business days before settlement","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received 7 business days before settlement (source wording)","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received fewer than 4 business days before settlement","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection for a failed or no-show inspection: same fee as the initial inspection tier","amount":"$45.00 to $161.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://forms.gle/oWLh33S1kuggYuRQ8$t$, $t$http://www.bridgetonfire.com/uniform-fire-code$t$, $j$[{"url":"http://www.bridgetonfire.com/uniform-fire-code","label":"Official source (bridgetonfire.com)"},{"url":"https://static1.squarespace.com/static/51cc4632e4b06e55251db119/t/691f23865714647f5f7c666a/1763648390990/Occupancy+%26+Smoke+Certificates.pdf","label":"Official source (static1.squarespace.com)"},{"url":"https://forms.gle/oWLh33S1kuggYuRQ8","label":"Official source (forms.gle)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The City of Bridgeton Fire Department is the local enforcing agency who is responsible for the enforcement of the Uniform Fire Safety Act within the City of Bridgeton, Hopewell Township, Greenwich Township, Stow Creek Township, Shiloh Borough, Fairfield Township, Downe Township, and Alloway Township.$t$, $t$039e92b89e1384814143020bfb54b2fde98f5a0dbc5a4dcdab16941db71df07c$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":12,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0611.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0611.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0612$t$, $t$Stow Creek Township$t$, $t$CUMBERLAND$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy (sale property)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Stow Creek Township Office of Housing and Zoning (Housing Officer)","Contact: Neal Sheppard, Housing Officer and Zoning Officer · 856-455-8640 · Zoninghousing@stowcreektwp.org","How to apply: Fill out the Township's Certificate of Occupancy Application (check 'Sale Property', give owner, buyer and agent details) and mail it with the $50.00 check to Stow Creek Township, Attn: Zoning/Housing Department, PO Box 308, Shiloh, NJ 08353. Also email copies of the application and check to the Zoning Officer (Zoninghousing@stowcreektwp.org). Inspections must be completed and passed before occupancy or before personal items are placed in the home.","Remove trash and debris inside and out; cut high grass and weeds; fix tripping hazards on walks, steps and driveways","Sheds, garages, fences and pools kept sound; pool gates self-closing and self-latching","Exterior walls, siding, roof, gutters, foundation and chimney in good repair; scrape and paint peeling paint","House numbers visible from the street, plus a 3 foot white 911 post at the end of the driveway with numbers on the left, right and street sides","Handrails on stairs with more than 4 risers; guardrails at least 30 inches high","Windows open easily and stay open, no broken glass, tight-fitting screens; exterior doors open from inside without a key","Bedroom and bathroom privacy locks; bathroom window or exhaust fan; dryer vented outside","Plumbing working and sanitary; water heater gives at least 110 degree water and has a discharge pipe about 6 inches from the floor","Heating system safe; fuel-burning appliances clear of combustibles; electrical safe and workmanlike","At least two outlets in every habitable room; grounded outlets in bathrooms and laundry; GFCI outlets within 6 feet of water and outdoors","Carbon monoxide detector outside the bedroom areas","Work done without permits must be permitted and finaled","Proof of extermination if insects or rodents are found","Also: Fire inspection report from the Bridgeton Fire Department: The Township's housing inspection list says a passing fire inspection report is required from the Bridgeton Fire Department.","Also: Septic certification or waiver: If there is a septic system, a passing certification or waiver from the County Health Department is required.","Also: Water certificate: A passing water certificate from the County Health Department is required.","Also: Chimney inspection for wood stoves: If there is a wood burning stove, a passing inspection report from a licensed chimney contractor or inspector is required.","Also: Open or missing construction permits: Work done without building permits must be permitted and final inspections completed (Upper Deerfield construction office)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of Occupancy application (sale property or rental unit)","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://stowcreektwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/SC-CO-Application-2025.pdf$t$, $t$https://stowcreektwp.org/planning-zoning-and-housing/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://stowcreektwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Stow-Creek-Township-Land-Development-Ordinance-2025.pdf","label":"Official source (stowcreektwp.org)"},{"url":"https://stowcreektwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/SC-CO-Application-2025.pdf","label":"Official source (stowcreektwp.org)"},{"url":"https://stowcreektwp.org/planning-zoning-and-housing/","label":"Official source (stowcreektwp.org)"},{"url":"https://stowcreektwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Common-Violations-1-2.pdf","label":"Official source (stowcreektwp.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$D. A certificate of occupancy shall be required in any of the following circumstances:$t$, $t$ecfbbf250a62a56d32878a976eff76f19264cfa1444813d5804069f9a1bf2dcb$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":15,"q_ok":15,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0612.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0612.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0612$t$, $t$Stow Creek Township$t$, $t$CUMBERLAND$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: City of Bridgeton Fire Department, Bureau of Fire Prevention (town fire bureau)","Contact: Jack Justice Jr., Fire Official and Chief of Department, City of Bridgeton Fire Department · 856-451-0091 · firedepartment@cityofbridgeton.com","Apply: Submit the request 2 to 3 weeks before settlement; the lowest fee applies when the request is received 10 or more business days before settlement","How to apply: Fill out the online 'CO and Smoke Certification Application' (Google Form) linked from the Bridgeton Fire Department's Uniform Fire Code page and pick Stow Creek Township as the municipality. Payment is by check or money order payable to the City of Bridgeton Fire Department (the form says an online payment link will be on the invoice). The certificate is valid for 90 days. Questions: firedepartment@cityofbridgeton.com or 856-451-0090 (guideline sheet) / (856) 451-0091 (Bureau of Fire Prevention).","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 4/30/2026: Jack Justice, Jr. · (856) 451-0091 · firedepartment@cityofbridgeton.com","Smoke alarms (UL listed) on every level; battery-only alarms must be the 10-year sealed battery type, and hardwired alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","Basement smoke alarm at the bottom of the stairwell, on the ceiling (not between joists)","A 10-year sealed smoke alarm in every bedroom","Smoke alarms and CO alarms must be less than 10 years old and working","Carbon monoxide alarm in the hallway within 10 feet of all bedrooms","House numbers at least 4 inches high, contrasting color, permanently fixed and visible from the street","Homes with solar panels, a backup generator or battery storage need a permanent printed 'Caution: Multiple Sources of Power' label at the main electrical panel and the electric meter","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received 10 or more business days before settlement","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received 7 business days before settlement (source wording)","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, 1-2 family, request received fewer than 4 business days before settlement","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection for a failed or no-show inspection: same fee as the initial inspection tier","amount":"$45.00 to $161.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://forms.gle/oWLh33S1kuggYuRQ8$t$, $t$http://www.bridgetonfire.com/uniform-fire-code$t$, $j$[{"url":"http://www.bridgetonfire.com/uniform-fire-code","label":"Official source (bridgetonfire.com)"},{"url":"https://static1.squarespace.com/static/51cc4632e4b06e55251db119/t/691f23865714647f5f7c666a/1763648390990/Occupancy+%26+Smoke+Certificates.pdf","label":"Official source (static1.squarespace.com)"},{"url":"https://forms.gle/oWLh33S1kuggYuRQ8","label":"Official source (forms.gle)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The City of Bridgeton Fire Department is the local enforcing agency who is responsible for the enforcement of the Uniform Fire Safety Act within the City of Bridgeton, Hopewell Township, Greenwich Township, Stow Creek Township, Shiloh Borough, Fairfield Township, Downe Township, and Alloway Township.$t$, $t$5e8b39e8e4390e30059c4b17ee991d034ad0cf65eac130b30628a799ce4f42e5$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":15,"q_ok":15,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0612.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0612.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0613$t$, $t$Upper Deerfield Township$t$, $t$CUMBERLAND$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy (Continued Certificate of Occupancy / certificate of property compliance)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Upper Deerfield Township (Housing Officer and Fire Marshal inspections)","Contact: Anthony Lamanteer, Jr., Township Housing Officer (also Zoning Officer) · 856-455-9591 · tlamanteer@upperdeerfield.com","Apply: Request the inspection 5 or more business days before closing for the lower fee","How to apply: No application form is posted online. Contact the Housing Officer (Anthony Lamanteer, Jr., tlamanteer@upperdeerfield.com, 856-455-9591; office hours Monday, Tuesday and Thursday 8:30 to 4:30) at the Municipal Building, 1325 Highway 77, Seabrook, NJ 08302, to request the certificate of occupancy inspection before closing."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Residential (single family, apartment, townhouse, mobile home or other dwelling unit), request received 5 or more business days before closing (Ordinance 892, adopted September 17, 2026)","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Residential, request received 4 or fewer business days before closing (Ordinance 892, adopted September 17, 2026)","amount":"$150"}]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://upperdeerfield.com/administration/housing-zoning/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ORD-892-Amending-Certificate-of-Occupancy.pdf","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ORD-892-final-Notice-Amending-Certificate-of-Occupancy.pdf","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/21-66-Continued-Certificate-of-Occupancy-Based-on-Seller-Self-Inspection-Copy.pdf","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/02-19-2026-Short-Minutes.pdf","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/02-05-2026-Short-Minutes.pdf","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/26-44-Appointing-Housing-Officer.pdf","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/administration/housing-zoning/","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Every application for a review and issuance of a certificate of occupancy as stipulated in § 303-6 of this chapter shall be accompanied by the fees normally required in connection with:$t$, $t$a3431f96184e01096d32c61681f9b6e455e382d514d7ed5dc3f5af819c59d3f7$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0613.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0613.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0613$t$, $t$Upper Deerfield Township$t$, $t$CUMBERLAND$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Upper Deerfield Township Fire Safety (Fire Marshal) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Chris Williams, Fire Inspector/Fire Marshal (Fire Safety Official, Director) · 856-455-9591 · cwilliams@upperdeerfield.com","Apply: Request 5 or more business days before closing for the lower Certificate of Occupancy fee","How to apply: The smoke/CO check is done with the Township Certificate of Occupancy inspection; arrange it through the Housing Officer (856-455-9591, tlamanteer@upperdeerfield.com). Fire Safety office: Chris Williams, 856-455-9591 or 856-451-3811 Ext. 143, cwilliams@upperdeerfield.com.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 12/19/2022: Christopher Williams · (856) 455-9591 · cwilliams@upperdeerfield.com","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Combined Township Certificate of Occupancy inspection, 5 or more business days before closing (the Township says the CO fee covers the housing and Fire Marshal certifications)","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Combined Township Certificate of Occupancy inspection, 4 or fewer business days before closing (same note)","amount":"$150"}]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://upperdeerfield.com/public-safety/fire-safety/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/public-safety/fire-safety/","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/administration/directory-of-officials/","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/02-19-2026-Short-Minutes.pdf","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/21-66-Continued-Certificate-of-Occupancy-Based-on-Seller-Self-Inspection-Copy.pdf","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://upperdeerfield.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ORD-892-Amending-Certificate-of-Occupancy.pdf","label":"Official source (upperdeerfield.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Fire Safety Official Chris Williams, Director Manuel Aquilar, Deputy Phone: 856-451-3811 Ext. 143$t$, $t$40f184e873e66d79a1bed9564e2c26db64058f5d238ad4941bcdc02fc0325eee$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0613.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0613.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0614$t$, $t$Vineland$t$, $t$CUMBERLAND$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Inspection / Continued Certification of Occupancy (CCO) for resale$t$, $j$["Issued by: Vineland Fire Department, Fire Prevention Division","Contact: Brian Murray, Sr., Fire Official · (856) 794-2338 · Bmurray@vinelandcity.org","Apply: File as soon as a settlement date is set; at least 4 business days are needed, and filing more than 10 days before closing gets the lower fee","How to apply: As soon as a settlement date is set, file the resale application in person at the Fire Administration building, 400 W. Plum St., Vineland (the application is in triplicate and must be completed in person; a watermarked sample is online). At least 4 business days are needed. Pay by check, cash or money order; fees are per unit and depend on how early you file. If the home fails, a new application and fee are needed before the reinspection. For vacant or uninhabitable homes the buyer can file a Certificate of Transfer of Title (CTT) affidavit together with the CCO application.","All construction permits closed before applying; unpermitted basement, garage or attic conversions are checked","No basement bedrooms without proper egress; zoning approval for duplex or triplex use; open Code Enforcement violations closed","Utilities on at the time of inspection","Exterior walls, gutters, foundation and accessory structures sound; yard free of trash, debris and abandoned vehicles","House numbers at least 4 inches high, contrasting and readable from the street","Stairs, decks, porches and balconies sound; guardrails on landings or porches 30 inches high; handrails where there are 3 or more risers","No keyed deadbolts on the inside of exit doors; bedroom doors close and latch","In-ground pools fenced with self-closing, self-latching gates","Smoke alarm on each level and within 10 feet of sleeping areas; sealed battery units unless hardwired alarms already exist (hardwired must be kept)","Carbon monoxide alarm near bedrooms where there are fuel-burning appliances or an attached garage","Homes with a generator, solar or battery storage need a printed 'Caution Multiple Sources of Power' label at the electrical panel and meter box","No excessive peeling paint in pre-1978 homes; windows open and stay open with no broken glass; no holes in walls, ceilings or floors","Heater, water heater and chimney in working order; bathroom exhaust fan or window","Electrical free of hazards (covers on outlets and boxes, no open panel holes, no taped splices); an electrical certification may be required","Toilets flush without leaks, hot and cold water work, water heater bonding strap and relief valve pipe 2 to 6 inches off the floor","Also: Open construction permits and unpermitted conversions: All construction permits must be closed out before applying; basement, garage or attic conversions without permits are checked (Licenses and Inspections, 856-794-4113).","Also: Zoning approval for duplex or multi-family use: Duplex and multi-family (15 units or fewer) owners should contact the Zoning Department before listing to confirm the use is conforming (856-794-4113).","Also: Open Code Enforcement violations: Any open Code Enforcement violations must be closed out (856-794-3806).","Also: Electrical certification: An electrical certification may be required."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale inspection (CCO), per unit, filed more than 10 days before closing","amount":"$125.00"},{"label":"Resale inspection (CCO), per unit, filed 4 to 10 days before closing","amount":"$200.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection (a new application is needed before a reinspection)","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Certificate of Transfer of Title affidavit (buyer, for vacant or uninhabitable homes), more than 10 days before closing","amount":"$25"},{"label":"Certificate of Transfer of Title affidavit, under 10 days before closing","amount":"$50"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$http://fire.vinelandcity.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Website-CCO-App-w-watermark.pdf$t$, $t$https://fire.vinelandcity.org/selling-your-home/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://fire.vinelandcity.org/selling-your-home/","label":"Official source (fire.vinelandcity.org)"},{"url":"http://fire.vinelandcity.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Website-CCO-App-w-watermark.pdf","label":"Official source (fire.vinelandcity.org)"},{"url":"https://fire.vinelandcity.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/RESIDENTIAL-DWELLING-RESALE-CHECKLIST-.pdf","label":"Official source (fire.vinelandcity.org)"},{"url":"https://www.vinelandcity.org/forms/","label":"Official source (vinelandcity.org)"},{"url":"https://www.vinelandcity.org/departments-contact-directory/","label":"Official source (vinelandcity.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$As is in most municipalities, the City of Vineland requires the owner intending to sell their home, duplex or multi-family units to obtain a Certificate of Inspection prior to settlement.$t$, $t$2754243079dda5bdd804b61d6a768672dd8f5eacde74101c249be764b10a9372$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0614.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0614.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0614$t$, $t$Vineland$t$, $t$CUMBERLAND$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Vineland Fire Department, Fire Prevention Division (same inspection as the resale CCO) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Brian Murray, Sr., Fire Official · (856) 794-2338 · Bmurray@vinelandcity.org","Apply: At least 4 business days; more than 10 days before closing for the lower fee","How to apply: As soon as a settlement date is set, file the resale application in person at the Fire Administration building, 400 W. Plum St., Vineland (the application is in triplicate and must be completed in person; a watermarked sample is online). At least 4 business days are needed. Pay by check, cash or money order; fees are per unit and depend on how early you file. If the home fails, a new application and fee are needed before the reinspection. For vacant or uninhabitable homes the buyer can file a Certificate of Transfer of Title (CTT) affidavit together with the CCO application.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 6/10/2025: Brian J Murray Sr · (856) 794-4000 · Bmurray@vinelandcity.org","Smoke alarm on each level and within 10 feet of sleeping areas; sealed 10-year battery units unless hardwired alarms already exist (hardwired must be kept)","Carbon monoxide alarm near bedrooms where there are fuel-burning appliances or an attached garage","Combination 10-year smoke and CO alarms recommended","Printed 'Caution Multiple Sources of Power' label at the electrical panel and meter box for homes with a generator, solar or battery storage","House numbers at least 4 inches high","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale inspection (CCO), per unit, filed more than 10 days before closing","amount":"$125.00"},{"label":"Resale inspection (CCO), per unit, filed 4 to 10 days before closing","amount":"$200.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection (a new application is needed before a reinspection)","amount":"$50"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$http://fire.vinelandcity.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Website-CCO-App-w-watermark.pdf$t$, $t$https://fire.vinelandcity.org/selling-your-home/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://fire.vinelandcity.org/selling-your-home/","label":"Official source (fire.vinelandcity.org)"},{"url":"https://fire.vinelandcity.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/RESIDENTIAL-DWELLING-RESALE-CHECKLIST-.pdf","label":"Official source (fire.vinelandcity.org)"},{"url":"https://fire.vinelandcity.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/NEW-2025-REAR-OF-CCO-APPLICATION-6-25.pdf","label":"Official source (fire.vinelandcity.org)"},{"url":"https://fire.vinelandcity.org/welcome-fire-marshall/","label":"Official source (fire.vinelandcity.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Inspections filed more than 10 days prior to the closing date are charged at a rate of $125.00 per unit.$t$, $t$b923f029af6b0ba0633971901e459afe1163485c5c62e2c64a68edb836201b95$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0614.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0614.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1501$t$, $t$Barnegat Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Letter of No Interest (in lieu of resale inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Barnegat Township Code Enforcement / Zoning Office (Construction Office)","Contact: John Durasky, Code Enforcement Officer and Zoning Officer · 609-698-0080 Ext. 159 · JohnD@barnegat.net","Apply: Allow 14 days to process the request","How to apply: Fill out the Request for Letter of No Interest in Lieu of Resale Inspection (block, lot, address, owner, requester) and submit it to Barnegat Township, 900 West Bay Avenue, Barnegat, NJ 08005 with the $100.00 fee paid at the time of the request. Checks are payable to Barnegat Township (the office-use section also lists cash). Allow 14 days.","Any open permits or violations on the property must be closed","The Township also checks for substantial damage, liens, and unpaid water, sewer and property taxes (office-use section of the form)","Also: Open permits and violations: Any and all open permits or violations must be closed before the Letter of No Interest is issued.","Also: Liens, water/sewer and property taxes: The Township's office-use section of the Letter of No Interest form checks liens, water/sewer and property taxes and whether the home has public water and sewer. Final water/sewer readings go through the Tax/Utility Collector (ext. 143 and 144)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Letter of No Interest processing fee (paid when the request is made)","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.barnegat.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Letter-of-No-Interest-12-2-24.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.barnegat.net/departments/building-department/home-re-sale-rentals/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.barnegat.net/departments/code-enforcement-zoning-office/","label":"Official source (barnegat.net)"},{"url":"https://www.barnegat.net/departments/building-department/home-re-sale-rentals/","label":"Official source (barnegat.net)"},{"url":"https://www.barnegat.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Letter-of-No-Interest-12-2-24.pdf","label":"Official source (barnegat.net)"},{"url":"https://www.barnegat.net/departments/building-department/","label":"Official source (barnegat.net)"},{"url":"https://www.barnegat.net/contact-us/","label":"Official source (barnegat.net)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Sale of House - Letter of No Interest now required for resales.$t$, $t$069fba3d8e9c6a40470f6ac8ccf91ab6f12e377b432d15ff8391da7f153207e4$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":1,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":17,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1501.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1501.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1501$t$, $t$Barnegat Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (NJ DCA, state)","Contact: Louis Kilmer, Bureau Chief, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement · (609) 633-6106 · BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov","Apply: Fee depends on how many business days before closing you apply (more than 10, 4 to 10, fewer than 4).","How to apply: Apply online through the NJ DCA Fire Safety portal (Start Your Smoke Certification Application). Pay by e-check or credit card before submitting; a valid email address is required. The certificate is emailed once the application is submitted, the fee is paid and any required inspections are done. Homes heated by electricity that need no CO alarm should also email BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 8/20/2025: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"State smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm and secondary power source label certificate, applied more than 10 business days before closing","amount":"$45"},{"label":"State smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm and secondary power source label certificate, applied 4 to 10 business days before closing","amount":"$90"},{"label":"State smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm and secondary power source label certificate, closing fewer than 4 business days away","amount":"$161"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/$t$, $t$https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.barnegat.net/forms/","label":"Official source (barnegat.net)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/divisions/dfs/codes/regulations/adopted_amendment_5_10_2.9.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$State Fire Instructions Smoke detector and Carbon Monoxide certification to be sent to State$t$, $t$edd136ee951908887a5a638a0bb1409559efd7d50c368143a2890cc425058e8a$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":1,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":17,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1501.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1501.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1503$t$, $t$Bay Head Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Real Estate Transfer Certificate (transfer certificate of occupancy; Application for Realty Transfer Permit)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Bay Head Code Enforcement Officer (Code Enforcement / Construction Office)","Contact: Darren Erbe, Technical Assistant / Code Enforcement · 732-892-0638 · derbe@bayheadnj.us","How to apply: The Borough's Code Enforcement page links 'Real Estate Transfer Certificate Application' to the Borough's SDL online portal (a free citizen account is needed). The older paper Application for Realty Transfer Permit asks for owner, purchaser, block and lot, closing attorney or agent and proposed closing date, and must include a current survey and the fire (smoke/CO) inspection certificate. Contact the office for an inspection appointment: 732-892-0638, 83 Bridge Ave, Bay Head.","Current smoke alarm and carbon monoxide alarm requirements (the fire inspection certificate must be provided with the application)","Applicable zoning and property maintenance rules and the property's development approvals","A current survey must be provided with the application","Also: Current survey: The Borough's realty transfer application must include a current survey.","Also: Fire inspection certificate: The Ocean County Fire Marshal smoke/CO certificate must be provided with the Borough transfer application."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Realty transfer inspection, per unit (2022 Borough form)","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection, per unit, if required (2022 Borough form)","amount":"$15.00"}]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.bayheadnj.org/code-enforcement$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.ecode360.com/35236631","label":"Official source (ecode360.com)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240517233737/https://www.bayheadnj.org/code-enforcement","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240518000009/https://www.bayheadnj.org/construction-and-building","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220525201637/https://www.bayheadnj.org/bhnj/Departments/Municipal%20Clerk/Forms%20%26%20Documents/Real%20Estate%20Transfer%20Application.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$transfer certificate of occupancy, issued by the Code Enforcement Officer of the Borough of Bay Head$t$, $t$581e1833d0169e7a25d8ab459e046c798137ebe46c615df6b35c148d54d9e25a$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":10,"fee_ok":10,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":19,"q_ok":16,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1503.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1503.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1503$t$, $t$Bay Head Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire code enforcing agency), Residential Resale and Rental Home Inspections","Contact: Bree Dominguez; Lynda Saverino, Residential Smoke CO Inspections staff (Chief Fire Marshal: Dennis M. Allen, dallen@co.ocean.nj.us) · (732) 929-2088 · OCFMSmokeDetect@co.ocean.nj.us","Apply: Apply more than 10 business days before closing for the lowest fee; the office calls to schedule the inspection after the application is submitted. The certificate is valid 12 months from the inspection.","How to apply: Fill out the online application (Ocean County SeamlessDocs form). The office then calls to schedule an inspection. Do not mail payment: pay at the inspection by paper check payable to Ocean County Fire Marshal (OCFM), credit card or e-check; no cash.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 8/5/2026: Dennis Allen · (732) 370-7360 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","Smoke alarms on every living level including the basement, and within 10 feet of bedrooms on levels with bedrooms","All smoke alarms, including hardwired, must be under 10 years old","Battery-only smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed battery units (since January 1, 2019); homes built before 1978 need at least one on each level","Homes built 1978 to 1983 need hardwired alarms on each level; 1984 to 1990 interconnected hardwired alarms with battery backup on each level; 1991 and later also in every bedroom","Hardwired alarms that need replacing must be replaced with hardwired alarms, not battery alarms","Carbon monoxide alarm near the sleeping areas if the home has a fuel-burning appliance or an attached garage; battery and plug-in CO alarms should be under 5 years old","Homes with a generator, solar panels or battery storage need a printed caution label (for example CAUTION: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER) within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and the electric meter","A monitored low-voltage fire alarm system needs an NFPA 72 test report sent to the Fire Marshal before closing","Portable fire extinguishers are no longer required (as of February 3, 2025)","Do not mount alarms in unfinished attics, garages, stairwells, the top of basement stairs or kitchens","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm and secondary power source label certificate, application received more than 10 business days before the change of occupancy","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Certificate, application received 4 to 10 business days before the change of occupancy","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Certificate, application received 3 business days or less before the change of occupancy","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Missed appointment or no entry to the home","amount":"$30.00"},{"label":"Reinspection (the first reinspection after a failed inspection may be free)","amount":"$30"},{"label":"Returned check processing fee","amount":"$15.00"},{"label":"Credit card convenience fee","amount":"$6.95"},{"label":"E-check convenience fee","amount":"$1.99"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://oceancounty.seamlessdocs.com/f/AppSDCO2FEComp$t$, $t$https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.co.ocean.nj.us//WebContentFiles//0299689d-3e63-4678-ad90-3b7c04b233c3.pdf","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmStaff.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Bay Head Resales and Rentals of 1-2 family buildings$t$, $t$a04323423008a6c8f8003cfe10a1ecaef6cee1d49ebf737724478ba49238ffa0$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":10,"fee_ok":10,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":19,"q_ok":16,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1503.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1503.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1504$t$, $t$Beach Haven Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate of Occupancy (resale inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Beach Haven Zoning Department (Construction and Zoning)","Contact: Vivienne “Veev” Washburn, Assistant Zoning Officer · 609-492-0111 x224 · vwashburn@beachhaven-nj.gov","Apply: Allow 2 weeks to schedule the inspection; resale inspections are done Tuesday and Thursday afternoons","How to apply: Bring the completed Resale Certificate of Occupancy form, the other listed paperwork (current plot plan and elevation certificate, filed deed restriction, condominium certification if a condo), a check made out to the Borough of Beach Haven and property access information to the Construction and Zoning office, 300 Engleside Avenue (the form also lists cash). The deed restriction must be filed with the Ocean County Clerk's Office in Toms River.","Visual inspection only, not a structural inspection","General condition of the lot, exterior and interior","Porch, deck and stair condition","Smoke alarms and carbon monoxide alarm(s)","Acceptable electrical and plumbing systems","Proper venting of heating equipment","Relief valves on water heaters and boilers piped down to within 6 inches of the floor (no plastic or galvanized pipe); water heater cabinets open for the inspection","Proper fire separation between an attached garage and living areas","Bedroom windows open easily for escape","House numbers on the building (3 inch numbers for homes)","Door locks on exit doors work and are not double-keyed","Portable fire extinguisher (2A:10B:C, no more than 10 lbs) mounted within 10 feet of the kitchen and no more than 5 feet above the floor (still listed on the Borough's 2024 sheet)","Current plot plan survey and flood elevation certificate with raised seals in the buyer's name","No open permits: all open permits must be finaled before the resale inspection","Property must be unoccupied, alarm systems disabled and dogs removed or crated at the inspection","Also: Deed restriction: A Declaration of Deed Restriction (FEMA flood regulations) must be filed with the Ocean County Clerk's Office in Toms River (or fees paid, per the form) for the resale certificate.","Also: Plot plan survey and flood elevation certificate: Current plot plan survey and flood elevation certificate with raised seals in the buyer's name.","Also: Open permits: All open permits must be finaled before the resale inspection.","Also: Condominium certification: Condo units use the Borough's Condominium Certification form listed with the resale paperwork.","Also: Emergency access placard: Resident Emergency Access Placards (non-condo owners) must be visible at the inspection and left in the property for the new owner."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale Certificate of Occupancy, each residential unit","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Resale Certificate of Occupancy, reinspection","amount":"$20.00"},{"label":"Resale Certificate of Occupancy, duplex (form)","amount":"$150.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://beachhaven-nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Resale-Form-2023.pdf$t$, $t$https://beachhaven-nj.gov/departments/construction-zoning/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://beachhaven-nj.gov/departments/construction-zoning/","label":"Official source (beachhaven-nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://beachhaven-nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Resale-Form-2023.pdf","label":"Official source (beachhaven-nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://beachhaven-nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/CURRENT-Resale-Inspection-Requirements.pdf","label":"Official source (beachhaven-nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Resale inspections will be done on Tuesday & Thursday afternoons. The property must be unoccupied, alarm systems must be disabled, and dogs must be removed or crated. Please allow 2 weeks to schedule inspection.$t$, $t$9e275008ad1ecc37a6845e5d02f39eabd16fa62be2d9ac8c105243fcbef5e751$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":11,"fee_ok":10,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":1,"quotes":24,"q_ok":22,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1504.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1504.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1504$t$, $t$Beach Haven Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire code enforcing agency), Residential Resale and Rental Home Inspections","Contact: Bree Dominguez; Lynda Saverino, Residential Smoke CO Inspections staff (Chief Fire Marshal: Dennis M. Allen, dallen@co.ocean.nj.us) · (732) 929-2088 · OCFMSmokeDetect@co.ocean.nj.us","Apply: Apply more than 10 business days before closing for the lowest fee; the office calls to schedule the inspection after the application is submitted. The certificate is valid 12 months from the inspection.","How to apply: Fill out the online application (Ocean County SeamlessDocs form). The office then calls to schedule an inspection. Do not mail payment: pay at the inspection by paper check payable to Ocean County Fire Marshal (OCFM), credit card or e-check; no cash.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 7/14/2026: Dennis Allen · (732) 370-7360 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","Smoke alarms on every living level including the basement, and within 10 feet of bedrooms on levels with bedrooms","All smoke alarms, including hardwired, must be under 10 years old","Battery-only smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed battery units (since January 1, 2019); homes built before 1978 need at least one on each level","Homes built 1978 to 1983 need hardwired alarms on each level; 1984 to 1990 interconnected hardwired alarms with battery backup on each level; 1991 and later also in every bedroom","Hardwired alarms that need replacing must be replaced with hardwired alarms, not battery alarms","Carbon monoxide alarm near the sleeping areas if the home has a fuel-burning appliance or an attached garage; battery and plug-in CO alarms should be under 5 years old","Homes with a generator, solar panels or battery storage need a printed caution label (for example CAUTION: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER) within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and the electric meter","A monitored low-voltage fire alarm system needs an NFPA 72 test report sent to the Fire Marshal before closing","Portable fire extinguishers are no longer required (as of February 3, 2025)","Do not mount alarms in unfinished attics, garages, stairwells, the top of basement stairs or kitchens","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm and secondary power source label certificate, application received more than 10 business days before the change of occupancy","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Certificate, application received 4 to 10 business days before the change of occupancy","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Certificate, application received 3 business days or less before the change of occupancy","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Missed appointment or no entry to the home","amount":"$30.00"},{"label":"Reinspection (the first reinspection after a failed inspection may be free)","amount":"$30"},{"label":"Returned check processing fee","amount":"$15.00"},{"label":"Credit card convenience fee","amount":"$6.95"},{"label":"E-check convenience fee","amount":"$1.99"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://oceancounty.seamlessdocs.com/f/AppSDCO2FEComp$t$, $t$https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://beachhaven-nj.gov/departments/construction-zoning/","label":"Official source (beachhaven-nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://beachhaven-nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/UPDATED-Letter-about-Rental-Requirements.pdf","label":"Official source (beachhaven-nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.co.ocean.nj.us//WebContentFiles//0299689d-3e63-4678-ad90-3b7c04b233c3.pdf","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmStaff.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Beach Haven Resales and Rentals of 1-2 family buildings$t$, $t$d682f87218939fecbf8af20d6ec604189ef942c6496dfe956e1e3ddb5c22601c$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":11,"fee_ok":10,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":1,"quotes":24,"q_ok":22,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1504.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1504.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1505$t$, $t$Beachwood Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Continued Occupancy (Resale Certificate of Occupancy)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Beachwood Borough Division of Code Enforcement/Housing (Construction, Land Use and Zoning office)","Contact: Meredith Triolo, Land Use / Code Enforcement/Zoning Secretary · 732 286 6000 ext. 220 · mtriolo@beachwoodusa.com","Apply: Submit the resale application about 60 days before closing","How to apply: Complete the Resale Application Packet (the whole application must be complete) and attach the heating, well and chimney paperwork that applies. Submit it by email to Meredith Triolo (mtriolo@beachwoodusa.com), in person at the Municipal Office, or by mail to Borough of Beachwood, Attn: Meredith Triolo, 1600 Pinewald Road, Beachwood, NJ 08722. After review a payment link is emailed; in-person payment is exact cash or check payable to Borough of Beachwood. Fees are non-refundable. Housing and Fire Prevention Bureau inspections are then scheduled for a Tuesday or Wednesday, 9:00 AM to 12:00 PM. If the home will not pass, a Transfer of Title application (fire inspection only, plus a notarized buyer letter that no one will occupy the home until a full resale inspection is passed) lets the sale proceed.","Receipt from a licensed HVAC professional showing the heating system works (not needed for electric heat)","Well water: Ocean County Health Department water analysis certificate","Wood-burning fireplace: receipt from a licensed professional showing the chimney is in working order","Electrical service panel has covers and working breakers; all lights, outlets and switches work with cover plates","GFCI outlets within 6 feet of any water source and in basements, garages and outside","Driveway and walkways free of trip hazards; lawn, hedges and trees trimmed and debris removed","Roof, siding, gutters and downspouts in good repair; a gutter over steps","Screens in windows and entry doors; windows unbroken, working and stay up when opened","3 inch house numbers visible on the home or both sides of the mailbox","Handrails on all stairs and guardrails on open sides","Pool properly safeguarded with bonded metal parts and self-closing, self-latching gates","Garage door opener with no extension cords or adapters; doors working and undamaged","Floors, walls and ceilings in good condition; stove burners and oven work","Hot and cold running water with no leaks and drains that drain freely; basement lit, ventilated and not overly damp","Owner or an authorized adult representative must be present for the inspection","Also: Heating system receipt: Receipt from a licensed HVAC professional that the heating system works (not needed for electric heat) must be submitted before the inspection is scheduled.","Also: Well water test: If the home has a well, an Ocean County Health Department water analysis certificate is required.","Also: Chimney certificate: Wood-burning fireplaces need a receipt from a licensed professional that the chimney works.","Also: Transfer of Title option: For homes that will not pass the resale inspection: fire inspection only ($30.00) plus a notarized buyer letter that the home will not be occupied until a full resale inspection is passed."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of Continued Occupancy (housing) inspection","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Housing re-inspection (failed or missed inspection)","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Resale housing application fee (resale packet)","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Transfer of Title (property not expected to pass resale inspection): fire inspection only","amount":"$30.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.beachwoodusa.com/DocumentCenter/View/671$t$, $t$https://www.beachwoodusa.com/159/CONSTRUCTIONZONING$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.beachwoodusa.com/159/CONSTRUCTIONZONING","label":"Official source (beachwoodusa.com)"},{"url":"https://www.beachwoodusa.com/DocumentCenter/View/671","label":"Official source (beachwoodusa.com)"},{"url":"https://www.beachwoodusa.com/DocumentCenter/View/830","label":"Official source (beachwoodusa.com)"},{"url":"https://www.beachwoodusa.com/Directory.aspx","label":"Official source (beachwoodusa.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$All home sales require a Certificate of Continued Occupancy prior to transfer of ownership.$t$, $t$4deb3080a7d36c94315d9f4420424d606607a1c0f74a6e444750c71d0ae2e643$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":4,"quotes":19,"q_ok":9,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":10},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1505.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1505.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1505$t$, $t$Beachwood Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Beachwood Bureau of Fire Prevention (town fire bureau)","Contact: Richard Foster, Fire Official (state fire directory) · (732) 286-6000","Apply: Schedule in advance; the fire inspection is done with the housing inspection on a Tuesday or Wednesday, 9:00 AM to 12:00 PM. The certificate is valid for 6 months.","How to apply: The fire application is part of the Borough's Resale Application Packet (or the Transfer of Title application) submitted to the Construction/Zoning office; to schedule, contact the Bureau of Fire Prevention at (732) 286-6000 for application paperwork.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 7/6/2026: Richard Foster · (732) 286-6000","Smoke alarms on every level including the basement and outside each sleeping area","Homes built before 1977: 10-year sealed battery smoke alarms on each level, within 10 feet of all bedrooms","Homes built January 1, 1977 to February 21, 1983: hardwired alarms on sleeping levels and in the basement, 10-year sealed battery alarms on other levels","Homes built February 22, 1983 to April 30, 1993: interconnected hardwired alarms with battery backup on every level; May 1, 1993 and later also inside every bedroom","Hardwired alarms must not be replaced with battery alarms; renovation-era rules apply to renovated homes","Carbon monoxide alarms within 10 feet of all bedrooms if the home has fuel-burning appliances or an attached garage (UL-2034, battery, hardwired or plug-in)","Homes with a fire alarm system must provide a contractor's inspection report; the Borough does not test fire alarm systems","Homes with a generator, solar panels or battery storage need a printed CAUTION: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER label within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and electric meter","Portable fire extinguishers are no longer required (as of February 3, 2025), although the older application page in the packet still lists one","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke alarm and carbon monoxide alarm inspection","amount":"$30"},{"label":"Fire Prevention Bureau re-inspection (resale)","amount":"$30"},{"label":"Certificate of Smoke Alarm, Carbon Monoxide Alarm and Portable Fire Extinguisher Compliance, initial inspection (2025 sheet)","amount":"$30.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection (2025 sheet)","amount":"$30.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.beachwoodusa.com/DocumentCenter/View/671$t$, $t$https://www.beachwoodusa.com/159/CONSTRUCTIONZONING$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.beachwoodusa.com/DocumentCenter/View/830","label":"Official source (beachwoodusa.com)"},{"url":"https://www.beachwoodusa.com/DocumentCenter/View/671","label":"Official source (beachwoodusa.com)"},{"url":"https://www.beachwoodusa.com/159/CONSTRUCTIONZONING","label":"Official source (beachwoodusa.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$If you are selling, leasing, or changing the occupancy of any one- or two-family home or attached single-family dwelling in Beachwood, you must obtain a Certificate of Smoke Alarm, Carbon Monoxide Alarm, and Portable Fire Extinguisher Compliance (CSACMAPFEC).$t$, $t$d0152bb9e0b2c2ca31908fb2fa577187823dc3e3673921d9223d72e378e407b8$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":4,"quotes":19,"q_ok":9,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":10},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1505.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1505.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1506$t$, $t$Berkeley Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate of Occupancy & Smoke Certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Berkeley Township Code Enforcement Office (housing inspection), with the Bureau of Fire Prevention (smoke/CO)","Contact: Kenneth Anderson, Supervising Code Enforcement Officer · 732-244-7400, ext. 1506 · codeenforcement@berkeleytownship.org","How to apply: Fill out the Township of Berkeley Certificate of Occupancy & Smoke Certificate Resale application (with the attached smoke and carbon monoxide certification form) and pay before the housing inspection; checks payable to Berkeley Township. Applications can also be picked up at the Code Enforcement Office, 627 Pinewald-Keswick Rd, Bayville, Monday through Friday, 8:30 am to 4 pm. Someone must be at the property at the inspection time. A failed inspection needs a $50 reinspection fee before it is rescheduled.","Safe, approved water supply; hot and cold water to sinks and tubs; plumbing fixtures working","Heating equipment properly installed and working","Smoke alarms and carbon monoxide alarms within 10 feet of sleeping areas","Safe, unobstructed exits; entry door deadbolts must not need a key to get out","Floors, foundation, walls, ceilings, doors and windows clean, working and free of dampness; no rodents","Handrail on any stairs with 3 or more steps; safe railings on decks, porches and balconies","Window screens from May 1 to October 1","Kitchen and bathroom floors impervious to water; paint and wallpaper in good condition","Solid core door or sheathing between garage and house; no extension cords or adapters for garage door openers","Roof, walls, windows, gutters, fences, driveway, steps, sidewalks, sheds, garages and bulkheads in good repair","Yard free of litter and debris; lawns and hedges trimmed; trash in approved containers","Street numbers visible from the road; pool fencing to code from original installation","A termite report may be required","All open permits must be closed before the Certificate of Occupancy is issued","Owner or a representative must be on site to operate all utilities","Also: HOA approval letter: Resales in age-restricted communities need an original approval letter from the Homeowners Association.","Also: Well water certificate: Ocean County Health Department certificate if a well is the primary water source.","Also: Oil tank: Certificate of tight tank if there is an above or below ground oil tank.","Also: Flood elevation certificate: Current flood elevation certificate with raised seal for flood-zone homes, reviewed by Zoning for a separate $100.00 fee.","Also: Open permits: All open permits must be closed before the Certificate of Occupancy is issued."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale Certificate of Occupancy and smoke certificate (combined, since April 8, 2024)","amount":"$150"},{"label":"Reinspection","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Transfer of Title (non-habitable dwellings only)","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Flood Elevation Certificate review (flood zone only; separate check to the Zoning Department)","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.berkeleytownship.org/DocumentCenter/View/415/Resales-Application-PDF$t$, $t$https://www.berkeleytownship.org/188/Rental-Resale-Inspections$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.berkeleytownship.org/188/Rental-Resale-Inspections","label":"Official source (berkeleytownship.org)"},{"url":"https://www.berkeleytownship.org/184/Code-Enforcement","label":"Official source (berkeleytownship.org)"},{"url":"https://www.berkeleytownship.org/DocumentCenter/View/415/Resales-Application-PDF","label":"Official source (berkeleytownship.org)"},{"url":"https://www.berkeleytownship.org/DocumentCenter/View/412/Housing-Inspection-Requirements-PDF","label":"Official source (berkeleytownship.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Any time you rent or sell your home in Berkeley Township, you must apply for a Certificate of Occupancy. For rental property owners, this applies every time the tenant changes.$t$, $t$6fbc064216c9c90f5ad5401e444f6e5c3c2a8466856e0da3309ebff96b58b0c0$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":17,"q_ok":17,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1506.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1506.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1506$t$, $t$Berkeley Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Berkeley Township Bureau of Fire Prevention (town fire bureau)","Contact: Kenneth Anderson, Fire Official · 732-244-7400 Ext. 1236 · fireofficial@berkeleytownship.org","How to apply: The smoke detector / carbon monoxide certification form is page 2 of the Township's resale Certificate of Occupancy application; file both together with the Code Enforcement Office.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 6/4/2025: Kenneth Anderson · (732) 244-7400 · fireofficial@berkeleytownship.org","Smoke alarms on each level including the basement (not attic or crawl space) and outside each separate sleeping area, located per NFPA 72","Battery-only smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed battery units (since January 1, 2019); hardwired alarms from original construction must not be replaced with battery alarms","Carbon monoxide alarm within 10 feet of the bedrooms if the home has a fuel-burning appliance or attached garage (UL 2034; battery, hardwired or plug-in)","Inspected by a Township inspector as part of the combined resale Certificate of Occupancy","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Included in the combined Resale Certificate of Occupancy & Smoke Certificate fee (paid to Code Enforcement)","amount":"$150"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.berkeleytownship.org/DocumentCenter/View/415/Resales-Application-PDF$t$, $t$https://www.berkeleytownship.org/220/Fire-Prevention-Bureau$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.berkeleytownship.org/220/Fire-Prevention-Bureau","label":"Official source (berkeleytownship.org)"},{"url":"https://www.berkeleytownship.org/DocumentCenter/View/415/Resales-Application-PDF","label":"Official source (berkeleytownship.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.berkeleytownship.org/184/Code-Enforcement","label":"Official source (berkeleytownship.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The Berkeley Township Fire Prevention Bureau is the local enforcement agency of the New Jersey Uniform Fire Code.$t$, $t$467b4ba531ab3667ad35530cb619a70e760ac6e672361fa887c8c46f4fc9e072$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":17,"q_ok":17,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1506.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1506.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1507$t$, $t$Brick Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$official_process_found$t$, $t$Resale / Continued Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Not required for sales, per Brick Township. Confirm with the office if the buyer's lender or title company asks.","Contact: 732-262-1033 · codeenforcement@twp.brick.nj.us","How to apply: No Township resale Certificate of Occupancy or resale inspection is required for a sale. The seller still needs the smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm and secondary power source certificate from the Brick Township Bureau of Fire Safety (732-458-4100)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.bricknj.gov/how_do_i/faq.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.bricknj.gov/how_do_i/faq.php","label":"Official source (bricknj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.bricknj.gov/departments/code_enforcement/index.php","label":"Official source (bricknj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The Township of Brick does not require a Certificate of Occupancy (CO) for resale of a property. You are however required to contact the Bureau of Fire Safety at (732) 458-4100 for the Certificate of Smoke Detector, Carbon Monoxide Detector, and Fire Extinguisher Compliance.$t$, $t$91fa621e2f5e1c33b468f5e71d1a272aa06e1313c54933f78ef880c45717dcc5$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":16,"q_ok":16,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1507.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1507.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1507$t$, $t$Brick Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Brick Township Bureau of Fire Safety (Brick Township Fire Districts 1, 2 and 3) (fire district)","Contact: Kevin C. Batzel, Bureau Chief, Brick Bureau of Fire Safety · 732-458-4100 · bureau@brickfire.org","Apply: Call to schedule 10 or more business days before the date you contact the Bureau for the lowest fee","How to apply: There is no form: call the Bureau at 732-458-4100 (Monday to Friday, 8 a.m. to 4 p.m.) or email bureau@brickfire.org to be put on the inspection schedule. Have ready the contact name and daytime phone, property address, block and lot, owner's name, year built, renovations or additions, number of stories, basement (finished or not) and whether there is a secondary power source. Credit card payment is available by calling the office (a processing fee may apply).","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 7/31/2026: Kevin C Batzel · (732) 458-4100 · kbatzel@brickfire.org","Smoke alarms on every level including the basement; on bedroom levels within 21 feet of the bedrooms (per the Bureau's September 2026 sheet)","All smoke alarms, including hardwired, must be under 10 years old","Homes built before 1978: at least one 10-year sealed battery smoke alarm on each level; 1978 to 1983 electric alarms on each level; 1984 to 1990 interconnected electric alarms with battery backup on each level; 1991 and later also in bedrooms","Hardwired alarms that are replaced must be replaced with hardwired alarms, not battery alarms","Carbon monoxide alarms on each level with sleeping areas, near the bedrooms; battery and plug-in CO alarms under 5 years old, combination smoke/CO alarms under 10 years old","Homes with a generator, solar panels or battery storage need a printed CAUTION: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER label (ANSI Z535.4) within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and the electric meter","A monitored low-voltage fire alarm system still needs the inspection plus an NFPA 72 test report sent to the Bureau before closing","Ceiling mount preferred; wall mounts 4 to 12 inches from the ceiling, 4 inches from corners and 3 feet from air registers; not in unfinished attics, stairwells, top of basement stairs or kitchens","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm and secondary power source certificate, scheduled inspection day (10 or more business days from the contact date)","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Certificate, non-scheduled appointment 5 to 9 business days from the contact date","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Certificate, non-scheduled appointment 1 to 4 business days from the contact date","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection, missed appointment or no entry","amount":"$30.00"}]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.brickfire.org/home-resale-detector-inspections$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.brickfire.org/home-resale-detector-inspections","label":"Official source (brickfire.org)"},{"url":"https://www.brickfire.org/_files/ugd/d315f6_0d7bfccc453e43509b257edd7503b4da.pdf","label":"Official source (brickfire.org)"},{"url":"https://www.brickfire.org/forms-applications","label":"Official source (brickfire.org)"},{"url":"https://www.brickfire.org/bureau","label":"Official source (brickfire.org)"},{"url":"https://www.brickfire.org/staff","label":"Official source (brickfire.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Ordinance fee change effective 8/12/2026.$t$, $t$927868641522674cbe97d6a2a8ff26fdefbb73c494be2ddf9fcc7215cc9e2eb3$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":16,"q_ok":16,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1507.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1507.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1508$t$, $t$Toms River Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$official_process_found$t$, $t$Resale / Continued Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Not required for sales, per Division of Code Enforcement (no longer issued for sales). Confirm with the office if the buyer's lender or title company asks.","Issued by: Division of Code Enforcement (no longer issued for sales)","Contact: Stan Ferriolo, Division Supervisor, Division of Code Enforcement · 732-341-1000, ext. 8532 · SFerriolo@tomsrivertownship.com","How to apply: Nothing to apply for. The Township stopped requiring the Municipal Certificate of Continued Use and Occupancy for home sales in January 2024. Sellers still need the smoke and carbon monoxide alarm certificate from the Toms River Bureau of Fire Prevention."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.tomsrivertownship.com/177/Property-MaintenanceRental-Application$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.tomsrivertownship.com/177/Property-MaintenanceRental-Application","label":"Official source (tomsrivertownship.com)"},{"url":"https://www.tomsrivertownship.com/DocumentCenter/View/10369","label":"Official source (tomsrivertownship.com)"},{"url":"https://www.tomsrivertownship.com/m/directory/department?did=16","label":"Official source (tomsrivertownship.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Resale Inspections The Township no longer requires a Municipal Certificate of Continued Use and Occupancy for the sale of a home. You are still required to obtain a Residential Smoke Inspection with the Bureau of Fire Prevention.$t$, $t$090cb65ec15b359a58658a47f48dff4eb71811a833279265c4665e1dd96c4c02$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":12,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1508.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1508.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1508$t$, $t$Toms River Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Toms River Bureau of Fire Prevention (fire code agency for Toms River Fire Districts 1 and 2) (fire district)","Contact: Matthew Janora, Chief Inspector / Fire Official · 732-240-5153 · TRFirePrevention@trfire.org","Apply: Submit at least 3 weeks before closing; certificate expires 6 months from issuance","How to apply: Apply online through the Township's SDL portal (create an account or log in, choose Fire/Smoke Detector Inspection, inspection reason Property Sold, enter the closing date, the address and the realtor's details), then pay the $75.00 by credit card. The Bureau then calls to schedule the inspection. The certificate can be emailed at the end of the inspection day. To cancel, call 732-240-5153.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 1/12/2026: Matthew Janora · (732) 240-5153 · mjanora@trfire.org","Someone 18 or older must be home for the inspection; inspections are scheduled between 9:00 a.m. and 12:00 p.m. and the inspector will not wait","Homes built before 1977: 10-year sealed battery smoke alarms on each level, including the basement, and within 10 feet of all bedrooms","Homes with hardwired (A/C powered) smoke alarms must keep them hardwired; they may not be swapped for battery alarms","Carbon monoxide alarms near all sleeping areas in homes with fuel-burning appliances or an attached garage (UL 2034 listed)","Homes with a generator, solar panels or battery storage need a printed (not handwritten) 'CAUTION: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER' label within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and of the electric meter","Portable fire extinguisher no longer required as of February 3, 2025 (per the Bureau's February 2025 requirements sheet)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Initial smoke and carbon monoxide alarm inspection","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"First re-inspection","amount":"$0.00"},{"label":"Each additional re-inspection after the first","amount":"$35"},{"label":"Appointment no-show (on top of the inspection fee)","amount":"$75"},{"label":"Duplicate copy of certificate","amount":"$30"},{"label":"Penalty for closing without the certificate","amount":"$500"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.sdlportal.com/towns/nj/ocean/tomsriver/requests/smokeAlarm$t$, $t$https://trfireprevention.com/residential-smoke-inspections/resale/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://trfireprevention.com/residential-smoke-inspections/resale/","label":"Official source (trfireprevention.com)"},{"url":"https://trfireprevention.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Residential-Resale-Requirements-Feb-2025.pdf","label":"Official source (trfireprevention.com)"},{"url":"https://trfireprevention.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/STEP_BY_STEP_INSTRUCIONS_ON_HOW_TO_APPLY_FOR_AN_INSPECTIONFOR_THE_RESALE_OF_A_HOME.pdf","label":"Official source (trfireprevention.com)"},{"url":"https://trfireprevention.com/about/employee-information/","label":"Official source (trfireprevention.com)"},{"url":"https://www.tomsrivertownship.com/442/Fire-Prevention","label":"Official source (tomsrivertownship.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://trfireprevention.com/residential-smoke-inspections/","label":"Official source (trfireprevention.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$If you are selling your home in Toms River, you are required to schedule an appointment with the Toms River Bureau of Fire Prevention for a resale inspection.$t$, $t$54589362967d541303091edef4ff6cde5a5f03e0328b6d679178d58124651a0d$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":12,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1508.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1508.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1509$t$, $t$Eagleswood Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate of Inspection (Certificate of Inspection, Existing Structure Rental/Resale)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Eagleswood Township Zoning/Code Enforcement Officer","Contact: 609-296-3040, ext. 18 · wackley@eagleswoodtwpnj.us","How to apply: Download the 2026 Inspection Application, fill in the Certificate of Inspection Application (seller, buyer and agent details, inspection type) and the Mechanical Certification page, and submit it with the fee to the Township of Eagleswood, 146 Division Street, West Creek. Cash, check or money order only, checks payable to Eagleswood Township. Then schedule the inspection with the Code Enforcement Officer, Monday and Thursday 3:30 pm to 7:30 pm, 609-296-3040 ext. 18.","No open construction permits: have the Stafford Township construction clerk check, and close any open permits before applying","Mechanical certification that the heating unit, hot water unit, plumbing and electrical system are safe and working (by the owner, a licensed contractor or a home inspector)","Ocean County Board of Health well certificate for homes on a well","House numbers permanently attached, 4 inches tall","Deadbolts may not need a key on the inside","10-year sealed battery smoke alarms (or hardwired alarms) on every floor, including the basement, and outside each sleeping area","Carbon monoxide alarms within 10 feet of every bedroom","Anti-tip device on the range","Water heater and boiler relief valves piped down to 6 inches from the floor","Metal dryer vent that ends outside","Hot water on the left, cold on the right; plumbing in good shape with no open sewer lines","Covers on all switches, outlets, junction boxes and panels, no gaps in the panel, and the electric service in good condition","No broken windows, missing siding, debris or uncut grass; chimneys and furnaces capped and vented; no holes in walls, floors or doors","Handrails and guardrails on open sides of decks and stairs 30 inches or more above grade; bulkhead maintained","Homes with a generator, solar or battery system need a 'Caution: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER' label within 18 inches of the main panel and the meter","Also: Open permits closed: Stafford Township's construction clerk (shared service for Eagleswood UCC permits) must confirm there are no open permits; any open permits must be inspected and closed before the resale application is filed.","Also: Mechanical certification: Signed certification that the heating unit, hot water unit, plumbing and electrical systems are safe and working, by the owner, a licensed contractor or a home inspector, delivered to the Zoning Official.","Also: Well certificate: Ocean County Board of Health well certificate required for Transfer of Title and Resale inspections (for homes on a private well)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale Certificate of Inspection (for occupancy)","amount":"$40"},{"label":"Resale Certificate of Inspection re-inspection","amount":"$15"},{"label":"Transfer of Title inspection (no occupancy)","amount":"$40"},{"label":"Transfer of Title re-inspection","amount":"$15"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://eagleswoodtwpnj.us/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Inspection-Application-2026.pdf$t$, $t$https://eagleswoodtwpnj.us/twp-business/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://eagleswoodtwpnj.us/twp-business/","label":"Official source (eagleswoodtwpnj.us)"},{"url":"https://eagleswoodtwpnj.us/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Inspection-Application-2026.pdf","label":"Official source (eagleswoodtwpnj.us)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$All Certificates of Occupancy for rental/resale must now be done through the Eagleswood Zoning Department @ 609-296-3040, ext. 18.$t$, $t$6fbca04b0b3fa5ea1e16417fe08eaf021a2eed73d3ba7a14ddf332afe91bdafe$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":11,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1509.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1509.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1509$t$, $t$Eagleswood Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Not confirmed. The NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety is the fire code agency, but the state does not list Eagleswood as a town where it issues smoke certificates; the Township's Resale Certificate of…","Contact: Louis Kilmer, Fire Official (NJ Division of Fire Safety, state-enforced towns) · 609-633-6132","How to apply: No separate smoke and CO certificate application or fee was found on the Township site. Ask the Township Zoning/Code Enforcement Officer (609-296-3040 ext. 18) whether the Resale Certificate of Inspection also serves as the state smoke and CO certificate, and ask the NJ DCA Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (609-633-6132) whether it issues the certificate for Eagleswood.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated n/a: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","Township resale checklist (2026): 10-year sealed battery smoke alarms (or hardwired) on every floor and outside each sleeping area, CO alarms within 10 feet of every bedroom, and a secondary power source label within 18 inches of the main panel and meter; fire extinguisher is a commercial requirement only","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://eagleswoodtwpnj.us/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Inspection-Application-2026.pdf","label":"Official source (eagleswoodtwpnj.us)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$S Eagleswood Township$t$, $t$73bc425b2efb3939d261f87c5ba9404ecdb6ddb263b7fbb13042fd0d785845ff$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":11,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1509.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1509.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1510$t$, $t$Harvey Cedars Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate of Occupancy (continuing Certificate of Occupancy)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Zoning Office (Zoning/Code Enforcement Officer)","Contact: Cecilia (Ceci) Morillo, Zoning/Code Enforcement Officer · 609-361-6000, option 8 · cmorillo@harveycedars.org","How to apply: Print the Resale CO Application and the Resale CO Checklist from the Zoning Office page, complete them (seller, buyer, agent, sale price, property type) and drop them off with the fee at Borough Hall, 7606 Long Beach Blvd, Harvey Cedars. Include the sealed survey and elevation certificate, the Ocean County Fire Marshal smoke/CO certificate and the recorded Declaration of Deed Restriction. If a deficiency is found, the Zoning Officer contacts the applicant or agent. If the property will be demolished and not occupied, a letter from the buyer and the application are all that is required.","Completed resale application and fee, with the buyer's contact information","Original sealed survey and elevation certificate dated within 1 year of the resale date","Current-year smoke and CO alarm certificate from the Ocean County Fire Marshal","Recorded Declaration of Deed Restriction (flood regulations covenant)","Work done without required permits will be cited; any open permits must be closed before the CO is issued","Water heater relief valve piped to within 6 inches of the floor","Enclosed spaces below the base flood elevation must comply","Proper fire separation between the garage and living area","Double-keyed deadbolts replaced with an inside thumb turn","Handrail on stairs with 4 or more risers; guards on walking surfaces 30 inches or more above grade","Public Works check of the curb box, meter pit and sewer clean-out","House numbers at least 4 inches tall, contrasting with the background","Driveway no wider than 18 feet at the pavement edge; trash corral and landscaping at least 5 feet from the pavement","Right-of-way cleared of obstructions except mailboxes; easements and corner sight triangles kept clear","Fences on the Boulevard set back 2 feet with a flat walkable surface","Also: Survey and elevation certificate: Original sealed survey and elevation certificate dated within 1 year of the resale date.","Also: Declaration of Deed Restriction: A recorded copy of the flood-regulation deed restriction must accompany the CO application.","Also: Water/sewer inspection by Public Works: Public Works checks the curb box, meter pit and sewer clean-out as part of the resale CO.","Also: Taxes, water and sewer paid: No certificate of occupancy is issued until taxes, assessments, and water and sewer charges are paid; a temporary 30 day CO may be issued on a transfer."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale Certificate of Occupancy, per living unit","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Reinspection (at the Zoning Officer's discretion)","amount":"$25"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.harveycedars.org/documents/Resale%20CO%20Application%202025.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.harveycedars.org/cn/webpage.cfm?tpid=16490$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.harveycedars.org/documents/Chapter%2013%20Zoning%20-%20Borough%20of%20Harvey%20Cedars%2C%20NJ%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (harveycedars.org)"},{"url":"https://www.harveycedars.org/cn/webpage.cfm?tpid=16490","label":"Official source (harveycedars.org)"},{"url":"https://www.harveycedars.org/documents/Resale%20CO%20Application%202025.pdf","label":"Official source (harveycedars.org)"},{"url":"https://www.harveycedars.org/documents/Zoning/Zoning%20Application/Resale%20Requirement%20List%20%202022.pdf","label":"Official source (harveycedars.org)"},{"url":"https://www.harveycedars.org/documents/ordinances/hc%20code%20book%202021%20january.pdf","label":"Official source (harveycedars.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Transfer of Ownership. A new certificate of occupancy shall be obtained whenever there occurs a sale, conveyance, transfer of ownership or change in occupancy of a building or structure to assure compliance with the provisions of this chapter and all other applicable laws, codes, ordinances and regulations.$t$, $t$1674284bdf5b6e791c13fa78c84aa8bca7a844651ff9735d081a712f5988bd72$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":9,"fee_ok":9,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":17,"q_ok":17,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1510.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1510.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1510$t$, $t$Harvey Cedars Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire code enforcing agency), Residential Resale and Rental Home Inspections","Contact: Bree Dominguez, Residential Smoke CO Inspections staff, Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office · 732-929-2088 · OCFMSmokeDetect@co.ocean.nj.us","Apply: Apply more than 10 business days before the change of occupancy for the lowest fee; certificate valid 12 months from the inspection date","How to apply: Fill out the Ocean County Fire Marshal's online application (SeamlessDocs). The office then calls to schedule the inspection. Do not mail payment: pay at the inspection by paper check payable to Ocean County Fire Marshal (OCFM), credit card or e-check. No cash. Inspections are done from the Manahawkin office, 179 South Main St.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 5/29/2025: Dennis Allen · (732) 370-7360 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","Smoke alarms, including hardwired ones, must be under 10 years old (Ocean County Fire Marshal, February 2025)","Battery-only and plug-in CO alarms should be under 5 years old; combination smoke/CO alarms under 10 years old","Homes built before 1978: at least one 10-year sealed battery smoke alarm on each level; newer homes need hardwired alarms by build year, and hardwired alarms must stay hardwired","Wall-mounted alarms 4 to 12 inches from the ceiling, 4 inches from corners and 3 feet from air registers","Homes with a generator, solar or battery system need a printed (not handwritten) 'CAUTION: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER' label within 18 inches of the main panel and the meter","A monitored low-voltage fire alarm system needs a copy of its NFPA 72 test report sent to the office before closing","Borough resale checklist requires a fire certificate for the current year","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke and CO alarm certificate, applied for more than 10 business days before the change of occupancy","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke and CO alarm certificate, applied for 4 to 10 business days before the change of occupancy","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Smoke and CO alarm certificate, applied for 3 business days or less before the change of occupancy","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Missed appointment or no entry","amount":"$30.00"},{"label":"Each re-inspection after the first free re-inspection","amount":"$30"},{"label":"Returned check processing fee","amount":"$15.00"},{"label":"Card payment fee / e-check fee","amount":"$6.95 / $1.99"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://oceancounty.seamlessdocs.com/f/AppSDCO2FEComp$t$, $t$https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmStaff.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.co.ocean.nj.us//WebContentFiles//0299689d-3e63-4678-ad90-3b7c04b233c3.pdf","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.harveycedars.org/documents/Zoning/Zoning%20Application/Resale%20Requirement%20List%20%202022.pdf","label":"Official source (harveycedars.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Harvey Cedars Resales and Rentals of 1-2 family buildings$t$, $t$37d95f68f530ca013446043b615fd6128598190d74d465388a299959dda75ea2$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":9,"fee_ok":9,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":17,"q_ok":17,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1510.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1510.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1511$t$, $t$Island Heights Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate (Existing Structure Inspection); Transfer Certificate if the home cannot pass$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough Office of Code Enforcement","Contact: Sean Asay, Code Enforcement Officer · 732-270-6415 · codeenforcement@islandheightsborough.gov","How to apply: Fill out the Existing Structure Inspection Application (check Resale Certificate, or Transfer Certificate if the home will not pass) and pay the $100 fee by cash or check to the Borough Office of Code Enforcement, PO Box 797, Island Heights (office at 1 East End Avenue). Close all permits, resolve violations and hand in the chimney and heating certifications before the inspection is scheduled. For a Transfer Certificate, include a letter from the buyer acknowledging the home may not be occupied until the new owner gets a Resale Certificate or a UCC Certificate of Occupancy.","Valid for: Resale Certificate: 1 year from issuance. Transfer Certificate: 180 days.","All construction (UCC) permits closed and all property maintenance violations resolved before the inspection is scheduled","Chimney certification from a licensed chimney sweep or HVAC contractor","Heating system certification from a licensed HVAC contractor or plumber","Yard kept up, with no overgrown grass or weeds and no debris or trash","Reflective house numbers at least 2 inches tall on the front of the house","Secure handrails on every staircase of 4 or more steps","Plumbing working with water flowing from each faucet; electricity, gas and water on","Outlets working, with GFI outlets in bathrooms, kitchen and outdoors","Anti-tip device on range stoves","Smoke detectors in all bedrooms and in the hall outside the bedrooms, plus at least one smoke detector and one CO detector on each level","2A-10BC fire extinguisher mounted within 10 feet of the kitchen (Borough ordinance and August 2024 checklist)","Interior and exterior doors open and close properly, exterior doors lock, windows lock and stay open when raised","Also: Open permits and violations: All UCC permits must be closed and all property maintenance violations resolved before the resale inspection is scheduled.","Also: Chimney and heating certifications: Chimney certification (licensed chimney sweep or HVAC contractor) and heating system certification (licensed HVAC contractor or plumber) are due before the inspection."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale Certificate inspection","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection after a failed inspection (request within 30 days)","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Transfer Certificate application (home that cannot pass the resale inspection)","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://islandheightsborough.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Form-Structure-Certificate-Application-and-Checklist-08-2024.pdf$t$, $t$https://islandheightsborough.gov/code/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://islandheightsborough.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Newsletter-240716.pdf","label":"Official source (islandheightsborough.gov)"},{"url":"https://islandheightsborough.gov/forms/","label":"Official source (islandheightsborough.gov)"},{"url":"https://islandheightsborough.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Form-Structure-Certificate-Application-and-Checklist-08-2024.pdf","label":"Official source (islandheightsborough.gov)"},{"url":"https://islandheightsborough.gov/code/","label":"Official source (islandheightsborough.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$12-1.4 Resale Certificate A. A Resale Certificate issued by the Borough Office of Code Enforcement shall be required: 1. Prior to the sale or transfer of any improved commercial or residential property in the Borough$t$, $t$eff9b62e34a4ddad14c24c1bc93e60957805fca8376fd8fc4696ad41b86b3f07$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1511.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1511.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1511$t$, $t$Island Heights Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Island Heights Borough Fire Official (municipal fire code enforcing agency) (town fire bureau)","Contact: William Richert, Fire Official (also Fire Sub-Code Official) · 732-270-6415","How to apply: The Borough does not post a smoke and CO certificate application or fee. The Fire Official's office hours are by appointment; call the Borough office at 732-270-6415 or write to the Fire Official at PO Box 797, Island Heights, NJ 08732. The Borough's Resale Certificate inspection also checks smoke and CO detectors; ask whether it serves as the state certificate.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 6/25/2026: William Richert · (732) 270-0388 · captainbill4022@gmail.com","Borough resale inspection (Ordinance 2024-06, August 2024 checklist) still lists a 2A-10BC fire extinguisher within 10 feet of the kitchen, although state law dropped the extinguisher on February 3, 2025","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://islandheightsborough.gov/fire-official/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://islandheightsborough.gov/fire-official/","label":"Official source (islandheightsborough.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://islandheightsborough.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Newsletter-240716.pdf","label":"Official source (islandheightsborough.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Island Heights Fire Official William Richert Telephone - 732-270-6415, Fax - 732-270-8586 OFFICE HOURS: By Appointment$t$, $t$185117710537a6ddbfe402d3113ba52a91dfafe4e57271abf2479a337bfd2909$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1511.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1511.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1513$t$, $t$Lacey Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$official_process_found$t$, $t$Resale / Continued Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Not required for sales, per Construction Office, Department of Community Development. Confirm with the office if the buyer's lender or title company asks.","Issued by: Construction Office, Department of Community Development","Contact: Christopher Reid, Director, Community Development (department that runs the Construction Office) · 609-693-1100, ext. 2253 · lacey.commdev@laceytownship.org","Apply: Allow 14 business days for the Letter of No Interest","How to apply: Download the Request for Letter of No Interest, fill in the block, lot, address, requester and closing date, and submit it with the $50 fee (cash, or check payable to the Township of Lacey) to the Construction Office, 124 South Main Street, Forked River (mail to 818 Lacey Road). Faxed requests are not accepted. The letter can be mailed, picked up or emailed. Allow 14 business days.","No open construction permits (the Letter of No Interest confirms this for the buyer)","Also: Letter of No Interest (no open permits): Required instead of a resale CO; $50, allow 14 business days; confirms there are no open permits on the house."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Letter of No Interest (required instead of a resale certificate of occupancy)","amount":"$50"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.laceytownship.org/DocumentCenter/View/243$t$, $t$https://www.laceytownship.org/1207/Building-Department$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.laceytownship.org/1207/Building-Department","label":"Official source (laceytownship.org)"},{"url":"https://www.laceytownship.org/DocumentCenter/View/243","label":"Official source (laceytownship.org)"},{"url":"https://www.laceytownship.org/m/directory/department?did=11","label":"Official source (laceytownship.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Lacey Township does not require a Certificate of Occupancy for resale. Lacey Township does require a Letter of No Interest .$t$, $t$e09a7a6ada7db1a09f10484322615c9d796bd8f3a04937a04ab3eefaa9efdc35$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":1,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":12,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1513.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1513.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1513$t$, $t$Lacey Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (NJ DCA, state)","Contact: Louis Kilmer, Fire Official (NJ Division of Fire Safety, Deputy Division Director) · 609-633-6132 · BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov","Apply: More than 10 business days before closing for the lowest fee; a new application is needed if the change of occupant does not happen within 6 months","How to apply: Apply online on the NJ DCA Fire Safety portal (the Township's Building Department page links to it). The applicant checks off each smoke alarm, CO alarm and power source label requirement and pays by e-check or credit card before submitting. The certificate is emailed once the fee is paid and any required inspection is done. Homes heated by electricity with no CO requirement should email BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 5/19/2025: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","CO alarms within about 10 feet of sleeping areas when the home has a fuel-burning appliance or attached garage (battery, hardwired or plug-in allowed)","State online form (CSACMASPSIL) covers smoke alarms, CO alarms and the secondary power source label; no fire extinguisher","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"More than 10 business days before closing","amount":"$45"},{"label":"4 to 10 business days before closing","amount":"$90"},{"label":"Less than 4 business days before closing","amount":"$161"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/$t$, $t$https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.laceytownship.org/1207/Building-Department","label":"Official source (laceytownship.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Single-Family Dwelling Resale When selling your home, a smoke detector certification is required through the State of New Jersey.$t$, $t$c830440f7445c0a82abc40e27627af77d2c138f538d2d73aac601512f0209ba1$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":1,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":12,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1513.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1513.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1514$t$, $t$Lakehurst Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Inspection Certificate for Resale or New Tenant (Residential Dwelling Reoccupancy Inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Lakehurst Borough Code Enforcement Officer (Construction Office, Borough Hall)","Contact: 732-657-4141","How to apply: Contact the Construction Office at Borough Hall, 5 Union Avenue, 732-657-4141 (8:30 am to 4:00 pm, Monday to Friday) to arrange the inspection. No application form is posted online.","Working, properly installed smoke detectors","Working, properly installed carbon monoxide alarms","Portable fire extinguisher (as listed on the Borough page)","Property maintenance review","House must match the tax assessor and building records","Also: Records check: The reoccupancy inspection confirms the house matches the tax assessor and building records."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Residential reoccupancy inspection, 1- or 2-family (covers two inspections)","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Third inspection, if needed","amount":"$25"}]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.lakehurst-nj.gov/department/construction.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.lakehurst-nj.gov/department/construction.php","label":"Official source (lakehurst-nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$RESIDENTIAL DWELLING REOCCUPANCY INSPECTIONS: Before a 1- or 2-family residential dwelling is sold, leased or a change of occupancy occurs, the dwelling must be inspected. Inspections are carried out by the Lakehurst Borough Code Enforcement Officer.$t$, $t$9c21288df0450a7015d9eb82a96bdc5de59e5497e4734be406c20cbe4b44c543$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1514.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1514.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1514$t$, $t$Lakehurst Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Lakehurst Borough (municipal fire code enforcing agency); smoke and CO compliance handled by the Borough Housing Office through the reoccupancy inspection (town fire bureau)","Contact: Dennis Allen, Fire Official · 732-657-4141 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","How to apply: The Borough checks smoke detectors, CO alarms and the extinguisher as part of its $100 Residential Dwelling Reoccupancy Inspection (see the town certificate above). Call Borough Hall at 732-657-4141 to schedule. No separate smoke/CO certificate fee is posted.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 6/23/2025: Dennis Allen · (732) 657-4141 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","Borough reoccupancy inspection checks smoke detectors, CO alarms and a portable fire extinguisher (the Borough page still lists the extinguisher after the February 2025 state change)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.lakehurst-nj.gov/department/construction.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.lakehurst-nj.gov/department/construction.php","label":"Official source (lakehurst-nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$M Lakehurst Borough$t$, $t$c4b55dd10135d8f2cac99081f429a2906ae17728fc4a60bfe9d91b62514df5ed$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1514.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1514.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1516$t$, $t$Lavallette Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Transfer Certificate of Occupancy (Application for Transfer of Title / Resale Inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Lavallette Building Department (Construction Code Official or Code Enforcement Officer)","Contact: Tom Brihn, Construction Official and Zoning Officer · 732-793-5105","How to apply: Download the Application for Transfer of Title from the Borough forms page, fill in owner, agent, buyer, sale price and number of occupants, sign the consent to inspection and the heating and fireplace certifications, and submit it with a check payable to the Borough of Lavallette. The fee is due when the form is submitted. Building Department, Municipal Building second floor, 1306 Grand Central Avenue, Lavallette, NJ 08735; 732-793-5105; open 8 AM to 3 PM weekdays.","General condition of the lot and the outside of the house","Porches, decks and stairs: handrails on stairs with 4 or more risers; guardrails on open sides more than 30 inches above grade, with openings under 4 inches and no horizontal rails","Smoke alarms within 10 feet of every bedroom and at least one on each level, including basements (battery alarms allowed)","Acceptable electrical and plumbing systems","Heating equipment properly vented","Relief valves on water heaters and boilers, piped downward to within 6 inches of the floor, full size, no plastic pipe","Approved separation between an attached garage and the living area, with solid wood or metal doors","General condition of the inside of the house","House numbers on the house, visible from the street, 3 inches high","Seller or agent signs a statement that the water heater and heating system are safe, and that the fireplace damper and flue meet code","Chimney caps on all fireplaces","Visual inspection only; not a full home inspection","Also: Seller or agent certification of heating, hot water and fireplace: The owner or agent signs that the hot water and heating system is safe and that the fireplace damper and flue meet code.","Also: Tax Office confirmation: The form has a Tax Collector sign-off on the number of structures and use."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Inspection fee, first unit (paid when the form is submitted)","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Each additional unit","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.lavallette.org/forms/zoning/ZoningTitleTransfer.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.lavallette.org/building.html$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://ecode360.com/6676186","label":"Official source (ecode360.com)"},{"url":"https://www.lavallette.org/forms/zoning/ZoningTitleTransfer.pdf","label":"Official source (lavallette.org)"},{"url":"https://www.lavallette.org/forms.html","label":"Official source (lavallette.org)"},{"url":"https://www.lavallette.org/building.html","label":"Official source (lavallette.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$No residential property shall be sold and title transferred until the owner of the property to be sold obtains a transfer certificate of occupancy signed by the Construction Code Official or Code Enforcement Officer of the Borough of Lavallette demonstrating that the property complies as to current smoke and carbon monoxide detector requirements and all applicable zoning and property maintenance laws of this Borough$t$, $t$b288a157367df50bf053aa9a37b6d2d5fcd74fab616545c5d7d8d1648440be31$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":15,"q_ok":13,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1516.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1516.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1516$t$, $t$Lavallette Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Lavallette Building Department (smoke and CO compliance checked in the Borough transfer certificate of occupancy) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Tom Brihn, Construction Official · 732-793-5105","How to apply: Apply for the Transfer of Title inspection with the Building Department (see the town certificate). Its checklist covers smoke alarms, and the Borough ordinance says the transfer certificate shows compliance with smoke and CO alarm requirements.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 7/22/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","Smoke alarms within 10 feet of every bedroom and at least one on each level, including basements (checked in the Borough transfer inspection)","Carbon monoxide alarm compliance is part of the transfer certificate under the Borough ordinance","The Borough form still prints the old N.J.A.C. 5:70-4.19 portable fire extinguisher rule (2.5 to 10 lb ABC, within 10 feet of the kitchen, mounted with the top no more than 5 feet up); the form is undated, and P.L.2025, c.19 has since removed the extinguisher from the state requirement","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Transfer of Title inspection (same single inspection as the town certificate; not charged twice)","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.lavallette.org/forms/zoning/ZoningTitleTransfer.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.lavallette.org/building.html$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://ecode360.com/6676186","label":"Official source (ecode360.com)"},{"url":"https://www.lavallette.org/forms/zoning/ZoningTitleTransfer.pdf","label":"Official source (lavallette.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.lavallette.org/building.html","label":"Official source (lavallette.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$demonstrating that the property complies as to current smoke and carbon monoxide detector requirements$t$, $t$d9425a2a5e4bfc735c081cc5f1a027e6beffc8440e0e25daf79ddc2a756094fa$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":15,"q_ok":13,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1516.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1516.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1517$t$, $t$Little Egg Harbor Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Existing Structure Certificate of Occupancy (resale)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Little Egg Harbor Township Construction Office (Construction Code Official)","Contact: Ronald Piszar, Construction Official / Fire Sub-Code Official · (609) 296-7241 ext. 618 · rpiszar@leht.com","How to apply: Download the Existing Structure Certificate of Occupancy application (residential), check 'Resale', and submit the complete packet with the fee, the signed Mechanical Certification, and any required prior approvals (open permits closed, LLC formation letter, estate Surrogate letter or POA, well water analysis if on a well). Incomplete applications are not accepted. Once accepted, the office emails an inspection date (check spam folders). The form asks for a lock box code or that someone be home. If the buyer will obtain the certificate, the seller and buyer sign the notarized acknowledgements on page 5. Construction Office, 665 Radio Road, Little Egg Harbor, NJ 08087; phone 609-294-9071, fax 609-294-9065.","House numbers permanently attached: 3 inches for homes","Deadbolts may not need a key on the inside","Smoke alarms on each floor including the basement and within 10 feet of all bedrooms; interconnected systems must stay interconnected","Carbon monoxide alarms outside of and within 10 feet of all bedrooms","Anti-tip device on all ranges","Relief valves on water heaters and boilers piped down to 2 to 6 inches from the floor, no reducers, no threads at the bottom, no plastic unless allowed by the plumbing code","Dryer exhaust of metal flex or rigid pipe, vented outside","Water on, with hot on the left and cold on the right","Plumbing in good condition with no open sewer or gas lines","Covers on all light fixtures, switches, outlets, junction boxes and panels; no gaps in breaker or fuse boxes; service mast, meter socket and panel in good condition","Fire extinguisher (2A-10B:C, mounted near the kitchen) is only required for rentals","Signed mechanical certificate that the heating unit, hot water unit and electrical systems are safe (owner, buyer, licensed contractor or home inspector)","The checklist is not all-inclusive","Also: Open permits closed: Open permit request; all permits must be closed out before the application is accepted.","Also: Well water analysis: If the property has a well, an approved water analysis from the Ocean County Board of Health is required before the certificate is issued.","Also: Mechanical certification: Signed certificate that the heating unit, hot water unit and electrical systems are safe.","Also: Estate or business owner papers: Surrogate letter or POA for estates; letter of formation for business owners."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale inspection (table row: Resale / Fee / Re-Inspection Fee)","amount":"$60.00"},{"label":"Resale reinspection","amount":"$30.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.leht.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/EXISTING-STRUCTURE-RESALE-RENTAL-APPLICATION.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.leht.com/zoning-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.leht.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/EXISTING-STRUCTURE-RESALE-RENTAL-APPLICATION.pdf","label":"Official source (leht.com)"},{"url":"https://www.leht.com/zoning-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (leht.com)"},{"url":"https://www.leht.com/construction/","label":"Official source (leht.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Pursuant to Little Egg Harbor Township Ordinance 2001-14 and 8-10.0 all properties sold and rented shall have their heating unit, hot water unit, plumbing and electrical system inspected and certified. Then the certification has to be delivered to the construction code official before Certificate of Inspection/ Occupancy can be issued.$t$, $t$2ed30a1bda00ff424689ae7ae65812da4287a35081f05e6712041574b580ec98$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":17,"q_ok":9,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":8},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1517.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1517.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1517$t$, $t$Little Egg Harbor Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Little Egg Harbor Township Construction Office (smoke and CO alarms checked in the Existing Structure Certificate of Occupancy inspection) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Ronald Piszar, Construction Official / Fire Sub-Code Official · (609) 296-7241 ext. 618 · rpiszar@leht.com","How to apply: Apply for the resale Existing Structure Certificate of Occupancy (see the town certificate); its inspection checklist covers smoke and CO alarms.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 5/30/2025: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","Smoke alarms on each floor including the basement and within 10 feet of all bedrooms; interconnected systems must stay interconnected","CO alarms outside of and within 10 feet of all bedrooms","Fire extinguisher only required for rentals (per the Township form revised 2/24/2026)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale Certificate of Occupancy inspection (same single inspection as the town certificate; not charged twice)","amount":"$60.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.leht.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/EXISTING-STRUCTURE-RESALE-RENTAL-APPLICATION.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.leht.com/construction/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.leht.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/EXISTING-STRUCTURE-RESALE-RENTAL-APPLICATION.pdf","label":"Official source (leht.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.leht.com/construction/","label":"Official source (leht.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Smoke Detectors: are required 1 on each floor of the house (including basement); also must be within 10 feet of any/all bedroom(s). If you have an interconnected system, all must be interconnected.$t$, $t$7515c8fa3184606f3782cd0c3bfd5b27138126669ea5af51c57d822787904099$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":17,"q_ok":9,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":8},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1517.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1517.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1518$t$, $t$Long Beach Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate of Occupancy (RCO)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Long Beach Township Construction Office","Contact: Kelly Phillips, Resale CO contact, Construction Office · (609) 361-1000 ext 6655","How to apply: Fill out the top of the Resale Certificate of Occupancy application and bring or send it with a check payable to Long Beach Township ($75 single family, $150 duplex), lock box or access code, a current survey (to scale, within 1 year), a flood elevation certificate if built after 1984, condo certification if applicable, and the recorded Deed Restriction. At minimum an application, check, survey and entry information are needed to schedule. Call to schedule the inspection: Wednesdays for the South End, Thursdays for the North End, weather permitting, with a daily limit. Construction Office, 6805 Long Beach Blvd, Brant Beach, NJ 08008; 609-361-6679; Monday to Friday 8:30 am to 3 pm.","Fire extinguisher: at least 2A:10BC, within 10 feet of the kitchen, no more than 5 feet off the floor, visible and mounted","CO alarm within 10 feet of all sleeping areas if there is a fuel-fired appliance or attached garage","Smoke alarm in each living space; battery units must be 10-year sealed; hard-wired or interconnected alarms in homes built after January 1977 must be kept working","House number visible on the house (a mailbox does not count)","Handrails on all stairs with 4 or more risers","Flood vents free of obstructions","Concrete sidewalks and curbs where applicable (Boulevard)","Buffer on windows at stairs or landings where applicable","Water meter installed and activated","No open permits: all permits paid, inspected and closed out","All structures in the right-of-way removed before the certificate is issued","Property visually inspected for compliance with general Township ordinances","Also: Deed restriction: Required on all homes; must be recorded with the Ocean County Clerk before the Resale CO is released (2026 form on the Construction & Zoning page, notarized).","Also: Survey and flood elevation certificate: Current survey to scale within 1 year; flood elevation certificate if built after 1984.","Also: Water meter: Must be installed and activated.","Also: Open permits: All permits must be paid for, inspected and closed out."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Single family","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Duplex","amount":"$150.00"},{"label":"Reinspection","amount":"$25.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.longbeachtownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/RESALE-CO-APP.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.longbeachtownship.com/construction-zoning/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.longbeachtownship.com/construction-zoning/","label":"Official source (longbeachtownship.com)"},{"url":"https://www.longbeachtownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/RESALE-CO-APP.pdf","label":"Official source (longbeachtownship.com)"},{"url":"https://www.longbeachtownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Resale-CO-Checklist.pdf","label":"Official source (longbeachtownship.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Resale CO’s: questions please contact: Kelly Phillips (609) 361-1000 ext 6655$t$, $t$c8c480c1a0adebffa36a40e87aac20daefc5a0d9c73020f827517c20b5375762$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":15,"q_ok":15,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1518.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1518.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1518$t$, $t$Long Beach Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Long Beach Township Construction Office (smoke, CO and extinguisher checked in the Resale Certificate of Occupancy) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Anthony Pesic, Construction Official · 609-361-6680","How to apply: Apply for the Resale Certificate of Occupancy with the Construction Office (see the town certificate); the application has lines for smoke detectors, hard-wired alarms, CO detectors and the fire extinguisher.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 2/12/2025: Dennis Allen · (732) 370-7360 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","Smoke alarm in each living space; battery units must be 10-year sealed; hard-wired or interconnected alarms in homes built after January 1977 must be kept working","CO alarm within 10 feet of all sleeping areas if there is a fuel-fired appliance or attached garage","Fire extinguisher at least 2A:10BC, within 10 feet of the kitchen, top no more than 5 feet off the floor, visible and mounted (Township checklist updated 1/3/2025, before P.L.2025, c.19 removed the extinguisher from the state rule)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale CO inspection, single family (same single inspection as the town certificate; not charged twice)","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Resale CO inspection, duplex (same single inspection as the town certificate)","amount":"$150.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.longbeachtownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/RESALE-CO-APP.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.longbeachtownship.com/construction-zoning/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.longbeachtownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/RESALE-CO-APP.pdf","label":"Official source (longbeachtownship.com)"},{"url":"https://www.longbeachtownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Resale-CO-Checklist.pdf","label":"Official source (longbeachtownship.com)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.longbeachtownship.com/construction-zoning/","label":"Official source (longbeachtownship.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Smoke Detectors: __________ Hard Wired: __________ CO Detectors: __________ Fire Extinguisher: __________$t$, $t$117ddbac8f268f4948ac9bb16a593a151a09595b2be3c0eef4a21f442ae8bc7a$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":15,"q_ok":15,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1518.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1518.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1519$t$, $t$Manchester Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Re-occupancy (non-rental / resale)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Manchester Township Department of Inspections, Land Use & Planning","Contact: Michael Martin, Construction Official / Electric Subcode Official / Fire Marshal · 732-657-6700 · building@manchestertwp.com","Apply: Standard inspections are scheduled by inspector availability; next-working-day inspection costs $300 and payment must be in by 3:00 p.m.","How to apply: Apply and pay online through the Township's FastTrackGov citizen portal ('Apply for a Reoccupancy Inspection'), or complete Section A of the Non-Rental (resale) Re-occupancy application and pay by check payable to Manchester Township. All fees are non-refundable. Department of Inspections, Land Use & Planning, 1 Colonial Drive (Town Hall basement), Manchester, NJ 08759; 732-657-6700; building@manchestertwp.com; office hours 9:00 a.m. to 3:30 p.m. weekdays.","Smoke alarms and carbon monoxide alarms (the application is the Uniform Fire Code smoke and CO alarm certificate application)","Well certification if the home is on a well","Fireplace or chimney certification if there is a fireplace","Open permits must be listed; homes with open permits cannot use the accelerated fee","Email address required for notices; only the named contact person receives inspection information","The applicant must read, initial and sign the Township notice to homeowners, buyers, sellers and realtors","Also: Open permits: List any open permits on the application; homes with open permits cannot use the accelerated next-day inspection until the permits are closed.","Also: Well and fireplace/chimney certifications: The application asks whether a well certification and a fireplace/chimney certification are provided."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Inspection, standard","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Inspection, next working day (accelerated; not available with open permits; pay by 3:00 p.m.)","amount":"$300.00"},{"label":"Reinspection when a smoke or CO alarm is deficient","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Reinspection for a missed appointment or locked door","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Failed reinspection, additional fee","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://manchestertwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Re-Occ_CO-Application__NON-RENTAL-REVISED-Nov-2025.pdf$t$, $t$https://manchestertwp.com/departments/department-of-inspection/inspections-division/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://manchestertwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Re-Occ_CO-Application__NON-RENTAL-REVISED-Nov-2025.pdf","label":"Official source (manchestertwp.com)"},{"url":"https://manchestertwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Re-Occupancy-ISSUES_LTR.-to-HOs_UPDATED_02-21-25.pdf","label":"Official source (manchestertwp.com)"},{"url":"https://manchestertwp.com/forms/","label":"Official source (manchestertwp.com)"},{"url":"https://manchestertwp.com/departments/department-of-inspection/inspections-division/","label":"Official source (manchestertwp.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Please be reminded that no dwelling unit may be occupied until a Certificate of Re-occupancy approval has been issued by this Department.$t$, $t$ce3e580d81231dfb4b1126c781907919b7cbeb6bb895cb2cc35d1d76a072e038$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":10,"fee_ok":10,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":16,"q_ok":16,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1519.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1519.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1519$t$, $t$Manchester Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Manchester Township Department of Inspections, Land Use & Planning (Fire Marshal; Re-occupancy smoke and CO certificate) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Michael P Martin, Fire Official (Construction Official / Fire Marshal) · 732-657-6700 · mmartin@manchestertwp.com","Apply: Next-working-day inspection available for $300 if paid by 3:00 p.m. and no open permits","How to apply: Same application and portal as the Certificate of Re-occupancy (see the town certificate).","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 7/17/2026: Michael P Martin · (732) 657-8121 · mmartin@manchestertwp.com","Smoke alarms and CO alarms are checked in the Township Re-occupancy inspection; a deficient smoke or CO alarm means a $100 reinspection fee","The current application (revised 11-6-2025) does not list a fire extinguisher","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Inspection, standard (same combined Re-occupancy inspection; not charged twice)","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Inspection, next working day (accelerated; not available with open permits; pay by 3:00 p.m.) (same combined Re-occupancy inspection; not charged twice)","amount":"$300.00"},{"label":"Reinspection when a smoke or CO alarm is deficient (same combined Re-occupancy inspection; not charged twice)","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Reinspection for a missed appointment or locked door (same combined Re-occupancy inspection; not charged twice)","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Failed reinspection, additional fee (same combined Re-occupancy inspection; not charged twice)","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://manchestertwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Re-Occ_CO-Application__NON-RENTAL-REVISED-Nov-2025.pdf$t$, $t$https://manchestertwp.com/departments/department-of-inspection/inspections-division/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://manchestertwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Re-Occ_CO-Application__NON-RENTAL-REVISED-Nov-2025.pdf","label":"Official source (manchestertwp.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://manchestertwp.com/departments/department-of-inspection/inspections-division/","label":"Official source (manchestertwp.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$New Jersey Uniform Fire Code Certificate of Smoke Alarm & Carbon Monoxide Alarm Compliance One and Two Family or Attached Single Family Dwellings Non-Rental Inspection Application$t$, $t$f364ee92cfb0f856d39bd68b2ec4e016eb6eb809a94f14fa7aafe82289c3f49d$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":10,"fee_ok":10,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":16,"q_ok":16,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1519.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1519.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1520$t$, $t$Mantoloking Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Transfer/Sale certification of inspection (Transfer/Sale & Rental Application)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Mantoloking Building Department and Fire Official","Contact: Todd Morgano, Construction Code Official · 732-475-6983 Ext. 310 · building@mantoloking.org","Apply: Application must be received 15 days before the home is occupied","How to apply: Download the Transfer/Sale & Rental Application, check 'Transfer/Sale' and give the closing date, owner, seller's attorney and agent, and buyer. Pay $100 by cash, check or money order payable to the Borough of Mantoloking. Submit at least 15 days before occupancy. The Construction Department asks for inspection requests in writing by email to building@mantoloking.org. Borough of Mantoloking, PO Box 247, 202 Downer Avenue, Mantoloking, NJ 08738; 732-475-6983 ext. 310.","Smoke alarms on all levels","Carbon monoxide alarms installed","Fire extinguisher (Borough checklist revised 4/2021)","All open permits must be closed out before the sale is approved","Also: Open permits: All open permits must be closed out before the sale is approved."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Transfer/Sale inspection (one inspection; the same fee covers the smoke, CO and extinguisher check)","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Reinspection for violations","amount":"$25"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.mantoloking.org/DocumentCenter/View/1413/Transfer-and-Rental-Application-$t$, $t$https://www.mantoloking.org/1213/Construction-and-Building$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.mantoloking.org/DocumentCenter/View/1413/Transfer-and-Rental-Application-","label":"Official source (mantoloking.org)"},{"url":"https://www.mantoloking.org/1302/Forms-Permits","label":"Official source (mantoloking.org)"},{"url":"https://www.mantoloking.org/1230/Contact-Information","label":"Official source (mantoloking.org)"},{"url":"https://www.mantoloking.org/1213/Construction-and-Building","label":"Official source (mantoloking.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$TRANSFER/SALE & RENTAL APPLICATION$t$, $t$4c357113a74c8eb8d442f4c034776d86002541bff305a519326a3e6bcda5fbd6$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1520.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1520.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1520$t$, $t$Mantoloking Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Mantoloking Fire Official (Transfer/Sale inspection) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Ron Piszar, Fire Official · 732-475-6983, ext. 310 · building@mantoloking.org","Apply: Application must be received 15 days before the home is occupied","How to apply: Submit the Borough Transfer/Sale & Rental Application with the $100 fee (see the town certificate). The Fire Official inspects on Mondays and Wednesdays, 4 pm to 6 pm.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 10/22/2019: Ronald J Piszar · building@mantoloking.org","Smoke alarms on each floor, including the basement and finished attics, within 10 feet of all bedrooms, and not in the stairway","Ceiling mounting at least 4 inches from the wall, or wall mounting with the top 4 to 12 inches below the ceiling's highest point","Homes built with electric interconnected smoke alarms must keep them; they cannot be replaced with battery units","CO alarms within 10 feet of all bedrooms","Fire extinguisher rated 2A:10BC, no more than 10 pounds, mounted within 10 feet of the kitchen and visible from it (not in a pantry or laundry room); the Borough sheet prints its height limit as 'no higher than 5\" from the floor'; the checklist (revised 4/2021) predates P.L.2025, c.19, which removed the extinguisher from the state requirement, and the packet still includes a 2005 DCA extinguisher memo","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Transfer/Sale inspection (same single inspection as the town certificate; not charged twice)","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Reinspection for violations","amount":"$25"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.mantoloking.org/DocumentCenter/View/1413/Transfer-and-Rental-Application-$t$, $t$https://www.mantoloking.org/1230/Contact-Information$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.mantoloking.org/DocumentCenter/View/1413/Transfer-and-Rental-Application-","label":"Official source (mantoloking.org)"},{"url":"https://www.mantoloking.org/1230/Contact-Information","label":"Official source (mantoloking.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$CHECKOFF LIST FOR TRANSFER/RENTAL APPLICATIONS$t$, $t$d88b8b6caef578d190c5a03027c2da8a6fdc7cecd304634c8128507c699c573e$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1520.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1520.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1522$t$, $t$Ocean Gate Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Existing Structure Certificate of Occupancy$t$, $j$["Issued by: Ocean Gate Borough Construction / Code / Zoning office (Borough Official Inspector)","Contact: Cindy Hummel, Technical Assistant to Construction Official · 732-269-3166, ext. 129 · ogcode@oceangatenjgov.com","How to apply: Fill out the Borough's Application for Resale Existing Structure Certificate of Occupancy and return it to the Construction office at Borough Hall, 801 Ocean Gate Avenue (CN 100), with the $75.00 fee (the form has spaces for check or cash) and the fireplace and furnace certificates. Add a Flood Elevation Certificate and the $110.00 flood review fee if the home is in a flood hazard zone. Office contact on the form: 732-269-3166, Ext 129, ogcode@oceangatenjgov.com. Office hours 9:00 am to 4:00 pm.","Visual inspection of structural and sanitary conditions, fire safety precautions, and any maintenance or zoning violations under Borough ordinances","Smoke and carbon monoxide alarms (the form says they are required by law)","Fireplace and furnace certificates must be submitted with the application","Flood Elevation Certificate (1988 datum) if the home is in an effective or preliminary flood hazard zone","An adult must be present at the inspection","Also: Fireplace and furnace certificates: Must be submitted with the resale Certificate of Occupancy application.","Also: Flood Elevation Certificate: Ordinance #663-22: required with the resale application if the property is in an effective and/or preliminary flood hazard zone; flood review fee $110.00."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale inspection, per building (non-multiple use)","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection if the home fails, per unit or building","amount":"$25.00"},{"label":"Flood review (homes in an effective or preliminary flood hazard zone, with Flood Elevation Certificate)","amount":"$110.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://img1.wsimg.com/blobby/go/3f5a6a60-f81d-45b2-bd17-4c05c6850268/downloads/bf05758b-dd29-4136-b59a-b5d9de7cc649/Resale%20Application.pdf?ver=1790796500164$t$, $t$https://oceangatenjgov.com/construction%2Fcode%2Fzoning-1$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://img1.wsimg.com/blobby/go/3f5a6a60-f81d-45b2-bd17-4c05c6850268/downloads/bf05758b-dd29-4136-b59a-b5d9de7cc649/Resale%20Application.pdf?ver=1790796500164","label":"Official source (img1.wsimg.com)"},{"url":"https://oceangatenjgov.com/construction%2Fcode%2Fzoning-1","label":"Official source (oceangatenjgov.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$APPLICATION FOR RESALE EXISTING STRUCTURE CERTIFICATE OF OCCUPANCY$t$, $t$f9e561132009223c4ad68cf8b7deeda0e48f548bd82718b67f263ab257cdfec8$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":16,"q_ok":9,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":7},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1522.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1522.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1522$t$, $t$Ocean Gate Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Not confirmed: Ocean Gate Borough Construction / Code office (resale Certificate of Occupancy inspection) or NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety","Contact: Charles White, Construction Official · 732-269-3166, ext.125 · ogconstruction@oceangatenjgov.com","How to apply: Not confirmed online. The NJ DCA is the fire code enforcing agency for Ocean Gate, but the DCA's July 2026 list of state-enforced towns does not mark Ocean Gate as a town where the State issues smoke certificates. The Borough's resale Certificate of Occupancy inspection covers fire safety and smoke/CO alarms, and the Borough posts the smoke alarm, CO alarm and extinguisher rules on its Construction page. Call the Construction office (732-269-3166) to confirm whether the resale CO inspection serves as the smoke/CO certificate or whether the seller must apply to the DCA.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 5/19/2025: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","Smoke alarms on each level and outside each separate sleeping area (Borough-posted N.J.A.C. 5:70-4.19 sheet)","Battery-only smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed battery units; AC-powered alarms from the original construction must not be replaced with battery alarms","Carbon monoxide alarm in the immediate vicinity of the sleeping areas (not needed if the building has no fuel-burning device and no attached garage)","The Borough-posted sheet (effective January 1, 2019) still lists a portable fire extinguisher (2A-10B:C, no more than 10 pounds, within 10 feet of the kitchen, mounted on its bracket, top no more than 5 feet above the floor, serviced within 12 months or with a recent receipt); state law P.L.2025, c.19 (February 3, 2025) removed the extinguisher from the state requirement","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://oceangatenjgov.com/construction%2Fcode%2Fzoning-1$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://img1.wsimg.com/blobby/go/3f5a6a60-f81d-45b2-bd17-4c05c6850268/downloads/bf05758b-dd29-4136-b59a-b5d9de7cc649/Resale%20Application.pdf?ver=1790796500164","label":"Official source (img1.wsimg.com)"},{"url":"https://oceangatenjgov.com/construction%2Fcode%2Fzoning-1","label":"Official source (oceangatenjgov.com)"},{"url":"https://img1.wsimg.com/blobby/go/3f5a6a60-f81d-45b2-bd17-4c05c6850268/downloads/Smoke-and-Fire-Ext-info-1.pdf?ver=1790796500114","label":"Official source (img1.wsimg.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$S Ocean Gate Borough$t$, $t$205ece8af102c2c8264a621fb03a375407c8f8e157048716189dbfa90efe9daf$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":16,"q_ok":9,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":7},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1522.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1522.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1523$t$, $t$Pine Beach Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Housing Certificate (Certificate of Occupancy) for resale$t$, $j$["Issued by: Pine Beach Borough Housing Department (Zoning Officer / CO Inspector / Code Enforcement)","Contact: (732) 349-6425 · GStocco@PineBeachNJ.gov","Apply: Allow at least two weeks' processing time; the first inspection needs about ten business days to schedule","How to apply: Bring the Borough Housing Certificate application (2026 COI application and checklist), the $75.00 fee and the heat and/or chimney certificate to Borough Hall, 599 Pennsylvania Avenue, Monday to Friday 9 am to 4 pm. The inspection is scheduled only after payment and all documents are received. The application has a box to request a water read and final utility bill. Inspections are on Wednesdays.","Heating system certification by a licensed contractor","Chimney certification by a licensed contractor if there is a wood-burning stove or fireplace","House number in place and visible from the street","Property free of debris and trash; exterior and interior in good repair (roof, siding, windows, paint, insect screens)","Handrails and guardrails on stairs and decks with three or more risers","Plumbing in working order and all utilities on (gas, electric, water, sewer)","Cooking appliance working, with the anti-tip bracket installed","GFCI outlets by all water sources, exterior outlets and washing machines","Water heater pressure relief valve to code","All open permits closed with final inspections","Comply with the International Property Maintenance Code","10-year sealed battery smoke alarms in every bedroom, one within 10 feet of each bedroom in the hallway, and one on every level (AC-powered interconnected alarms do not need to be replaced)","Carbon monoxide alarm on each level; plug-in or battery, 10-year model not required","Fire extinguisher, 2-A:10-B:C type, 2.5 to 10 lbs, wall-mounted and visible within 10 feet of the kitchen, top no higher than 5 feet, near an exit path, not blocked, with the owner's manual","Homes with a generator, solar panels or battery storage need a printed 'Caution: Multiple Sources of Power' label within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and meter (P.L.2025, c.19)","Also: Heat and/or chimney certificate: Heating system certification by a licensed contractor is required before the inspection; chimney certification too if there is a wood-burning stove or fireplace.","Also: Water read and final utility bill: The resale application has a box: 'Requesting water read & final utility bill'.","Also: Open permits and violations: The applicant certifies that all permits are obtained and closed and any code, zoning or complaint matters are resolved; the office searches for open construction, land use, code and zoning items."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale Certificate of Occupancy inspection (exact cash or check)","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$40.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/api/blob/viewBlob?i=H%2FRTLmPytu9f7Hz3G%2BvzzOQIyufDmVOZAnu3bSEffyaMssMczSf3Jm6wthLdOjvs$t$, $t$https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/housingdepartment$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/housingdepartment","label":"Official source (pinebeachnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/resaleandrentalcertificates","label":"Official source (pinebeachnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/api/blob/viewBlob?i=H%2FRTLmPytu9f7Hz3G%2BvzzOQIyufDmVOZAnu3bSEffyaMssMczSf3Jm6wthLdOjvs","label":"Official source (pinebeachnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/api/blob/viewBlob?i=9dmdajZ6HNBoEgy/H%2BiMKyhOlB2tkA5OhZVvrzq6BMEs7SccYTfJ6zWfGzxyrK/A","label":"Official source (pinebeachnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/codeenforcement","label":"Official source (pinebeachnj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$All residential and commercial units must be inspected by the Housing Department and a Certificate of Occupancy issued prior to: A change in occupancy for a rental unit The sale of a residential or commercial property (both rental and owner-occupied)$t$, $t$bb11b8a3c3ef48977210b3a28925aaddbc47e4427207ded314fa052612f66473$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1523.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1523.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1523$t$, $t$Pine Beach Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Pine Beach Borough Housing Department (smoke, CO, extinguisher and power-source label checked in the Borough Housing Certificate inspection) (town fire bureau)","Contact: (732) 349-6425 · GStocco@PineBeachNJ.gov","Apply: Allow at least two weeks","How to apply: Same application and inspection as the Borough Housing Certificate for resale: submit the 2026 application, $75.00 fee and heat/chimney certificate at Borough Hall. Not confirmed that the Borough issues a separate smoke/CO certificate; see notes.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 6/13/2025: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","10-year sealed battery smoke alarms in every bedroom, one within 10 feet of each bedroom in the hallway, and one on every level (AC-powered interconnected alarms do not need to be replaced)","Carbon monoxide alarm on each level; plug-in or battery, 10-year model not required","Fire extinguisher, 2-A:10-B:C type, 2.5 to 10 lbs, wall-mounted and visible within 10 feet of the kitchen, top no higher than 5 feet, near an exit path, not blocked, with the owner's manual","Homes with a generator, solar panels or battery storage need a printed 'Caution: Multiple Sources of Power' label within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and meter (P.L.2025, c.19)","The Borough's 2026 checklist still lists a portable fire extinguisher even though P.L.2025, c.19 removed it from the state requirement","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Combined Borough Housing Certificate inspection including the smoke/CO check (paid once)","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection (same as the Housing Certificate re-inspection)","amount":"$40.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/api/blob/viewBlob?i=H%2FRTLmPytu9f7Hz3G%2BvzzOQIyufDmVOZAnu3bSEffyaMssMczSf3Jm6wthLdOjvs$t$, $t$https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/housingdepartment$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/api/blob/viewBlob?i=H%2FRTLmPytu9f7Hz3G%2BvzzOQIyufDmVOZAnu3bSEffyaMssMczSf3Jm6wthLdOjvs","label":"Official source (pinebeachnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pinebeachnj.gov/housingdepartment","label":"Official source (pinebeachnj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Smoke Alarms: 10-yr sealed battery smoke detectors are required in every bedroom, an additional smoke alarm is required within 10 feet of each bedroom in the hallway, as well as on every level within the structure.$t$, $t$3286b8fa7b646c036a0ca9db1eb57187b25f55c6678b34058e9ca4218b1e5ea5$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1523.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1523.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1524$t$, $t$Plumsted Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$official_process_found$t$, $t$Resale / Continued Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Not required for sales, per Plumsted Township. Confirm with the office if the buyer's lender or title company asks.","Contact: Robert Thomas, Resale/Rental Inspector · 609-758-2241 Ext: 107 · rthomas@plumsted.org","How to apply: No separate Township Certificate of Occupancy is needed for a resale. The only resale requirement is the Township's smoke and carbon monoxide certification, issued by the Construction Office (see the fire certificate section).","Also: Taxes, abandoned property fees and permits: The office checks that taxes are paid to date, abandoned property fees are paid and all permits are closed before issuing the certificate; unpaid Abandoned/Foreclosed property fees must be paid first.","Also: Uninhabitable or bank-owned resales: The Township has a TCO form for resales of uninhabitable / bank-owned uninhabitable property and an 'Affidavit instead of Permit for Resales'."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.plumsted.gov/1252/Resale-RequirementsSmoke-Certification$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.plumsted.gov/1252/Resale-RequirementsSmoke-Certification","label":"Official source (plumsted.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.plumsted.gov/1202/Construction","label":"Official source (plumsted.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.plumsted.gov/directory.aspx","label":"Official source (plumsted.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Certification of Smoke and Carbon Monoxide Is the Only Inspection Required for a Resale in Plumsted Township$t$, $t$c5a9aba031e19588e37f43d884bda5915093d13a4dfe85866445882abcc84732$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":15,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1524.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1524.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1524$t$, $t$Plumsted Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Plumsted Township Construction Office (Resale/Rental Housing Inspector) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Robert Thomas, Resale/Rental Inspector · 609-758-2241 Ext: 107 · rthomas@plumsted.org","Apply: Schedule two weeks in advance","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Resale Certification completely and sign it. Mail it with a $75 check payable to Plumsted Township to the Municipal Office, 121 Evergreen Road, New Egypt, NJ 08533, or drop it off at the Construction Office (checks, cash and money orders accepted, exact change). Schedule at least two weeks ahead. The inspector does not call to set a time: an adult must be at the home or a lock box number given. The certificate is left at the home unless other arrangements are made. Fees are non-refundable.","Required for all resales, including uninhabitable bank-owned properties","Smoke alarms on each level including basements (not unfinished attic or crawl space) and within 10 feet of sleeping areas; less than 10 years old and at least 3 feet from vents","Battery smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed battery type; an alarm with a removable battery fails the inspection","Hardwired smoke alarms must be replaced with hardwired alarms","Carbon monoxide alarms within 10 feet of the sleeping area, not inside sleeping areas; hardwired, plug-in or battery","Certificate is valid only for a change in occupancy within 6 months of issue","The older Township form (updated 10/26/22) also required a portable ABC fire extinguisher mounted in the kitchen; the current form does not mention one","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale smoke and carbon monoxide certification, paid in advance","amount":"$75"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$50"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.plumsted.gov/DocumentCenter/View/2103$t$, $t$https://www.plumsted.gov/1252/Resale-RequirementsSmoke-Certification$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.plumsted.gov/1252/Resale-RequirementsSmoke-Certification","label":"Official source (plumsted.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.plumsted.gov/DocumentCenter/View/2103","label":"Official source (plumsted.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.plumsted.gov/directory.aspx","label":"Official source (plumsted.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Smoke and Carbon Monoxide detectors are required for the resale, rental, or change of occupancy to single-family houses, condos, townhouses, and mobile homes.$t$, $t$0940fa55484adf3d947478943171e68ad62b248beb4382046be15ab32b8ed43e$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":15,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1524.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1524.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1525$t$, $t$Point Pleasant Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$official_process_found$t$, $t$Resale / Continued Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Not required for sales, per Point Pleasant Borough. Confirm with the office if the buyer's lender or title company asks.","Contact: Colleen Malvasio, Zoning & Code Enforcement Officer · 732-892-3434 ext. 120 · zoningcode@ptboro.com","How to apply: The Borough does not require a Certificate of Occupancy for a resale. The seller only needs the state smoke alarm / carbon monoxide alarm certificate from the Ocean County Fire Marshal (see the fire certificate section)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://ptboro.com/departments/building-code-enforcement/zoning-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://ptboro.com/departments/building-code-enforcement/zoning-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (ptboro.com)"},{"url":"https://ptboro.com/departments/building-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (ptboro.com)"},{"url":"https://ptboro.com/contact/municipal-directory/","label":"Official source (ptboro.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Our Borough does not require a Certificate of Occupancy (CO) for a resale or rental of a home.$t$, $t$2618b54143a2e6b90eeb23f92acf50190ddc4212be0673f3f822973b7d0af23a$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1525.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1525.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1525$t$, $t$Point Pleasant Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office, Residential Resale & Rental Home Inspections (county agency)","Contact: Dennis M. Allen, Chief Fire Marshal (phone and email shown are the resale inspections office) · (732) 929-2088 · OCFMSmokeDetect@co.ocean.nj.us","Apply: Apply more than 10 business days before closing for the lowest fee","How to apply: Fill out the Ocean County Fire Marshal's online application (Fill Out Application link on the Resale & Rental Home Inspections page). The office then contacts you to schedule the inspection. Do not mail payment: pay at the inspection by paper check payable to Ocean County Fire Marshal (OCFM), credit card or e-check. Cash is not accepted. Office: 179 South Main St., Manahawkin, NJ 08050.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 5/30/2025: Dennis Allen · (732) 370-7360 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","Smoke alarms on every level including the basement; on levels with bedrooms, within 10 feet of the bedrooms","All smoke alarms, including hardwired ones, must be under 10 years old","Homes built before 1978: at least one 10-year sealed battery smoke alarm on each level","Homes built 1978 to 1983: hardwired alarms on each level; 1984 to 1990: interconnected hardwired alarms with battery backup on each level; 1991 and later: interconnected hardwired alarms with battery backup in bedrooms and on each level","Hardwired alarms that must be replaced because of age must be replaced with hardwired alarms, not battery alarms","Carbon monoxide alarm near the sleeping areas (not needed if no fuel-burning device and no attached garage); battery-only and plug-in CO alarms should be under 5 years old, combination smoke/CO alarms under 10 years","Homes with a generator, solar panels or battery storage need a printed 'CAUTION: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER' label within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and the electric meter","Homes with a monitored low-voltage fire alarm system need an NFPA 72 test report from the alarm company before closing","No fire extinguisher is required since February 3, 2025","Certificate is valid for 12 months from the inspection date","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, application received more than 10 business days before the change of occupancy","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, application received 4 to 10 business days before the change of occupancy","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, application received 3 business days or less before the change of occupancy","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Missed appointment or no entry","amount":"$30.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection after the first free re-inspection, each","amount":"$30"},{"label":"Credit card convenience fee","amount":"$6.95"},{"label":"E-check convenience fee","amount":"$1.99"},{"label":"Returned check processing fee","amount":"$15.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://oceancounty.seamlessdocs.com/f/AppSDCO2FEComp$t$, $t$https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://ptboro.com/departments/building-code-enforcement/zoning-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (ptboro.com)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.co.ocean.nj.us//WebContentFiles//0299689d-3e63-4678-ad90-3b7c04b233c3.pdf","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmStaff.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$New Jersey State Law requires a smoke detector/carbon monoxide/fire extinguisher inspection if you sell or rent your 1 or 2 family home. Please reach out to the Ocean County Fire Marshal at 732-929-2088$t$, $t$7b8ce34c1a55f7570bd9dfa742994c50b19f9e33447e4d39ccd59f071deba10d$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1525.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1525.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1526$t$, $t$Point Pleasant Beach Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale CCO Application$t$, $j$["Issued by: Point Pleasant Beach Building Department / Fire Official","Contact: Brian Martin, Construction Official, Fire Official, Code Enforcement Officer, Fire Subcode Official · 732-892-1118, ext. 224 · bmartin@pointpleasantbeach.gov","How to apply: Apply online through the Borough's GovPilot 'Sale Application for Residential Real Estate' (CCO Application), one application per unit, with the estimated closing date, owner, buyer and agent details and the contact for scheduling. Online applications are paid by credit card only; the form also offers pay later by cash, check or money order. Building Department, 416 New Jersey Avenue, 732-899-3306, Monday to Friday 9 am to 4 pm.","Separate application for each unit (for example each side of a duplex)","The owner, agent or other listed party must be present at the inspection","The application asks for the number of open permits on the property","Smoke alarm on each level; type depends on the year built: before 1977, battery alarms (10-year sealed battery since January 1, 2019) in the hall by the bedrooms and on each level including the basement; 1977-1980, AC alarm in the hall by the bedrooms and battery alarms elsewhere; 1981-1983, interconnected AC alarms in the hall by the bedrooms and the basement; 1984-1990, interconnected AC alarms on all levels; 1991 and later, interconnected AC alarms in all bedrooms, the hall by the bedrooms and all levels (battery backup from 1992)","Carbon monoxide alarm in the common hall outside, but within 10 feet of, the bedroom doors; battery, hardwired or plug-in (not needed if no fuel-burning device and no attached garage)","Homes with a monitored NFPA 72 fire alarm system instead of AC alarms need an inspection and certificate of compliance from a certified alarm contractor or electrician"]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale CCO application per unit, which is the smoke/CO/extinguisher certificate application (paid once, not a second fee)","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection, if needed","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://main.govpilot.com/web/public/ec1c9006-de7_CCO-Application-pointpleasantbeach?uid=7316&ust=NJ&pu=1&id=0$t$, $t$https://www.pointpleasantbeach.gov/162/Building-Department$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.pointpleasantbeach.gov/162/Building-Department","label":"Official source (pointpleasantbeach.gov)"},{"url":"https://main.govpilot.com/web/public/ec1c9006-de7_CCO-Application-pointpleasantbeach?uid=7316&ust=NJ&pu=1&id=0","label":"Official source (main.govpilot.com)"},{"url":"https://www.pointpleasantbeach.gov/directory.aspx","label":"Official source (pointpleasantbeach.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Sale Application for Residential Real Estate$t$, $t$2679c398e2667314572d84fe5dab040e57ef5655910a7d24197059a56c86326a$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":12,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1526.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1526.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1526$t$, $t$Point Pleasant Beach Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Point Pleasant Beach Bureau of Fire Prevention (Borough Fire Official, Building Department) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Brian Martin, Fire Official · 732-892-1118, ext. 224 · bmartin@pointpleasantbeach.gov","How to apply: Apply online through the GovPilot 'Sale Application for Residential Real Estate' (CCO Application), one per unit; pay by credit card online, or choose pay later (cash, check or money order). One of the listed parties must be present at the inspection.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 5/30/2025: Brian L Martin · (732) 892-1118 · bmartin@pointbeach.org","Smoke alarm on each level; type depends on the year built: before 1977, battery alarms (10-year sealed battery since January 1, 2019) in the hall by the bedrooms and on each level including the basement; 1977-1980, AC alarm in the hall by the bedrooms and battery alarms elsewhere; 1981-1983, interconnected AC alarms in the hall by the bedrooms and the basement; 1984-1990, interconnected AC alarms on all levels; 1991 and later, interconnected AC alarms in all bedrooms, the hall by the bedrooms and all levels (battery backup from 1992)","Carbon monoxide alarm in the common hall outside, but within 10 feet of, the bedroom doors; battery, hardwired or plug-in (not needed if no fuel-burning device and no attached garage)","Homes with a monitored NFPA 72 fire alarm system instead of AC alarms need an inspection and certificate of compliance from a certified alarm contractor or electrician","The Borough application still lists a portable fire extinguisher: 2A-10B:C, no more than 10 lbs, within 10 feet of the kitchen in the path of egress, on the maker's bracket, top no more than 5 feet above the floor, with the owner's manual left for the buyer, serviced within 12 months or with a purchase receipt (state law P.L.2025, c.19 removed the extinguisher from the state requirement)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm and fire extinguisher certificate, per unit (same fee as the resale CCO application, paid once)","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection, if needed","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://main.govpilot.com/web/public/ec1c9006-de7_CCO-Application-pointpleasantbeach?uid=7316&ust=NJ&pu=1&id=0$t$, $t$https://www.pointpleasantbeach.gov/194/Fire-Department$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://main.govpilot.com/web/public/ec1c9006-de7_CCO-Application-pointpleasantbeach?uid=7316&ust=NJ&pu=1&id=0","label":"Official source (main.govpilot.com)"},{"url":"https://www.pointpleasantbeach.gov/194/Fire-Department","label":"Official source (pointpleasantbeach.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pointpleasantbeach.gov/directory.aspx","label":"Official source (pointpleasantbeach.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$APPLICATION FOR CERTIFICATE OF SMOKE ALARM, CARBON MONOXIDE ALARM & PORTABLE FIRE EXTINGUISHER COMPLIANCE$t$, $t$771735ca04b6c50de2c13ed7bf8180976dac88cfbb1619eeb31541e51f9740cb$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":14,"q_ok":12,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1526.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1526.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1527$t$, $t$Seaside Heights Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Title Transfer inspection (Title Transfer Application)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Seaside Heights Code Enforcement / Housing Department","Contact: Ken Roberts, Code Enforcement, Zoning Officer & Flood Plain Manager · (732) 793-9100 Ext. 122 · kroberts@seaside-heightsnj.org","How to apply: Fill out the Title Transfer Application (owner, property, block and lot, agent, buyer, sale price, email) and submit it with the $100 per unit fee, payable to the Borough of Seaside Heights (check, money order or cash), to the Code Enforcement / Housing office, 100 Grant Avenue, Municipal Complex Building B. After the application and payment are received, an inspector contacts you to set an inspection time (inspections Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday). General questions: housing@seaside-heightsnj.org, 732-793-9100.","Visual inspection only; it does not include plumbing, heating or electrical inspections","10-year sealed lithium battery smoke detectors in each room, including the utility room and attic (not in kitchens or bathrooms)","Carbon monoxide detector where the property has gas service, mounted between sleeping areas","In pre-existing homes, a mounted 1A:10B-C 5 lb fire extinguisher in the kitchen, 4 feet from the floor and within 10 feet of the stove (Borough form dated 10/2020; state law P.L.2025, c.19 later removed the extinguisher from the state requirement)","The office checks for outstanding construction permits and whether the home was substantially damaged","Final readings on all utility bills before closing","Also: Final utility readings: Final readings must be obtained on all utility bills before closing.","Also: Open construction permits: The office checks for outstanding construction permits and substantial damage when processing the Title Transfer Application.","Also: Buyer who plans to rent: Must contact Code Enforcement for a mercantile license and a rental certificate of occupancy."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Title Transfer inspection, per residential unit, per inspection (check, money order or cash)","amount":"$100"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.seaside-heightsnj.org/DocumentCenter/View/748/Title-Transfer-Application-$t$, $t$https://www.seaside-heightsnj.org/171/Code-EnforcementHousing$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.seaside-heightsnj.org/171/Code-EnforcementHousing","label":"Official source (seaside-heightsnj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.seaside-heightsnj.org/DocumentCenter/View/748/Title-Transfer-Application-","label":"Official source (seaside-heightsnj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Title Transfer Application$t$, $t$460380ae9dd9bd4de7cad4d62ba5863f004013074f57bb15a733118957efdfe2$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":17,"q_ok":13,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1527.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1527.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1527$t$, $t$Seaside Heights Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Seaside Heights Code Enforcement / Housing Department (smoke, CO and extinguisher certified in the Title Transfer inspection) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Ken Roberts, Code Enforcement, Zoning Officer & Flood Plain Manager · (732) 793-9100 Ext. 122 · kroberts@seaside-heightsnj.org","How to apply: Same application as the Title Transfer inspection: submit the Title Transfer Application and the $100 per unit fee to the Code Enforcement / Housing office, 100 Grant Avenue, Building B.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 1/22/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609) 633-6132","10-year sealed lithium battery smoke detectors in each room, including the utility room and attic (not in kitchens or bathrooms)","Carbon monoxide detector where the property has gas service, mounted between sleeping areas","In pre-existing homes, a mounted 1A:10B-C 5 lb fire extinguisher in the kitchen, 4 feet from the floor and within 10 feet of the stove (Borough form dated 10/2020; state law P.L.2025, c.19 later removed the extinguisher from the state requirement)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Combined Title Transfer inspection including the smoke/CO/extinguisher certification, per residential unit (paid once)","amount":"$100"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.seaside-heightsnj.org/DocumentCenter/View/748/Title-Transfer-Application-$t$, $t$https://www.seaside-heightsnj.org/171/Code-EnforcementHousing$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.seaside-heightsnj.org/DocumentCenter/View/748/Title-Transfer-Application-","label":"Official source (seaside-heightsnj.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$1. 10 yr , sealed lithium battery smoke detectors in each room including utility & attic (not required in kitchen & baths).$t$, $t$118eea8eedce1fa0481e35ab6071c4418f946809740b821738708ecd80ec053b$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":17,"q_ok":13,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1527.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1527.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1528$t$, $t$Seaside Park Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Title Transfer Permit (Certificate of Occupancy on title transfer)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Code Enforcement Office (Zoning / Code Enforcement)","Contact: Alexa Palmieri, Code Compliance Supervisor · 732-250-7569 · apalmieri@seasideparknj.org","How to apply: Fill out the Title Transfer Application (property, seller, buyer, realtors and a contact for scheduling the inspection) and bring it to the Code Enforcement Office at Seaside Park Elementary School, 313 SW Central Avenue (use the 4th Avenue entrance), phone 732-250-7569. The office-use section shows $100 per dwelling unit, paid by cash or check. After inspection the permit is approved, conditionally approved (repairs within 7, 14 or 30 days, with or without a re-inspection) or denied until the deficiencies are corrected.","Close out all open construction permits and any existing violations","Property taxes and water and sewer bills paid up to date before the inspection can take place","A fireplace chimney needs a certification of its status from a licensed company before the title transfer is approved","Working smoke alarms (10-year sealed battery, hardwired or interconnected) in every bedroom, within 10 feet of sleeping areas and on each level","Working carbon monoxide detector on every level and within 10 feet of sleeping areas","All smoke and CO detectors replaced within the last 10 years","Portable fire extinguisher mounted in an exit path: ABC rated, 2.5 to 10 lbs, not blocked or enclosed, replaced every 7 years","GFCI outlets at every water source, including washing machine, bathrooms and exterior outlets","Plumbing fixtures working with hot and cold water; heating equipment properly installed and working","Exits safe and unobstructed; no double-keyed locks","Floors, foundation, walls, ceilings, doors and windows clean and in good condition; no rodents or insects","Window screens from May 15 to October 15; bathroom exhaust fan or operable window; all utilities on","House number easily visible from the road; trash and recycling in approved lidded containers (45 gallons max)","Roof, windows, siding, decks, porches, railings (handrail for 3 or more steps), fences, driveways, sidewalks, curbs and sheds in good repair","Yard free of litter and debris; vegetation trimmed back from sidewalks and curbs","Also: Open permits and violations: Close out all construction permits and any violations before the inspection to avoid a re-inspection.","Also: Taxes and water/sewer paid: All property taxes and water and sewer charges must be paid up to date before the inspection can take place.","Also: Chimney certification: If the unit has a fireplace chimney, a certification of its status by a licensed company is needed for title transfer approval.","Also: Flood fee / elevation certificate line on the form: The office-use section of the title transfer form lists 'Flood Fee $100' next to 'Flood Elevation Certificate included'. When it applies is not stated."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Title transfer permit, per dwelling unit (office-use fee line on the application)","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.seasideparknj.org/Documents/Resources/Forms/2025%20TITLE%20TRANSFER.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.seasideparknj.org/departments/code_enforcement.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.seasideparknj.org/Documents/Departments/Code%20Enforcement/AS-IS-Letter-2014-11-21.pdf","label":"Official source (seasideparknj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.seasideparknj.org/Documents/Resources/Forms/2025%20TITLE%20TRANSFER.pdf","label":"Official source (seasideparknj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.seasideparknj.org/Documents/Departments/Code%20Enforcement/HELPFUL-HINTS-2025.pdf","label":"Official source (seasideparknj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.seasideparknj.org/departments/code_enforcement.php","label":"Official source (seasideparknj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$In addition, I also stipulate that occupancy will not take place until an inspection by the Borough of Seaside Park has been completed, and an approved Certificate of Occupancy has been issued, as required by the Borough Code.$t$, $t$20bcc64d2c10894865e49a6b4fef8185a91c8fae7d89abb683d8397760c394b6$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":1,"fee_ok":1,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":16,"q_ok":16,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1528.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1528.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1528$t$, $t$Seaside Park Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Entire borough: issued by Seaside Park Code Enforcement Office (checks smoke alarms, CO alarms and extinguisher during its housing and title transfer inspections; not confirmed as the issuer of the state smoke/CO certificate)","Entire borough contact: Theresa Russo, Code Enforcement Officer · 732-250-7569 · code.enforcement@seasideparknj.org","Entire borough, how to apply: Not confirmed. The Code Enforcement Office enforces the smoke and CO alarm rules during its housing inspections; call 732-250-7569 to confirm who issues the Certificate of Smoke Alarm, Carbon Monoxide Alarm compliance for a sale and whether it is covered by the title transfer fee.","Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire…: issued by Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire code enforcing agency of record for Seaside Park). Covers: Registered fire code enforcing agency for the whole borough, but its resale and rental smoke/CO inspection list does not include Seaside Park","Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire… contact: Dennis M. Allen, Chief Fire Marshal · 732-370-7360 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire…, how to apply: Not confirmed for Seaside Park sales: the County's smoke/CO inspection page says it inspects only in the municipalities it lists, and Seaside Park is not on that list.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 8/5/2025: Dennis Allen · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","10-year sealed battery smoke alarms required where battery alarms are used; hardwired (A/C) alarms from original construction may not be replaced with battery alarms (Borough letter of January 15, 2022)","Smoke alarms on each level including the basement, in each bedroom, and in the hallway within 10 feet outside each bedroom","CO alarms in the immediate vicinity of sleeping areas in homes with fuel-burning devices or an attached garage","Smoke and CO detectors replaced within the last 10 years (Borough housing inspection sheet, November 2024)","Portable fire extinguisher still listed on the Borough's November 2024 inspection sheet: ABC rated, 2.5 to 10 lbs, mounted in an exit path, replaced every 7 years","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.seasideparknj.org/departments/code_enforcement.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.seasideparknj.org/Documents/Departments/Code%20Enforcement/Smoke-Detector-Code-Update.pdf","label":"Official source (seasideparknj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.seasideparknj.org/Documents/Departments/Code%20Enforcement/HELPFUL-HINTS-2025.pdf","label":"Official source (seasideparknj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.seasideparknj.org/departments/code_enforcement.php","label":"Official source (seasideparknj.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmStaff.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmContact.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Updates to the code regarding battery- operated smoke alarms and carbon monoxide alarms went into effect on January 1, 2019. Many homeowners are not aware of these new life safety requirements which are now being enforced on rental and housing inspections in 2022.$t$, $t$bd71058767e197d13aa50af3ba16eee7e16e3fb808657a5d5a68408eb1efe3d8$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":1,"fee_ok":1,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":16,"q_ok":16,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1528.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1528.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1529$t$, $t$Ship Bottom Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate of Occupancy (Certificate of Occupancy for Transfer of Title)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Building & Zoning Office (the zoning officer inspects; the Construction Official signs off on any repairs)","Contact: Matt Bernstein, Code Enforcement & Trash and Recycling Coordinator (resale certificate contact) · (609) 494-2171 Ext. 131 · mbernstein@shipbottom.org","Apply: The Borough approves or denies within 15 working days after a complete application is received","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Resale Certificate of Occupancy and the 'Certificate of Occupancy for Transfer of Title' data form, attach a current survey and Flood Elevation Certificate, and submit them with a check payable to the Borough of Ship Bottom to the Building & Zoning Office, Borough Municipal Building, 1621 Long Beach Blvd. Also complete the Declaration of Deed Restriction for recording. Questions about resale certificates go to Matt Bernstein.","Complete application with the fee check; incomplete applications are not accepted","Current plot plan (survey) and a Flood Elevation Certificate; condos also need a Condo Certificate Survey","Zoning officer confirms the property is a permitted use or a valid nonconforming use under the Land Development Ordinance","Smoke alarms and carbon monoxide detectors on each floor, all working at the time of inspection","Fire extinguisher within 10 feet of the kitchen area (2014 form)","Unsafe conditions are referred to the Construction Official; the CO is issued only after required repairs are done","Leave keys with the application if the home is vacant; otherwise arrange access with the owner or tenant","A Declaration of Deed Restriction (use limited by FEMA flood regulations) must be filed for resale certificates and recorded with the Ocean County Clerk","Also: Deed restriction: A Declaration of Deed Restriction (FEMA flood rules; inspection of areas below base flood elevation on 48 hours notice) must be filed for resale certificates and recorded with the Ocean County Clerk. Condominiums may differ.","Also: Survey and flood elevation certificate: The resale CO application must include a current plot plan (survey) and a Flood Elevation Certificate; condos need a Condo Certificate Survey.","Also: Temporary CO for transfer of title: The form refers to Land Development Ordinance Sections 1002.E.8.I and 1002.E.9 for a temporary Certificate of Occupancy that permits transfer of title only."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale Certificate of Occupancy, per residential dwelling unit","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$25.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$http://www.shipbottom.org/uploads/2/9/2/0/29205155/july-10-2014-co-application-resale.pdf$t$, $t$https://shipbottom.org/government/departments/building-zoning/$t$, $j$[{"url":"http://www.shipbottom.org/uploads/2/9/2/0/29205155/july-10-2014-co-application-resale.pdf","label":"Official source (shipbottom.org)"},{"url":"http://www.shipbottom.org/uploads/2/9/2/0/29205155/july-10-2014-certificate-of-occupancy.pdf","label":"Official source (shipbottom.org)"},{"url":"https://shipbottom.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/rev-deed-restriction-letter-and-form.pdf","label":"Official source (shipbottom.org)"},{"url":"https://shipbottom.org/contact/","label":"Official source (shipbottom.org)"},{"url":"https://shipbottom.org/government/departments/building-zoning/","label":"Official source (shipbottom.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The Construction Official shall issue a Certificate of Occupancy only when the required repairs and/or other remedial action have been satisfactorily completed in compliance with the Uniform Construction Code.$t$, $t$d4df8fa8343cdf49c6fc4b1abb7b8f50509616c5a9610c99a779afdb853d8282$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":21,"q_ok":21,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1529.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1529.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1529$t$, $t$Ship Bottom Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Entire borough (resales): issued by Borough of Ship Bottom Building & Zoning Office (its resale CO inspection checks smoke alarms, CO detectors and the extinguisher; not confirmed as the issuer of the state smoke/CO certificate)","Entire borough (resales) contact: Matt Bernstein, Code Enforcement & Trash and Recycling Coordinator (resale certificate contact) · (609) 494-2171 Ext. 131 · mbernstein@shipbottom.org","Entire borough (resales), how to apply: Not confirmed. The smoke/CO alarm check is part of the Borough's resale Certificate of Occupancy application; confirm with the Borough whether that inspection also produces the state Certificate of Smoke Alarm and CO Alarm compliance for a sale.","Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire…: issued by Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire code enforcing agency), Residential Resale & Rental Home Inspections. Covers: Registered fire code enforcing agency for the borough; the County's page says it inspects Ship Bottom 1-2 family homes for RENTALS only, not resales","Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire… contact: Bree Dominguez, Residential Smoke CO Inspections staff, Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office · (732) 929-2088 · OCFMSmokeDetect@co.ocean.nj.us","Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire…, how to apply: For Ship Bottom the County lists rental inspections only. If the Borough sends a seller to the County for a resale, the County process is: fill out the online application, the office calls to schedule, pay at the inspection (check payable to Ocean County Fire Marshal (OCFM), credit card or e-check; no cash).","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 1/14/2026: Dennis Allen · (732) 370-7360 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","Smoke alarms and carbon monoxide detectors on each floor, all working at the time of the Borough's resale inspection (2014 resale CO form)","Fire extinguisher within 10 feet of the kitchen area (still on the 2014 resale CO form; P.L.2025, c.19 later removed it from the state requirement)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://shipbottom.org/government/departments/building-zoning/$t$, $j$[{"url":"http://www.shipbottom.org/uploads/2/9/2/0/29205155/july-10-2014-co-application-resale.pdf","label":"Official source (shipbottom.org)"},{"url":"https://shipbottom.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/rev-deed-restriction-letter-and-form.pdf","label":"Official source (shipbottom.org)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmStaff.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmContact.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.co.ocean.nj.us//WebContentFiles//0299689d-3e63-4678-ad90-3b7c04b233c3.pdf","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://shipbottom.org/","label":"Official source (shipbottom.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Smoke alarms/detectors and carbon monoxide detectors must be installed on each floor as required by Uniform Construction Code of the State of New Jersey (N.J.A.C. 5:23- et seq.), and must all be in operating condition at the time of inspection.$t$, $t$5a062b00ab21e9cf3e8d2afa7f35e2b6010114db6b771acbf525ae19274ffcf3$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":21,"q_ok":21,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1529.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1529.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1530$t$, $t$South Toms River Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Continued Occupancy (Resale/Rental Certificate)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough Zoning & Code Enforcement office","Contact: (732) 349-0403","Apply: Get the Ocean County Fire Marshal smoke/CO certificate first; the Borough schedules its own inspection only after it receives a copy","How to apply: Fill out the online Resale/Rental (Certificate of Continued Occupancy) form in the Borough's Munilogic portal (southtomsriver.egov.munilogic.com; you log in to an account there). First get the Ocean County Fire Marshal smoke/CO certificate (732-929-2088) and send the Borough a copy; the Borough then schedules its inspection. Borough Hall: 19 Double Trouble Rd., (732) 349-0403, 8:30 am to 4:00 pm Monday to Friday.","Since March 26, 2026, a smoke detector / carbon monoxide certificate from the Ocean County Fire Marshal must be obtained first and a copy sent to the Borough","Also: Fire Marshal certificate before Borough inspection: A copy of the Ocean County Fire Marshal smoke/CO certificate must be sent to the Borough before it will schedule the resale inspection."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.southtomsriver.org/rentalsresalesapplications$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.southtomsriver.org/zoningandcodeenforcement","label":"Official source (southtomsriver.org)"},{"url":"https://www.southtomsriver.org/rentalsresalesapplications","label":"Official source (southtomsriver.org)"},{"url":"https://www.southtomsriver.org/contact","label":"Official source (southtomsriver.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$If you are purchasing, selling or renting a home in South Toms River, please fill out the Online Certificate of Continued Occupancy form.$t$, $t$fe23f22dabc3690463d6b2e0e7a338332cc135ed46fd6c52b3cc67abc0ac6106$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":16,"q_ok":16,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1530.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1530.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1530$t$, $t$South Toms River Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office (county fire code enforcing agency), Residential Resale & Rental Home Inspections","Contact: Bree Dominguez, Residential Smoke CO Inspections staff, Ocean County Fire Marshal's Office · (732) 929-2088 · OCFMSmokeDetect@co.ocean.nj.us","Apply: Apply more than 10 business days before closing for the lowest fee; the office calls to schedule after the online application is received","How to apply: Fill out the County's online application; the office then contacts you to schedule the inspection. Do not mail payment: pay at the inspection by paper check payable to Ocean County Fire Marshal (OCFM), credit card or e-check (no cash). Residential Resale & Rental Home Inspections office: 179 South Main St., Manahawkin, NJ 08050. The certificate is valid for 12 months from the inspection date.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 6/17/2026: Dennis Allen · (732) 370-7360 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","Smoke alarms on every level including the basement; on bedroom levels within 10 feet of the bedrooms","Ceiling mounting preferred; wall alarms 4 to 12 inches below the ceiling, 4 inches from corners and at least 3 feet from air registers","All smoke alarms, including hardwired ones, must be under 10 years old","By year built: before 1978 at least one 10-year sealed battery alarm per level; 1978 to 1983 hardwired alarms on each level; 1984 to 1990 interconnected hardwired alarms with battery backup on each level; 1991 and later interconnected hardwired alarms with battery backup in bedrooms and on each level","Hardwired alarms that must be replaced for age must be replaced with hardwired alarms, not battery alarms","CO alarms in the immediate vicinity of sleeping areas when the home has a fuel-burning device or attached garage; battery-only and plug-in CO alarms under 5 years old; combination smoke/CO alarms under 10 years old","Homes with a generator, solar panels, battery storage or other secondary power source need a printed ANSI Z535.4 label (wording like 'CAUTION: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER') within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and the electric meter","A primary low-voltage monitored fire alarm system needs a current NFPA 72 test report sent to the office before closing","Fire extinguisher no longer required (Ocean County Fire Marshal requirements sheet, updated February 2025)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Application received more than 10 business days before the change of occupancy","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Application received 4 to 10 business days before the change of occupancy","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Application received 3 business days or less before the change of occupancy","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Missed appointment or no entry to the structure","amount":"$30.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection after a failed inspection (first re-inspection may be free; each additional one $30)","amount":"$30"},{"label":"Credit card processing fee","amount":"$6.95"},{"label":"E-check processing fee","amount":"$1.99"},{"label":"Returned check processing fee","amount":"$15.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://oceancounty.seamlessdocs.com/f/AppSDCO2FEComp$t$, $t$https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmStaff.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmContact.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.co.ocean.nj.us//WebContentFiles//0299689d-3e63-4678-ad90-3b7c04b233c3.pdf","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.southtomsriver.org/rentalsresalesapplications","label":"Official source (southtomsriver.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Residential Resale & Rental Home Inspections 179 South Main St. Manahawkin, NJ 08050 Phone: (732) 929-2088 Fax: (732) 929-2077 Email: OCFMSmokeDetect@co.ocean.nj.us$t$, $t$c27d494ad92ca363c727d8daa55d4db4f5e1c980b46ab37c7179bd140efaf375$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":16,"q_ok":16,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1530.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1530.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1531$t$, $t$Stafford Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Continuing Certificate of Occupancy (Resale C.O. for an existing structure)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Building Department (Office of Inspection); housing inspection by the housing official","Contact: Edmond Alvare, Construction Official / Zoning Official · 609-597-1000 ext 8563","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Existing Structure Certificate of Occupancy (check 'Resale C.O.', and in Special Instructions say how the inspector gets in: key, lock box number, owner home). Include the notarized Heat Certification form (clerical staff can notarize it at the counter) and the S.M.U.A. water/sewer letter or approved well test. Submit to Building Inspections, 260 East Bay Avenue, Manahawkin, 609-597-1000 ext 8532.","Notarized Heat Certification from the seller or agent that the heating system, water heater and any fireplace or wood/solid-fuel stove were inspected by a professional","Stafford Municipal Utility Authority letter confirming water and sewer service (if on S.M.U.A.); private wells tested by a licensed well driller or tester and approved by the Ocean County Health Department","Lot and exterior in good condition (roofing, siding, no chipped or badly weathered paint)","House numbers on the structure, 3 inches for residential","Chimney caps on all fireplace chimneys","Electrical: no exposed connections or missing plates, secure fixtures with globes on exterior and closet lights, no open spaces in the panel, no extension cords as permanent wiring, ceiling fans permanently wired, service equipment properly supported","Plumbing and heating: proper venting of heating equipment; water heater and boiler relief valves piped down to within 6 inches of the floor; cold on the right and hot on the left; no leaks; metal dryer vents","Smoke detectors within 10 feet of any sleeping area and at least one on each level including the basement; 10-year sealed battery alarms where battery alarms are used; hardwired alarms may not be replaced with battery alarms","CO detectors within 10 feet of sleeping areas in homes with fuel-burning appliances or an attached garage","Bathroom exhaust fans working if installed","Porches, decks and stairs secure; handrails on stairs with more than 3 risers; guardrails on open sides 30 inches or more above grade","Interior in satisfactory condition with holes repaired and painted","Also: Heat certification: Notarized statement by the seller or agent that the heating system, water heater and any fireplace or wood/solid-fuel stove were inspected by a professional; needed before the C.C.O. is issued. Staff can notarize it at the counter.","Also: Water and sewer / well: Provide a Stafford Municipal Utility Authority letter confirming water and sewer are supplied by the S.M.U.A.; existing well water must be tested by a licensed well driller or tester and approved by the Ocean County Health Department (732 341-9700)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale C.O. (existing structure)","amount":"$40.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.staffordnj.gov/DocumentCenter/View/5917/2023-Updated---Existing-Structures-CO-Application$t$, $t$https://www.staffordnj.gov/156/Rentals-Resales$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.staffordnj.gov/155/Building-Department","label":"Official source (staffordnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.staffordnj.gov/156/Rentals-Resales","label":"Official source (staffordnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.staffordnj.gov/DocumentCenter/View/5917/2023-Updated---Existing-Structures-CO-Application","label":"Official source (staffordnj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Issue Continuing Certificate of Occupancy (rental/resale property)$t$, $t$6c04e27e29647296230489e030b953729ed1272a65c4e96ed958e707194edfbe$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":1,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":4,"quotes":15,"q_ok":12,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1531.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1531.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1531$t$, $t$Stafford Township$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Stafford Township Bureau of Fire Prevention (Fire Official) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Heidi Michel, Fire Official · (609) 597-1000 x8577 · HMichel@staffordnj.gov","Apply: 10 or more business days before closing for the lowest fee; inspections Tuesdays and Thursdays 9 am to 1 pm","How to apply: Send the completed Application for Smoke / CO Detector Certification (with the closing date) to FIRE@STAFFORDNJ.GOV or drop it off at the Fire Prevention Office, 260 East Bay Ave, Manahawkin. Payment must be dropped off at the Fire Prevention Office by check or cash only; scheduling is done after payment, in person or by phone. Inspections are Tuesdays and Thursdays 9 am to 1 pm. Certificates for passed inspections are picked up at the Fire Prevention Office the next business day.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 5/12/2025: Heidi Michel · (609) 597-1000 · hmichel@staffordnj.gov","Smoke alarms on every living level including the basement; on bedroom levels within 10 feet of the bedroom door","Ceiling mounting preferred; wall alarms 4 to 12 inches below the ceiling, 4 inches from corners and at least 3 feet from air registers","All smoke alarms, including hardwired ones, under 10 years old","By year built: before 1978 at least one 10-year sealed battery alarm per level; 1978 to 1983 hardwired alarms on each level; 1984 to 1990 interconnected hardwired alarms with battery backup on each level; 1991 to present interconnected hardwired alarms with battery backup in bedrooms and on each level","Hardwired detectors cannot be replaced with battery detectors","CO alarms in the immediate vicinity of sleeping areas in homes with a fuel-burning device or attached garage; battery-only and plug-in CO alarms under 5 years old; combination smoke/CO alarms under 10 years old","Homes with a generator, solar panels, battery storage or other secondary power source need a printed ANSI Z535.4 label (wording like 'CAUTION: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER') within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and the electric meter","No fire extinguisher item on the current Stafford requirements sheet","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"10 or more business days notice before closing","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"4 to 10 business days before closing","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"4 business days or less before closing","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$25.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.staffordnj.gov/DocumentCenter/View/9232/smokeapp$t$, $t$https://www.staffordnj.gov/815/RESIDENTIAL-SMOKE-DETECTOR-INSPECTIONS$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.staffordnj.gov/190/Fire-Prevention","label":"Official source (staffordnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.staffordnj.gov/815/RESIDENTIAL-SMOKE-DETECTOR-INSPECTIONS","label":"Official source (staffordnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.staffordnj.gov/DocumentCenter/View/9232/smokeapp","label":"Official source (staffordnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.staffordnj.gov/DocumentCenter/View/9231/SMOKEORDINANCE","label":"Official source (staffordnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.staffordnj.gov/DocumentCenter/View/10654/requirements","label":"Official source (staffordnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$RESIDENTIAL RESALE, RENTAL & COMMERCIAL SMOKE DETECTOR INSPECTIONS$t$, $t$c88ad8c3a5c3864e7e88b195c50c3122d5d9d2b077c78e59142d62fe2964f58f$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":1,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":4,"quotes":15,"q_ok":12,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1531.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1531.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1532$t$, $t$Surf City Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate (continuing Certificate of Occupancy)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Zoning Office","Contact: Sandi Gomez, Zoning Office (title not stated) · (609)494-6448 · sgomez@surfcitynj.org","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Resale Certificate (owner, prospective buyer, broker, list and sale data, key or lockbox code) and submit it to the Zoning Office at Borough Hall, 813 Long Beach Boulevard, with the fee. All taxes and water and sewer charges must be paid before approval. The sealed survey and Flood Elevation Certificate in the buyer's name can follow but are needed before the C.O. for closing. A permanent curb must be in place (separate curb permit).","General interior and exterior condition of the structure","Visible house numbers","Final permit approval for all improvements on the lot (sheds, decks, additions, etc.)","Use of the property matches the tax records","Smoke and CO detectors installed and working on each floor and within 10 feet of bedrooms","Living space below base flood elevation checked (whether permitted, flood vents, etc.)","Bedroom egress: no double-keyed locks on interior egress doors","Proper fire separation between garage and living areas (solid core full-thickness door, drywall on walls and ceilings)","Permanent curb in place (curb permit from the Zoning Official)","Fire extinguisher mounted within 10 feet of the kitchen and not more than 5 feet off the floor","Sealed Flood Elevation Certificate in the new owner's name (not needed to start, needed for the C.O. for closing)","Sealed survey in the new owner's name (not needed to start, needed for the C.O. for closing)","All property taxes, water and sewer charges paid before approval; disaster placard returned (checklist item on the form)","Also: Curb: Resales must have a permanent poured-concrete curb; curb, sidewalk and driveway permit fee $50.00 from the Zoning Office. Properties on Long Beach Boulevard, Central Boulevard or North 9th also need an Ocean County road opening permit.","Also: Survey and flood elevation certificate in buyer's name: Sealed survey and sealed Flood Elevation Certificate in the new owner's name are needed to obtain the C.O. for closing.","Also: Taxes, water and sewer paid: All property taxes, water and sewer charges must be paid before the resale certificate is approved.","Also: Disaster placard: The resale application has a checklist line 'DISASTER PLACARD RETURNED'."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale certificate, single-family home","amount":"$75"},{"label":"Resale certificate, duplex","amount":"$150"},{"label":"Re-inspection, each occurrence","amount":"$25"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://surfcitynj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Resale-CO-application-2025-updated.pdf$t$, $t$https://surfcitynj.org/zoning-2/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://surfcitynj.org/zoning-2/","label":"Official source (surfcitynj.org)"},{"url":"https://surfcitynj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Resale-CO-application-2025-updated.pdf","label":"Official source (surfcitynj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Resale Certificates The fee is $75 for a single-family home and $150 for a duplex. Reinspection fees are $25 for each occurrence.$t$, $t$3a62ec16ad2f8dee866e1aec0348b242787f1bfb1905e90618ce326e8c0f9d2a$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":12,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1532.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1532.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1532$t$, $t$Surf City Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Surf City Borough Offices (municipal smoke alarm, CO alarm and extinguisher certificate of compliance)","Contact: Christine Hannemann, Municipal Clerk/Administrator/Registrar (Borough Offices) · (609)494-3064 · frontdesk@surfcitynj.org","Apply: Before any change of occupancy","How to apply: For a sale, contact the Borough Offices, 813 Long Beach Boulevard, at (609)494-3064 or frontdesk@surfcitynj.org to apply for the smoke alarm, CO alarm and extinguisher inspection and certificate of compliance before the change of occupancy. The posted 'Fire CO and Liability Application' is a rental form ('Rental Application & Certification in Lieu of Inspection'), so it is not linked here as the resale application.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 8/17/2026: Dennis Allen · (732) 370-7360 · dallen@co.ocean.nj.us","Smoke detector on each level including basements (not attic or crawl space), and smoke detector and CO alarm outside each separate sleeping area within 10 feet of bedrooms, all working","10-year sealed battery smoke alarms (since January 1, 2019); A/C-powered alarms from original construction may not be replaced with battery alarms","CO alarms in the immediate vicinity of sleeping areas in homes with a fuel-burning device or attached garage (battery, hardwired or plug-in, UL 2034 listed)","Fire extinguisher still listed by the Borough (Zoning page for resales and the Borough's rental certification form): listed 2A-10B:C, no more than 10 pounds, within 10 feet of the kitchen in the path of egress, mounted on its bracket with the top no more than 5 feet above the floor, serviced and tagged within 12 months or a recent purchase receipt, manual left for the new occupant","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Single-family home","amount":"$45"},{"label":"Duplex","amount":"$90"}]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://surfcitynj.org/zoning-2/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://surfcitynj.org/zoning-2/","label":"Official source (surfcitynj.org)"},{"url":"https://surfcitynj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Both-apps.pdf","label":"Official source (surfcitynj.org)"},{"url":"https://surfcitynj.org/municipal-clerk-administrators-office/","label":"Official source (surfcitynj.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://co.ocean.nj.us/OC/FireMarshal/frmSmokeDetector.aspx","label":"Official source (co.ocean.nj.us)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Please be advised that if you are planning on selling, leasing, or renting your property, you must contact the Borough Offices to apply for a smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm, and portable fire extinguisher inspection in your residence and to obtain a certificate of compliance before any change of occupancy or the commencement of the lease or rental of your property as required by the Uniform Fire Safety Code, N.J.A.C.5:70-2.3.$t$, $t$41216e3aca24970a2f441482ee4744ae4fbaa9ad005709a64dcd14c39d1a3eca$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":12,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1532.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1532.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1533$t$, $t$Tuckerton Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale inspection (Residential Resale / Rental Inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Construction & Code Enforcement (Code Enforcement / Housing Official)","Contact: Joe Ventresca, Code Enforcement Officer / Housing Official · 609-296-4916","Apply: Inspections are done on Fridays only","How to apply: Fill out the Borough's Rental/Resale Application packet (check 'Resale Inspection', give closing date and access or lock box instructions), attach the required professional certifications (well and septic, chimneys, woodstoves, fireplaces, heat and hot water, elevation, and lead paint for homes built before 1978), and submit it to Construction & Code Enforcement, 420 East Main Street (609-296-4916). Cash, check or money order only. Inspections are Fridays only.","Yard free of debris and weeds and sheds empty; waterfront lots: bulkhead in good condition, fill maintained on the landward side, no floatable debris around or under the house","Home clean and move-in ready: trash, debris and hazardous material removed; paint, flooring, siding, roofing, windows and screens in good condition","Attached garage: 1/2 inch drywall on walls next to living space and on attic ceilings; two layers of type X drywall under living space above the garage; metal or rated doors in separation walls, including attic access","Stairs with graspable handrails and closed risers; decks and landings 30 inches or more above grade need 36 inch guardrails with openings under 4 inches","Smoke detectors to code (at least one per level in older homes and one within 10 feet of each bedroom) and CO detector within 10 feet of all bedrooms","Anti-tip device on the range","Electrical: no exposed wires, panel labeled, all boxes covered","Plumbing: water heater relief valve piped to within 6 inches of the floor; heating equipment properly vented","House numbers at least 4 inches near the front door (not on the door) and contrasting","Well water test by the Board of Health (if on a well)","Flood elevation certificate in a special flood hazard area","Chimney caps on all fireplaces; chimney, woodstove, fireplace and heat and hot water certificates from professionals","Lead paint certificate if built before 1978; bulkhead certificate (waterfront)","Portable fire extinguisher, minimum 2A:10BC, 2.5 to 10 lb dry chemical, within 10 feet of the kitchen","No sleeping space on the third floor in Tuckerton Meadows or in second-floor loft areas in Bartletts Landing","Also: Professional certifications: Attach well and septic (well water test by the Board of Health), chimney, woodstove, fireplace, heat and hot water, elevation, and lead paint (homes built before 1978) certifications, all done by professionals.","Also: Bulkhead certificate (waterfront): The resale checklist lists a bulkhead certificate and bulkhead condition for waterfront lots."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://tuckertonborough.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Rental-and-Resale-2026.pdf$t$, $t$https://tuckertonborough.com/government/departments/construction-and-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://tuckertonborough.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Rental-and-Resale-2026.pdf","label":"Official source (tuckertonborough.com)"},{"url":"https://tuckertonborough.com/government/departments/construction-and-code-enforcement/forms/","label":"Official source (tuckertonborough.com)"},{"url":"https://tuckertonborough.com/government/departments/construction-and-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (tuckertonborough.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$RESALE / RENTAL Tuckerton Borough 420 East Main Street Tuckerton, NJ 08087 INSPECTIONS PERFORMED FRIDAYS ONLY Joe Ventresca Code Enforcement Residential Resale / Rental Inspection Checklist$t$, $t$d6d087f5696b2a5de60981b182b65d2cf0a150910c894d006a096de7b383da81$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":12,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":6},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1533.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1533.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1533$t$, $t$Tuckerton Borough$t$, $t$OCEAN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Tuckerton Fire Prevention (Construction & Code Enforcement office) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Phil Reed, Construction Official, Zoning Official, Fire Protection Subcode Official and Fire Protection Inspector · 609-296-4916 · PReed@TuckertonBorough.com","Apply: Apply more than 10 business days ahead for the lowest fee; inspections Fridays only; must be done before the new owners occupy","How to apply: Fill out page 1 of the Borough's Rental/Resale Application (inspection address, owners, buyers, contact person, closing date) and bring it with the non-refundable fee to 420 East Main Street, Tuckerton (609-296-4916). Cash, check or money order only. Inspections are Fridays only.","Smoke detectors on each level and outside each sleeping area near the bedrooms; hardwired or interconnected alarms required by year built: 1979 to 1981 hardwired outside sleeping areas; 1981 to 1987 hardwired outside sleeping areas and in the basement; 1987 to 1991 hardwired interconnected on each level; 1991 to present hardwired interconnected with battery backup in all bedrooms, outside each sleeping area and on every level","Since January 1, 2019 battery smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed units; all non-sealed battery detectors must be replaced; hardwired alarms from original construction may not be replaced with battery alarms","Smoke detectors not within 3 feet of a kitchen or bathroom, not within 20 feet of a flame-producing device, and not within 4 inches of a corner or lower than 12 inches from the ceiling on a wall","CO alarm within 10 feet of the sleeping areas","Portable fire extinguisher still on the May 2026 Borough form: minimum 2A:10BC, 2.5 to 10 lb dry chemical, within 10 feet of the kitchen","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Inspection done more than 10 business days after the application is received","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Inspection done 4 to 10 business days after the application is received","amount":"$150.00"},{"label":"Inspection done 1 to 4 business days after the application is received","amount":"$225.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://tuckertonborough.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Rental-and-Resale-2026.pdf$t$, $t$https://tuckertonborough.com/government/departments/construction-and-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://tuckertonborough.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Rental-and-Resale-2026.pdf","label":"Official source (tuckertonborough.com)"},{"url":"https://tuckertonborough.com/government/departments/construction-and-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (tuckertonborough.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$BOROUGH OF TUCKERTON Fire Prevention 420 East Main Street Tuckerton, New Jersey 08087 (609) 296-4916 Phil Reed Joseph Ventresca Housing Official RENTAL/RESALE APPLICATION Certification of smoke detector, carbon monoxide alarm and portable fire extinguisher compliance.$t$, $t$c868a8cf9c545236c0384826ed995ae0994d3652cc5ed6787477ee84ba97ff74$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":12,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":6},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1533.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1533.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1701$t$, $t$Alloway Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Pre-Occupancy Certificate (Certificate of Occupancy)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Alloway Township Housing and Zoning Official (Housing Department)","Contact: Brett Wolvin, Housing and Zoning Official · (856) 935-4080 x210 · housingzoning@allowaytownship.com","How to apply: Fill out the Pre-Occupancy Application (realtor or agent, property, block and lot, buyers, number of occupants, bedrooms, settlement date) and give it to the Housing and Zoning Official with the fee. Pay by check or money order made payable to Alloway Township; payment must be received at the time of the inspection. Also provide the well and septic certificates if they apply, the smoke and carbon monoxide certificate from the City of Bridgeton Fire Department, and a chimney certification if there is a wood burning fireplace or woodstove.","Completed Pre-Occupancy Application and payment","Well certificate (if the home has a well)","Septic certification (if the home has a septic system)","Smoke alarm and carbon monoxide alarm certificate from the City of Bridgeton Fire Department","Chimney certification if the home has a wood burning fireplace or woodstove","Bedrooms: at least 70 square feet for one occupant, and at least 50 square feet per person when more than one person sleeps in the room","Township checklist (undated, older staff name): smoke detector on every level (10-year sealed battery; hardwired alarms must stay hardwired)","Township checklist: carbon monoxide detector on the bedroom level if there are fuel burning appliances","Township checklist: handrails on steps with more than 4 risers","Township checklist: no broken glass in or around the house, such as windows","Township checklist: passing water test","Township checklist: fire extinguisher (2A10BC) in the kitchen","Also: Well certificate: Required with the Resale Pre-Occupancy Certificate if the home has a well.","Also: Septic certification: Required with the Resale Pre-Occupancy Certificate if the home has a septic system.","Also: Chimney certification: Required if the home has a wood burning fireplace or woodstove."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Pre-Occupancy (resale) application and inspection","amount":"$75.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$http://www.allowaytownship.com/downloads/Docs_Misc_Forms/PRE-OCCUPANCY%20APPLICATION.pdf$t$, $t$https://allowaytownship.com/?page_id=147$t$, $j$[{"url":"http://www.allowaytownship.com/downloads/Docs_Misc_Forms/PRE-OCCUPANCY%20APPLICATION.pdf","label":"Official source (allowaytownship.com)"},{"url":"https://allowaytownship.com/?page_id=147","label":"Official source (allowaytownship.com)"},{"url":"http://www.allowaytownship.com/downloads/Housing/CORequirementsandChecklist.pdf","label":"Official source (allowaytownship.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$the following information MUST be submitted to this department prior to the issuance of the "Certificate of Occupancy".$t$, $t$cb66862efeda67c4efea810ab1cfdeb922741ae79f1e7febedd88d3bcc14b793$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":13,"q_ok":13,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1701.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1701.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1701$t$, $t$Alloway Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: City of Bridgeton Fire Department, Bureau of Fire Prevention (Fire Marshal's Office), for Alloway Township under a shared services agreement (town fire bureau)","Contact: Jack Justice Jr., Fire Official (Chief), City of Bridgeton Fire Department · (856) 451-0091 · firedepartment@cityofbridgeton.com","Apply: Submit the request 2 to 3 weeks before the settlement date. Certificate is valid for 90 days.","How to apply: Fill out the City of Bridgeton Fire Department's online 'CO and Smoke Certification Application' (Google form) linked from bridgetonfire.com; the department contacts you to schedule the inspection. Payment is due at the inspection by check or money order payable to The City of Bridgeton Fire Department (the online form says an online payment link will be on the invoice). Questions: email firedepartment@cityofbridgeton.com or call 856-451-0090.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 5/18/2026: Jack Justic Jr · (856) 451-0091 · justicej@cityofbridgeton.com","10-year sealed battery smoke alarm on every level, or hardwired where required; hardwired alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","Basement alarm at the bottom of the stairwell at ceiling level (not between joists)","A 10-year sealed smoke alarm in every bedroom","Smoke and carbon monoxide alarms must be less than 10 years old and working","Carbon monoxide alarm in the hallway within 10 feet of all bedrooms","House numbers at least 4 inches high, in a contrasting color, permanently fixed and visible from the street","Homes with solar panels, a backup generator or battery storage need a permanent, not handwritten, 'Multiple Sources of Power' style label at the main electrical panel and the electric meter","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke and carbon monoxide certificate, request received 10 or more business days before settlement or change of occupant","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke and carbon monoxide certificate, request received 7 business days before settlement or change of occupant","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Smoke and carbon monoxide certificate, request received fewer than 4 business days before settlement or change of occupant","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection for a failed or no-show inspection, same fee schedule as the initial inspection","amount":"$45.00 to $161.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd9PvQCoB-cH5v1UqIaPvFMeDzejV1zzNEnuFMw0yH7LAaFng/viewform$t$, $t$https://www.bridgetonfire.com/uniform-fire-code$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://allowaytownship.com/bureau-of-fire-protection","label":"Official source (allowaytownship.com)"},{"url":"https://www.bridgetonfire.com/uniform-fire-code","label":"Official source (bridgetonfire.com)"},{"url":"https://www.bridgetonfire.com/s/Occupancy-Smoke-Certificates.pdf","label":"Official source (bridgetonfire.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The Alloway Township Bureau of Fire Prevention is administered by The City of Bridgeton Fire Department under a shared services agreement for inspections covered under the Uniform Fire Safety Act.$t$, $t$eba96fcac980cd4b9d7c8951884ba3794a64ad074864bfdf95ba705581e171c3$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":13,"q_ok":13,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1701.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1701.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1702$t$, $t$Carneys Point Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy (Resale/Rental and UFSA inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Carneys Point Township Housing Office (Office of Housing and Inspection)","Contact: Robert Schmid, Housing / Zoning / Public Health Officer / Vacant Property · 856-299-0070 x128 · housingzoningofficer@carneyspointtwp.org","Apply: Submit the Certificate of Occupancy application at least 3 weeks before settlement. Inspections must be scheduled by 3 p.m. and at least 48 hours ahead.","How to apply: Fill out the Township's Resale/Rental and UFSA Application (check 'Resale/UFSA'), listing the property, owner, buyer, both agents and any well, chimney or septic, and submit it to the Housing Office at 303 Harding Highway with payment at least 3 weeks before settlement. Payment must be exact cash, check or money order made out to Carneys Point Twp and is due with the application before review or scheduling. When emailing the Housing and Zoning Department, put the address or block and lot in the subject line.","Buyer may not occupy the home until the Township issues a certificate of occupancy (Township code section 64-2)","All construction permits must be in place for anything newly or previously installed or replaced, such as air conditioning/HVAC, water heater, furnace or chimney","Well, chimney and septic certifications are required when the property has them","Inspector may cite any other item under the International Property Maintenance Code","Smoke, carbon monoxide and secondary power source label inspection (UFSA) is done by the same office on the same application","Also: Well, chimney and septic certifications: The application says a certification is required if the property includes a well, chimney or septic system.","Also: Open construction permits: All construction permits must be obtained for anything newly or previously installed or replaced (for example HVAC, water heater, furnace, chimney) before the inspection."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Residential resale inspection, initial inspection and one re-inspection","amount":"$125.00"},{"label":"Residential resale, each later re-inspection","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Resale/rental application fee, total of certificate of occupancy fee and fire (smoke/carbon monoxide) inspection when not a rush","amount":"$170"},{"label":"Returned check","amount":"$20"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.carneyspointtwp.org/Document/Department/Construction/NEW%20CO%20%26%20UFSA%20APPLICATION-%202026.pdf?t=202604221132360$t$, $t$https://www.carneyspointtwp.org/departments/construction_department/housing___health/index.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.carneyspointtwp.org/Document/Department/Construction/NEW%20CO%20%26%20UFSA%20APPLICATION-%202026.pdf?t=202604221132360","label":"Official source (carneyspointtwp.org)"},{"url":"https://www.carneyspointtwp.org/departments/construction_department/housing___health/index.php","label":"Official source (carneyspointtwp.org)"},{"url":"https://www.carneyspointtwp.org/Document/Government/Township%20Forms%20%26%20Applications/CERTIFICATE%20OF%20OCCUPANCY%20%26%20UFSA%20CHECKLIST%20%26%20FEES-%20NEW.pdf?t=202604021418560","label":"Official source (carneyspointtwp.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$nor shall any person, group of persons, association, partnership or corporation, or any combination thereof, purchasing or acquiring, in any manner, occupy a dwelling unit or permit it to be occupied by another without first securing from the Office of Housing and Inspection of the Township a certificate of occupancy for said dwelling unit.$t$, $t$0fa3cb287dca07ffd1cab6f890364d4e1b1f597ebda434c53ada39c73cd290f5$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":13,"q_ok":12,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1702.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1702.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1702$t$, $t$Carneys Point Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Carneys Point Township Housing Office (smoke and carbon monoxide inspection on the combined Resale/UFSA application) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Robert Schmid, Housing / Zoning / Public Health Officer / Vacant Property · 856-299-0070 x128 · housingzoningofficer@carneyspointtwp.org","Apply: Fee depends on how many business days ahead the inspection is scheduled (10 or more, 4 to 9, 3 or fewer). The combined application should be in at least 3 weeks before settlement.","How to apply: Use the Township's combined Resale/Rental and UFSA Application (the same form as the certificate of occupancy) and submit it to the Housing Office, 303 Harding Highway, with exact cash, check or money order made out to Carneys Point Twp.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 5/19/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","10-year sealed smoke detectors in the common area and in each separate sleeping room","10-year sealed smoke detector within 10 feet of all bedroom doors","10-year sealed smoke detector on each additional story, including the basement (not crawl spaces or uninhabitable attics)","Carbon monoxide detectors within 10 feet of each bedroom in homes with fuel burning appliances or an attached garage","Homes with a secondary power source need a warning label within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and the electric meter","Newly built or renovated homes must have hardwired, interconnected smoke and carbon monoxide detectors with battery backup; regular battery-only detectors are no longer allowed","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke alarm / carbon monoxide inspection, scheduled 10 or more business days ahead","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke alarm / carbon monoxide inspection, scheduled 4 to 9 business days ahead","amount":"$90"},{"label":"Smoke alarm / carbon monoxide inspection, scheduled 3 or fewer business days ahead","amount":"$161"},{"label":"Smoke/carbon monoxide re-inspection (missed appointment, no access, or failed for inoperable or badly placed detectors)","amount":"$30.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.carneyspointtwp.org/Document/Department/Construction/NEW%20CO%20%26%20UFSA%20APPLICATION-%202026.pdf?t=202604221132360$t$, $t$https://www.carneyspointtwp.org/departments/construction_department/housing___health/index.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.carneyspointtwp.org/Document/Department/Construction/NEW%20CO%20%26%20UFSA%20APPLICATION-%202026.pdf?t=202604221132360","label":"Official source (carneyspointtwp.org)"},{"url":"https://www.carneyspointtwp.org/Document/Government/Township%20Forms%20%26%20Applications/CERTIFICATE%20OF%20OCCUPANCY%20%26%20UFSA%20CHECKLIST%20%26%20FEES-%20NEW.pdf?t=202604021418560","label":"Official source (carneyspointtwp.org)"},{"url":"https://www.carneyspointtwp.org/departments/construction_department/housing___health/index.php","label":"Official source (carneyspointtwp.org)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/_odata/firedistricts","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$the owner shall obtain a certificate of Smoke Alarm, Carbon Monoxide Alarm, and Secondary Power Source Identification Label Compliance (CSACMASPSIL) evidencing compliance with N.J.A.C. 5:70-4.19, from the appropriate agency.$t$, $t$027d0905de5c832dce5c79f7403361012ec12aa6dc7281c9bca2f641f9cc2dd8$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":13,"q_ok":12,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1702.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1702.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1703$t$, $t$Elmer Borough$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Resale$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Elmer Housing and Property Maintenance Office","Contact: David Elwell, Housing and Property Maintenance Officer · 856-358-4010 X119 · housing@elmerboroughnj.com","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Certificate of Resale (address, block and lot, seller, buyer, realtor, settlement date, bedrooms and proposed occupants) and send it to the Housing and Property Maintenance Office at 120 S. Main Street, PO Box 882, Elmer, NJ 08318, or email housing@elmerboroughnj.com. Make checks payable to Borough of Elmer. The officer works Thursdays by appointment only. Real estate taxes must be paid to date before any certificate is issued, and the application is void after 30 days.","Valid for: The application is void after 30 days.","Sidewalks in proper condition under Borough ordinance","5-inch reflective house numbers","No trash, debris or unregistered vehicles","Roof, siding, gutters and downspouts in satisfactory condition; no structural damage or rotting wood","GFI outlets outside (including sheds and garages) and within 6 feet of all water sources","Graspable handrails on steps with 3 or more risers (handrails must turn in); guard rails on decks 30 inches or higher","Pools enclosed and GFI protected","No broken windows; windows open, lock and have screens; deadbolts not keyed on both sides","Walls, floors and ceilings without holes or damage and properly painted","Working appliances with an anti-tip range; hot and cold water, working toilets and shower; bathroom exhaust fan or opening window","Water heater relief valve pipe ending 2 to 6 inches from the floor; working heating system; oil heat needs an emergency shut-off at the top of the stairs","Electrical boxes covered, circuits labeled, working outlets, switches, cover plates and fixtures; no extension cords in place of hard wiring","10-year sealed smoke detectors, 1 per level and 1 in each bedroom; carbon monoxide detectors, 1 per level near bedrooms","Fire extinguisher (2A:10B:C) mounted in the kitchen (listed on the February 2025 checklist)","All required permits obtained and approved; real estate taxes paid to date","Also: Real estate taxes paid to date: Real estate taxes must be paid to date before any Certificate of Resale is issued.","Also: Open permits: The resale checklist requires all required permits to be obtained and approved."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of Resale inspection, includes the initial inspection and 1 re-inspection","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Each additional re-inspection","amount":"$25"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/files/141100297.pdf$t$, $t$http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/Officers.html$t$, $j$[{"url":"http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/files/141100296.pdf","label":"Official source (elmerboroughnj.com)"},{"url":"http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/files/141100297.pdf","label":"Official source (elmerboroughnj.com)"},{"url":"http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/Officers.html","label":"Official source (elmerboroughnj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$No person shall occupy the dwelling without an approved Certificate of Resale or New Tenant Certificate for Rental Properties.$t$, $t$a2143475b15f98072145befaab2d116d9484c1bfbda162370647d60f5f6059a9$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":10,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1703.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1703.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1703$t$, $t$Elmer Borough$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Elmer Bureau of Fire Prevention (town fire bureau)","Contact: Jack Justice, Jr., Fire Safety Code Official · 856-358-4010 X113 · fireofficial@elmerboroughnj.com","Apply: Fee depends on how many business days of notice are given before settlement or change of occupant.","How to apply: Fill out the Borough of Elmer Bureau of Fire Prevention 'Certificate of Smoke/Carbon Monoxide Detector Compliance' application (owner, property, block and lot, realtor) and send it to the Bureau at 120 South Main Street, PO Box 882, Elmer, NJ 08318, or email fireofficial@elmerboroughnj.com. Payment is by check or money order payable to Borough of Elmer Bureau of Fire Prevention and must be received at the time of the inspection.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 3/9/2026: Jack Justice Jr · (856) 358-4010 · jdusticejr@comcast.net","10-year sealed battery smoke alarm on every level, or hardwired where required; hardwired alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","Basement alarm at the bottom of the stairwell at ceiling level (not between joists)","A 10-year sealed smoke alarm in every bedroom","Smoke and carbon monoxide alarms must be less than 10 years old and working","Carbon monoxide alarm in the hallway within 10 feet of all bedrooms","A low voltage fire alarm system installed by an alarm company must be tested and certified by an alarm contractor before the inspection; bring the certification","House numbers at least 4 inches high, in a contrasting color, permanently fixed and visible from the street","Homes with solar panels, a backup generator or battery storage need a permanent, not handwritten, 'Caution: Multiple Sources of Power' style label at the main electrical panel and the electric meter","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke and carbon monoxide certificate, 10 or more business days notice","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke and carbon monoxide certificate, 4 to 10 business days notice","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Smoke and carbon monoxide certificate, less than 4 business days notice","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection for a failed or no-show inspection, same fee schedule as the initial inspection","amount":"$45.00 to $161.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/files/141730201.pdf$t$, $t$http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/Fire.html$t$, $j$[{"url":"http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/files/141730199.pdf","label":"Official source (elmerboroughnj.com)"},{"url":"http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/files/141730201.pdf","label":"Official source (elmerboroughnj.com)"},{"url":"http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/Officers.html","label":"Official source (elmerboroughnj.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"http://www.elmerboroughnj.com/files/141730200.pdf","label":"Official source (elmerboroughnj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Smoke detector and carbon monoxide alarms shall be inspected by the Bureau of Fire Prevention within the Borough of Elmer, in accordancewith N.J.A. C. 5:70-4. 19 et seq. and certificates of approval with respect to operation thereof shall be issued by the Bureau of Fire Prevention.$t$, $t$968b25ac4278fc10e4c747120f0956b51f4e1532980b074aec0bde1c298f052d$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":10,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1703.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1703.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1704$t$, $t$Elsinboro Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy for Change in Occupancy (Certificate of Continued Occupancy)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Elsinboro Township Housing and Zoning Officer","Contact: Andy Hoglen, Zoning and Housing Official (also Construction and Building Subcode Official) · 856-935-2200 · inspector@elsinborotownship.com","How to apply: Fill out the Township's Application for Certificate of Occupancy for Change in Occupancy (property, current owner, buyer, both realtors, type of dwelling and rooms) and have the seller's realtor or owner sign it. The application is not complete until the owner or realtor calls the Housing/Zoning Officer at 935-2200 to schedule the inspection. Housing and zoning hours are Thursday 3pm to 4pm at the Municipal Building, 619 Salem Ft-Elfsborg Rd, Salem.","Home may not be occupied until the Housing/Zoning Officer issues a certificate of occupancy","Water test (NJDEP and federal EPA chemical, bacteriological and gross alpha limits); not needed on a public water system","Chimney certification for all fossil fuel systems","Smoke detectors (each level, including the top of the basement stairs and a heated garage) and carbon monoxide alarms near bedrooms","Electrical panel labeled, 100 amp service or more","GFCI outlets in kitchen, bathrooms, laundry, garage and outside","Handrails on basement, porch and deck steps; emergency heater switch at the top of the stairs; heater serviced and inspected","Water heater relief pipe piped down","Roof, siding, windows, doors and screens in good repair; house numbered; trash, debris and abandoned vehicles removed","Fire-resistant door and walls between an attached garage and the house","Fire extinguisher (2A:10B:C) listed on the Township instructions, which predate P.L.2025, c.19","Also: Water test: A water test (NJDEP and federal EPA chemical, bacteriological and gross alpha limits) must be provided before the certificate is issued, unless the home is on a public water system.","Also: Chimney certification: Required for all fossil fuel systems; the visual inspection can be done by a heating contractor or chimney sweep."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of occupancy (change in occupancy) inspection","amount":"$30.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$30.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://assets.zyrosite.com/Hk1eZdfjLtvdh0WU/coapplication-M5puFZ2iiXlZcJ53.pdf$t$, $t$https://elsinborotownship.com/elsinboro-township-departments$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://assets.zyrosite.com/Hk1eZdfjLtvdh0WU/coapplication-M5puFZ2iiXlZcJ53.pdf","label":"Official source (assets.zyrosite.com)"},{"url":"https://elsinborotownship.com/elsinboro-township-departments","label":"Official source (elsinborotownship.com)"},{"url":"https://assets.zyrosite.com/Hk1eZdfjLtvdh0WU/reorganization-2026-min-jgjLAaapjvJQWMij.pdf","label":"Official source (assets.zyrosite.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$APPLICATION FOR CERTIFICATE OF OCCUPANCY FOR CHANGE IN OCCUPANCY PURSUANT TO ORDINANCE # 77-9 & 79-3$t$, $t$c764bc3b3754a18a2151d5e220862288b4aac5afda38fd304029d6896d5df63e$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":10,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":5},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1704.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1704.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1704$t$, $t$Elsinboro Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Entire township: issued by Elsinboro Township Housing and Zoning Officer (smoke and carbon monoxide checked in the Township certificate of occupancy inspection; not confirmed as the smoke certificate issuer)","Entire township contact: Andy Hoglen, Zoning and Housing Official · 856-935-2200 · inspector@elsinborotownship.com","Entire township, how to apply: Unconfirmed. The Township's certificate of occupancy inspection covers smoke detectors and carbon monoxide alarms; call the Township at 856-935-2200 to ask whether it also issues the state smoke and carbon monoxide certificate, or whether to apply to the NJ DCA.","Entire township (fire code enforcement): issued by NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (State is the fire code enforcing agency) (NJ DCA, state)","Entire township (fire code enforcement) contact: Louis Kilmer, State Fire Official listed for Elsinboro Township in the state fire directory (DCA Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement) · (609) 633-6132","Entire township (fire code enforcement), how to apply: Do not rely on the State's online smoke certificate application for this town: the DCA portal data marks ELSINBORO TWP-001 as smoke-certificate exempt, which means the town is not offered in the State's online application. Ask the Township who issues the certificate; the DCA Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement can confirm.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 3/9/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","Township certificate of occupancy checks smoke detectors on each level (including the top of the basement stairs and a heated garage) and carbon monoxide alarms near bedrooms","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://elsinborotownship.com/elsinboro-township-departments$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://assets.zyrosite.com/Hk1eZdfjLtvdh0WU/coapplication-M5puFZ2iiXlZcJ53.pdf","label":"Official source (assets.zyrosite.com)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/_odata/firedistricts","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Carbon Monoxide Alarms Attachment enclosed ... Smoke Detectors Attachment enclosed$t$, $t$1c7bf579fa57f22f17ea6c5001a98fddbc78869f83b14fd8a16d2dca94afb8e8$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":10,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":5},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1704.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1704.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1705$t$, $t$Lower Alloways Creek Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy for Change in Occupancy (certificate of continued occupancy)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Lower Alloways Creek Township Housing and Zoning Officer (Zoning Housing Office)","Contact: John Carney, Zoning Officer (Housing/Zoning Officer) · (856) 935-1549 Ext. 6560 · zoning@lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov","Apply: Schedule the inspection at least 10 business days before settlement. The inspection is only scheduled after the completed application and the required certifications are received.","How to apply: Fill out the Township's Application for Certificate of Occupancy for Change in Occupancy and gather the septic, well water, chimney and other certifications. The application is not complete until the owner or realtor contacts the Housing/Zoning Officer (856-935-1549 x 6560 or zoning@lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov) to schedule. Bring a $50.00 check payable to Lower Alloways Creek Twp to the inspection.","Buyer must get the certificate before buying and moving in; the home may not be occupied until it is issued","Septic certification","Well water test by a New Jersey state approved lab","Chimney certification","Fire extinguisher mounted on the wall no higher than 5 feet, within 10 feet of the kitchen, not blocked","GFCI outlets in the kitchen, bathrooms, sump pumps, utility sinks and outside","Smoke and carbon monoxide detectors must be new 10-year sealed battery units","Water heater discharge pipe ending 2 to 6 inches from the floor","Electrical panel with every breaker labeled","Yard free of debris, trash and junk; grass and weeds mowed","Owner or owner's representative must be present if the home is vacant","Also: Septic certification, well water test and chimney certification: Must be received before the Township will schedule the certificate of occupancy inspection; the well water test must be done by a New Jersey state approved lab."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of occupancy inspection","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://web.archive.org/web/20250216201402/https://www.lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov/sites/g/files/vyhlif3381/f/uploads/co_application_2023.pdf$t$, $t$https://web.archive.org/web/20260402153038/https://www.lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov/zoning$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240702071319/https://www.lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov/sites/g/files/vyhlif3381/f/uploads/lac_code_ver01012020.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250216201402/https://www.lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov/sites/g/files/vyhlif3381/f/uploads/co_application_2023.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250216104431/https://www.lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov/sites/g/files/vyhlif3381/f/uploads/lac_co_pre_inspection_list09242024_0.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260402153038/https://www.lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov/zoning","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The purchaser of any dwelling or dwelling unit situate in the Township of Lower Alloways Creek shall, prior to purchase of the same and occupancy thereof, obtain from the Lower Alloways Creek Township Housing Officer a certificate of continued occupancy as required by this chapter$t$, $t$945a8adb9adbed735e66980704093ef08ce585a7f6288d2a8ebfb8f4ccbfe897$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":11,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1705.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1705.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1705$t$, $t$Lower Alloways Creek Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Entire township: issued by Lower Alloways Creek Township Housing and Zoning Officer (smoke and carbon monoxide detectors checked in the Township certificate of occupancy inspection; not confirmed as the smoke certificate…","Entire township contact: John Carney, Zoning Officer (Housing/Zoning Officer) · (856) 935-1549 Ext. 6560 · zoning@lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov","Entire township, how to apply: Unconfirmed. The Township certificate of occupancy inspection checks smoke and carbon monoxide detectors; ask the Housing/Zoning Officer whether it also issues the state smoke and carbon monoxide certificate or whether to apply to the NJ DCA.","Entire township (fire code enforcement): issued by NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (State is the fire code enforcing agency) (NJ DCA, state)","Entire township (fire code enforcement) contact: Louis Kilmer, State Fire Official listed for Lower Alloways Creek Township in the state fire directory (DCA Bureau of Fire Code… · (609) 633-6132","Entire township (fire code enforcement), how to apply: Do not rely on the State's online smoke certificate application for this town: the DCA portal data marks LOWER ALLOWAYS CREEK TWP-001 as smoke-certificate exempt, which means the town is not offered in the State's online application. Ask the Township who issues the certificate; the DCA Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement can confirm.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 5/19/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609) 633-6132","Township certificate of occupancy list requires new 10-year sealed battery smoke and carbon monoxide detectors","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://web.archive.org/web/20260402153038/https://www.lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov/zoning$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250216104431/https://www.lowerallowayscreek-nj.gov/sites/g/files/vyhlif3381/f/uploads/lac_co_pre_inspection_list09242024_0.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/_odata/firedistricts","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$SMOKE/CO2 DETECTORS (must be the new 10-year battery sealed units)$t$, $t$7e65eac03c120ee3076c4407d6141e6b3cb2868c22ece935e761d4f4c7e6cc70$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":11,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1705.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1705.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1706$t$, $t$Mannington Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Housing Certificate of Occupancy (HCO)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Mannington Township Zoning/Housing Department (Housing Officer)","Contact: Neal Sheppard, Housing/Zoning Officer · 856-935-2359 x104 · zoning@manningtontwp.com","How to apply: Fill out the Township's Certificate of Occupancy Application (check 'Sale Property', list the owner, all occupants and the agent) and give it with the $50.00 fee to Neal Sheppard, Housing/Zoning Officer, at 491 Route 45, Mannington, NJ 08079 (in person Wednesdays 9:00 to 11:00 AM, by mail, or at the Clerk's office or drop box). Questions: zoning@manningtontwp.com or 856-935-2359 x104 (leave a voicemail).","Valid for: The certificate may be issued (or reissued at no charge) any time within 90 days after the inspection that confirms full compliance.","A new certificate is needed at every change of occupancy; no one may move in or place personal items in the home until inspections are passed","Application must list all occupants (name, age, gender) before the certificate is issued","Home must meet the Township housing chapter, local plumbing, building, electrical, fire, zoning, health and safety ordinances, and the New Jersey state housing standards","Housing Officer checklist (2016): septic certification and water test","Checklist: GFCI outlets in kitchen, bathrooms, laundry, garage and outside","Checklist: handrail to the basement and on porch and deck steps; emergency heater switch at the top of the stairs","Checklist: electrical box labeled, 100 amps or more; water heater relief piped down","Checklist: smoke detector at the top of the basement stairs and in a heated garage","Checklist: chimney certification (visual inspection by a heating contractor or chimney sweep); heater serviced and inspected","Checklist: roof, siding, windows, doors and screens in repair; house numbered; trash, debris and abandoned vehicles removed","Checklist: fire-resistant door and walls between an attached garage and the house","Also: Septic certification and water test: Listed at the top of the Housing Officer Checklist (2016).","Also: Chimney certification: Housing Officer Checklist: needs a visual inspection, which can be done by a heating contractor or chimney sweep."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of occupancy application","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Housing certificate of occupancy, single-family building (initial inspection and one follow-up)","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Housing certificate of occupancy, each unit in a multi-unit building (initial inspection and one follow-up)","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Each inspection visit after the first follow-up, paid in advance","amount":"$ 50"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://manningtontwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/CO-Application-Sheppard-1.1.2026-min.pdf$t$, $t$https://manningtontwp.com/housing-zoning/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://manningtontwp.com/wp-content/uploads/meetings/ordinances/2018/ord_18-04.pdf","label":"Official source (manningtontwp.com)"},{"url":"https://manningtontwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/CO-Application-Sheppard-1.1.2026-min.pdf","label":"Official source (manningtontwp.com)"},{"url":"https://manningtontwp.com/housing-zoning/","label":"Official source (manningtontwp.com)"},{"url":"https://manningtontwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/2016_Housing-Officer-Checklist.pdf","label":"Official source (manningtontwp.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$A new HCO (or RCO, if applicable) shall be obtained each time there is a change of occupancy of any building, structure, dwelling, dwelling unit, hotel/motel, rooming house, rooming unit or any other unit or structure for residential purposes.$t$, $t$8f20de8e173e411bc9cc89b392786aaf7ffb108329790429f6dbb25215718803$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":12,"q_ok":9,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1706.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1706.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1706$t$, $t$Mannington Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (NJ DCA, state)","Contact: Louis Kilmer, Bureau Chief, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement · (609) 633-6106 · BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov","Apply: Fee depends on how many business days before closing you apply (more than 10, 4 to 10, under 4).","How to apply: Apply online through the NJ DCA Fire Safety portal ('Start Your Smoke Certification Application'). Pay by e-check or credit card before submitting; a valid email address is required. The certificate is emailed once the application is submitted, the fee is paid and any required inspections are done. Homes heated by electricity that do not need a carbon monoxide alarm should also email BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 2/19/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"State smoke/carbon monoxide certificate, applied more than 10 business days before closing","amount":"$45"},{"label":"State smoke/carbon monoxide certificate, applied 4 to 10 business days before closing","amount":"$90"},{"label":"State smoke/carbon monoxide certificate, closing less than 4 business days away","amount":"$161"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/$t$, $t$https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/_odata/firedistricts","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$S Mannington Township$t$, $t$ab897c538a4e1bcc6952ca24ab4eba83339a4bcbd25a26bc293b32c08145479c$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":12,"q_ok":9,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1706.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1706.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1707$t$, $t$Oldmans Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Residential Certificate of Occupancy (Occupancy Certificate)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Oldmans Township Housing Office (Housing Officer)","Contact: Peter Voros, Housing Officer · 856-299-0780 · clerk@oldmanstownship.com","How to apply: Fill out the Township's Occupancy Application (Word form: address, block and lot, owner or seller, all buyers or tenants, realtor, flood hazard notice) and pay the $50.00 fee with the application before the inspection. Call the Housing Office at 856-299-0780 to make an appointment; CO inspections are Tuesday and Thursday 11:00 am to 2:00 pm. Office: Oldmans Township Municipal Complex, 40 Freed Road, PO Box 416, Pedricktown, NJ 08067.","Needed whenever there is a change of ownership or residents; home must meet Township ordinances and the 2015 International Property Maintenance Code","All utilities on for the inspection; no open permits","Septic certification from the Salem County Department of Health for a transfer of ownership","Well water potable certification (not needed on public water)","Recent chimney certification if there is a fireplace","Address numbers at least 3 inches, contrasting, visible from the road (post at the driveway if the house is more than 100 feet from the street)","Roof, gutters, soffit, fascia, sidewalks and paint in good repair; no abandoned vehicles or standing water; pools fenced 4 feet with a self-closing, self-locking gate","Windows open, lock and have untorn screens; no broken glass; no double cylinder deadbolts or removable interior keys on exit doors","Handrails on stairs with more than 4 risers; guards on walking surfaces more than 30 inches above grade","Hot and cold water at all fixtures, no leaks, bathroom exhaust fan if no window; no gas water heater in a bedroom or bathroom; water heater relief down pipe","Working stove with exhaust hood and anti-tilt device; dryer vented outside; heating emergency shut-off switch","GFCI outlets in the garage, within 6 feet of sinks, in an unfinished basement (including sump pump) and outside; labeled electrical panel, 100 amps or more","10-year battery smoke alarms in each bedroom, outside each sleeping area within 10 feet of bedroom doors, and on each story including the basement","Carbon monoxide detector within 10 feet of bedrooms and one on each floor, including the basement","Fire extinguisher (at least 2A:10B:C, no more than 10 lbs) mounted in plain sight within 10 feet of the kitchen, top no higher than 5 feet","Also: Septic certification: Septic certification from the Salem County Department of Health for a transfer of ownership.","Also: Well water potable certification: Needed unless the home is on a public water system (NJDEP and federal EPA chemical, bacteriological and gross alpha limits).","Also: Open permits: No open permits allowed at the occupancy inspection.","Also: Chimney certification: A recent chimney certification is needed if there is a fireplace."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Occupancy certificate, first inspection (second inspection at no extra cost)","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Third inspection","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://oldmanstownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Housing-Occupancy-Certificate.docx$t$, $t$https://oldmanstownship.com/housing-office/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://oldmanstownship.com/housing-office/","label":"Official source (oldmanstownship.com)"},{"url":"https://oldmanstownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Housing-Application-Checklist.pdf","label":"Official source (oldmanstownship.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$An Occupancy Certificate is required whenever a change of ownership or residents takes place. In order to be eligible for an Occupancy Certificate, a dwelling unit must comply with all Township Ordinances, as well as the 2015 International Property Maintenance Code.$t$, $t$8cb10fe21d85b3ade68edc5427923aca4bc66e400b3664a197a630d8ece9c101$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":10,"q_ok":9,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1707.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1707.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1707$t$, $t$Oldmans Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Entire township: issued by Oldmans Township Housing Office (smoke and carbon monoxide alarms checked in the Township occupancy inspection; not confirmed as the smoke certificate issuer)","Entire township contact: Peter Voros, Housing Officer · 856-299-0780 · clerk@oldmanstownship.com","Entire township, how to apply: Unconfirmed. The Township's occupancy inspection has a Fire Safety section covering smoke alarms, carbon monoxide detectors and an extinguisher; call the Housing Office at 856-299-0780 to ask whether it also issues the state smoke and carbon monoxide certificate or whether to apply to the NJ DCA.","Entire township (fire code enforcement): issued by NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (State is the fire code enforcing agency) (NJ DCA, state)","Entire township (fire code enforcement) contact: Louis Kilmer, State Fire Official listed for Oldmans Township in the state fire directory (DCA Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement) · (609) 633-6132","Entire township (fire code enforcement), how to apply: Do not rely on the State's online smoke certificate application for this town: the DCA portal data marks OLDMANS TWP-001 as smoke-certificate exempt, which means the town is not offered in the State's online application. Ask the Township who issues the certificate; the DCA Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement can confirm.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 5/18/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","Township occupancy checklist (Fire Safety section): 10-year battery smoke alarms in each bedroom, outside each sleeping area and on each story; carbon monoxide detector within 10 feet of bedrooms and on each floor; mounted kitchen fire extinguisher","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://oldmanstownship.com/housing-office/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://oldmanstownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Housing-Application-Checklist.pdf","label":"Official source (oldmanstownship.com)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/_odata/firedistricts","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Carbon Monoxide detector is required within ten feet of bedrooms AND one on each floor (including basement)$t$, $t$cfcbcd5837e2632766867cd27222b919f051a2f238fe0f3d5948626523eeb892$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":10,"q_ok":9,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1707.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1707.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1708$t$, $t$Penns Grove Borough$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy (Sale/Transfer of Ownership)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Penns Grove Housing Office","Contact: Enid Reyes, Housing Office contact · 856-299-0098 ext 100 · housinginspector@pennsgrove-nj.org","Apply: Fee is due before the inspection is scheduled. Any re-inspection must be requested in writing within 30 days of the first inspection.","How to apply: Fill out the Borough's Certificate of Occupancy Application (check 'Sale/Transfer of Ownership'; list the owner, all occupants, the buyer and the realtor), sign the re-inspection rules and ordinance acknowledgment pages, and pay the $50 fee (cash, check or money order) before the inspection is scheduled. Housing Office: 1 State Street, First Floor, Penns Grove, Monday to Friday 8am to 4pm, 856-299-0098 ext. 100.","Home must comply with all Borough building, plumbing, electrical, zoning, health, safety, fire and minimum housing ordinances","All property taxes and water and sewer charges must be paid in full before the certificate is issued","Application must list all occupants (names and ages) and the buyer","Smoke detectors on each level including the basement (top of basement stairs), outside each sleeping area and inside all bedrooms; carbon monoxide detector within 10 feet of bedrooms","Mounted fire extinguisher in the kitchen (listed on the 2021 checklist)","GFCI protection for outlets within 6 feet of water; stove with anti-tilt device; bathroom exhaust fan if no window","Handrails and guardrails on stairs, decks, porches and basement stairs; pool fence at the pool entrance","House number, painted surfaces, gutters, soffit and fascia, sidewalks in good condition; no abandoned vehicles or standing water; all trash and debris removed","Roof, electrical service or chimney certification may be required; heating emergency shut-off switch","Exterior doors may not have a removable key on the inside","Also: Taxes and water/sewer charges paid: No certificate of occupancy is issued until all property taxes and water and sewer charges are paid in full (Borough code section 106-5 C).","Also: Open permits: The application's office section checks for open permits and current taxes."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of occupancy application, covers the initial inspection and one re-inspection","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Each later inspection (a no-show without cancelling counts as an inspection)","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Certificate of occupancy (Borough fee list)","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://pennsgrove-nj.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/Certificate_of_Occupancy-min.pdf$t$, $t$https://pennsgrove-nj.org/housing-office/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://pennsgrove-nj.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/Certificate_of_Occupancy-min.pdf","label":"Official source (pennsgrove-nj.org)"},{"url":"https://pennsgrove-nj.org/housing-office/","label":"Official source (pennsgrove-nj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$CERTIFICATE OF OCCUPANCY APPLICATION Fee: $50 Due (Cash, Check, Money Order) Prior to Scheduling Inspection$t$, $t$29729397ef7224a2db8eef540d4e9d81aa7ebd95abfc5f04604cddbd2ad8d49f$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":12,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1708.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1708.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1708$t$, $t$Penns Grove Borough$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (NJ DCA, state)","Contact: Louis Kilmer, Bureau Chief, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement · (609) 633-6106 · BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov","Apply: Fee depends on how many business days before closing you apply (more than 10, 4 to 10, under 4).","How to apply: Apply online through the NJ DCA Fire Safety portal ('Start Your Smoke Certification Application'). Pay by e-check or credit card before submitting; a valid email address is required. The certificate is emailed once the application is submitted, the fee is paid and any required inspections are done. Homes heated by electricity that do not need a carbon monoxide alarm should also email BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 3/20/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"State smoke/carbon monoxide certificate, applied more than 10 business days before closing","amount":"$45"},{"label":"State smoke/carbon monoxide certificate, applied 4 to 10 business days before closing","amount":"$90"},{"label":"State smoke/carbon monoxide certificate, closing less than 4 business days away","amount":"$161"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/$t$, $t$https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/_odata/firedistricts","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://pennsgrove-nj.org/construction-code-office/","label":"Official source (pennsgrove-nj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$S Penns Grove Borough$t$, $t$f60ecb2f00ed3eb12b6bcac1a4c51e0d8e7b4e19d26e01b148aa31de67d717c1$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":12,"q_ok":11,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1708.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1708.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1709$t$, $t$Pennsville Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Continued Certificate of Occupancy (Residential Resale housing inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Housing Officer, Construction Code Office (Department of Code Enforcement / Bureau of Housing Inspections)","Contact: Dave Curry, Housing Officer · 856-678-3089 Ext: 1150 · housingofficer@pvtwp.com","Apply: No minimum stated. The fee must be paid in full before an inspection is scheduled; the clerk calls to set an appointment within 5 working days of payment.","How to apply: Fill in the Township of Pennsville Application for Continued Certificate of Occupancy, Residential Resale, and pay in full by certified check or money order payable to \"Township of Pennsville\" (or exact cash) at the Construction Code Office, 90 N Broadway. Applications can also be filed through the Township citizen portal (Apply for a Property Inspection, which needs a portal login). Inspections are Tuesday to Thursday, 3:00 to 5:30 PM.","Smoke alarms on every level, in each bedroom and within 10 feet outside each sleeping area (10-year sealed battery type)","Carbon monoxide alarm in the hallway within 10 feet of the bedrooms","Fire extinguisher 2A-10BC, under 10 pounds, mounted within 10 feet of the kitchen in plain sight, tagged or with a current receipt, top no higher than 5 feet","House numbers at least 4 inches and visible from the street","Handrails on stairs with 3 or more risers; guardrails with spindles no more than 4 inches apart on porches or decks 30 inches or higher","GFCI outlets within 6 feet of any water source or the breaker panel","Electric properly installed with no bare wires; heat working","Water heater working, at least 110 F, with the relief valve pipe extended to within 6 inches of the floor","Chimney certificate for fireplaces","Walls, ceilings and floors free of holes, chipped paint, cracks or stains; no rubbish inside or out","Doors and windows working with locks, screens on opening windows, one egress window in each sleeping area","Globe covers on closet and shelf lights; bathroom window or exhaust fan","Gutters, downspouts and roof sound; all plumbing working","Appliances working with an anti-tip bracket on the range; key locks on entry doors only","All utilities on at the inspection and no open construction permits","Also: Taxes, sewer and water current: No certificate of occupancy is issued unless Township taxes, sewer and water bills are current; for a change of ownership the Housing Officer may issue a conditional certificate with taxes paid by the settlement agent at closing.","Also: No open permits or violations: Documentation is needed that there are no outstanding open building permits, housing violations or court judgments barring occupancy; the resale form office section also checks open permits.","Also: As-is sale option: An \"As Is\" Document for Settlement (revised 11/14/22) lets the buyer take the home as-is, signed and notarized; the home must meet the property maintenance code before anyone occupies it."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Continued Certificate of Occupancy, residential resale (initial inspection)","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Housing Officer inspection, house for sale (ordinance)","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection (office form)","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Second re-inspection (office form)","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Second or later inspection for the same certificate (ordinance; per house or unit)","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.pennsville.org/DocumentCenter/View/472/Residential-Resale-PDF$t$, $t$https://www.pennsville.org/175/Construction-Code-Office$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://pennsvillenj.portal.fasttrackgov.com/","label":"Official source (pennsvillenj.portal.fasttrackgov.com)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsville.org/DocumentCenter/View/255/Chapter-07-Buildings-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsville.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsville.org/DocumentCenter/View/472/Residential-Resale-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsville.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsville.org/DocumentCenter/View/481/Minimum-CO-Requirements-For-Housing-Inspection-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsville.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsville.org/Directory.aspx?EID=23","label":"Official source (pennsville.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Apply for a Certificate of Continued Occupancy inspection. This inspection is required when residential property is sold or for changes in tenancy for residential rental properties.$t$, $t$834429aeaac946c73489107fc300781c1233a2743f9f49ee36fc96e914c3c6f2$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":13,"q_ok":8,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":5},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1709.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1709.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1709$t$, $t$Pennsville Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Pennsville Township Bureau of Fire Prevention and Inspections (town fire bureau)","Contact: Eric Guglielmo, Fire Administrator (Fire Official in the state fire directory) · 856-678-3089 ext. 1144 · pvfirecode@pvtwp.com","How to apply: Not published separately. Smoke alarm, CO alarm and extinguisher checks are part of the Township resale housing inspection (Continued Certificate of Occupancy). Ask the Construction Code Office or the Fire Administrator whether a separate smoke/CO certificate and fee apply.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 5/19/2026: Eric Guglielmo · (856) 678-3089 · pvfireofficial@pvtwp.com","Township handout asks for 10-year sealed battery smoke alarms on each level, in each bedroom and within 10 feet outside each sleeping area","Carbon monoxide alarm in the hallway within 10 feet of the bedrooms","Township handout still lists a 2A-10BC fire extinguisher (under 10 pounds) mounted within 10 feet of the kitchen, tagged or with a current receipt, top no more than 5 feet above the floor","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.pennsville.org/221/Pennsville-Township-Fire-Department$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsville.org/DocumentCenter/View/247/Chapter-14-Protection-Of-Life-And-Property-Doc-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsville.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsville.org/221/Pennsville-Township-Fire-Department","label":"Official source (pennsville.org)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsville.org/DocumentCenter/View/481/Minimum-CO-Requirements-For-Housing-Inspection-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsville.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$M Pennsville Township$t$, $t$7d38bd47de0b3cdc34021c771e33c1d2787bd929f7ccbb707d43ed0d86d8a168$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":13,"q_ok":8,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":5},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1709.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1709.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1710$t$, $t$Pilesgrove Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy (CO), Sales$t$, $j$["Issued by: Zoning & Housing Office (Housing Official)","Contact: Tanya Timberman, Zoning & Housing Officer (Housing Official) · 856-769-4814 Ext. 6 · zoning@PilesgroveNJ.org","Apply: 48 hours notice is required for the inspection; the application and fee must be in before an inspection is scheduled.","How to apply: Fill in the Township of Pilesgrove Application for Certificate of Occupancy (CO), Sales Only (revised 5/13/2025) and submit it with the fee to the Zoning & Housing Office; the office form records payment by cash or check. The owner or agent then calls to schedule the inspection (48 hours notice). Office hours are Monday and Wednesday 8:30 am to 2 pm; inspections 12 pm to 2 pm.","House numbers 5 inches high and visible from the street","GFI protected outlets within 6 feet of a water source and on all exterior outlets","Fire extinguisher mounted in the kitchen","Appliances installed properly and working, no extension cords; exhaust fan over the stove (ductless hood allowed) and anti-tip bracket on the stove","Adequate electric, heating and plumbing service; two separate outlets in each habitable room","Bathroom vented or with a working window","Screened window in each room; all windows working with locks; exterior doors and hardware working","Handrails on steps with more than 3 risers; rails around landings or porches 30 inches or higher","Water heater relief valve piped to within 6 inches of the floor; emergency shut-off at the top of the stairs for a basement heater","In-ground pool fenced at least 4 feet high with a self-latching gate","House free of insect infestation","No work done without permits and no open construction permits","Well water test, chimney inspection and smoke/CO inspection must pass","Also: Well water test: A well certificate / passing water test is needed before the CO is issued.","Also: Chimney certificate: A chimney certificate is needed before the CO is issued.","Also: Septic: The Township does not inspect septic systems as part of the CO; a septic inspection is recommended but not required by the state.","Also: No open permits: The CO checklist checks for work done without permits and open construction permits."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of Occupancy for a sale (initial inspection and one follow-up)","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$75"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/DocumentCenter/View/321/CO-Sales-Application$t$, $t$https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/230/Zoning-Housing$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/DocumentCenter/View/321/CO-Sales-Application","label":"Official source (pilesgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/DocumentCenter/View/326/CO-Inspection-Checklist","label":"Official source (pilesgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Minutes/_02242026-33","label":"Official source (pilesgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/230/Zoning-Housing","label":"Official source (pilesgrovenj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Township of Pilesgrove Application for Certificate of Occupancy (CO) SALES Only (Revised 5/13/2025)$t$, $t$8002a1dff0611a4d4044d3335dd3cf5a80056d0679deae83902cddababbf337e$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":18,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1710.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1710.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1710$t$, $t$Pilesgrove Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Pilesgrove Township Fire Inspector for CO…: issued by Pilesgrove Township Fire Inspector for CO Requirements (through the Zoning & Housing Office). Covers: Entire township, as part of the Township Certificate of Occupancy for a sale (per 2026 Township actions; not yet reflected in state lists)","Pilesgrove Township Fire Inspector for CO… contact: Leroy Pierce, Fire Inspector for CO Requirements (appointed by Resolution 26-027, February 10, 2026); no direct phone or email… · 856-769-4814 Ext. 6 · zoning@PilesgroveNJ.org","Pilesgrove Township Fire Inspector for CO…, how to apply: Not published. The Township CO application says the smoke/carbon monoxide certificate is needed before the CO is issued, and its checklist includes a smoke/CO inspection. Ask the Zoning & Housing Office whether the Township fire inspector issues the smoke/CO certificate or whether the seller should apply to the NJ DCA.","NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire…: issued by NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (NJ DCA, state). Covers: Entire township (per the state LEA registry, state towns list and fire directory)","NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire… contact: Louis Kilmer, Bureau Chief, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement · 609-633-6106 · BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov","NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire…, apply: Fee depends on how many business days before closing you apply (more than 10, 4 to 10, under 4).","NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire…, how to apply: Apply online through the NJ DCA Fire Safety portal (Certificate of Smoke Alarm, Carbon Monoxide Alarm, and Secondary Power Source Identification Label Compliance). Pay by e-check or credit card before submitting; a valid email address is required. The certificate is emailed once the application is submitted, the fee is paid and any required inspections are done. Homes heated by electricity with no CO alarm requirement should also email BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 5/18/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","Smoke alarms must be UL listed, less than 10 years old and 10-year sealed battery units; wired or interconnected systems must stay hardwired and interconnected","CO alarms on every occupiable level including the basement, within 10 feet of any sleeping area","Homes with a generator, solar panels or battery backup need a warning label within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and the electric meter","The Township CO checklist still lists a fire extinguisher mounted in the kitchen","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire…: State smoke/CO certificate, applied more than 10 business days before closing","amount":"$45"},{"label":"NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire…: State smoke/CO certificate, applied 4 to 10 business days before closing","amount":"$90"},{"label":"NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire…: State smoke/CO certificate, closing less than 4 business days away","amount":"$161"}]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/230/Zoning-Housing$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Minutes/_02102026-32","label":"Official source (pilesgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Minutes/_02242026-33","label":"Official source (pilesgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/DocumentCenter/View/326/CO-Inspection-Checklist","label":"Official source (pilesgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pilesgrovenj.org/DocumentCenter/View/323/Smoke-Alarm-Info-Sheet-for-Co-Inspections","label":"Official source (pilesgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/_odata/firedistricts","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Resolution 26-027, Resolution Appointing Leroy Pierce as Fire Inspector for CO Requirements.$t$, $t$ae0f964e6f3cdfca966cb8055c427efdcfdb789e7eff49cc77fcc80640230038$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":18,"q_ok":14,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1710.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1710.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1711$t$, $t$Pittsgrove Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Continuing Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Housing/Zoning/Code Enforcement Office","Contact: Edward Ramsay, Housing/Zoning/Code Enforcement Official · 856/358-2300 ext 6029 · eramsay@pittsgrovetownship.com","Apply: Inspection fee is paid in advance. The application is void after 45 days.","How to apply: Fill in the Township of Pittsgrove Application and Continuing Certificate of Occupancy (mark \"Resale\", give the settlement date and the number of smoke detectors, CO detectors and extinguishers) and return it with the $40.00 inspection fee to the Housing/Zoning/Code Enforcement Office, 989 Centerton Road, Pittsgrove. The form records payment by check.","Smoke detectors in each bedroom, within 10 feet of bedroom areas and at least one per level including the basement and walk-up attic; battery units must be 10-year sealed","CO detectors within 10 feet of bedroom areas and kitchens, at least one per level including basements and walk-up attics","Fire extinguisher rated 2A:10BC, no more than 10 pounds, visibly mounted in the kitchen or within 10 feet of it toward an exit","911 post (4 x 4 inch, 6 feet, 2 feet in the ground) at the driveway entrance with 4-inch reflective numbers on each side","Tree limbs cut back at least 10 feet from the roof line","Handrails on stairways and stoops with 3 or more steps; guardrails on porches, decks and raised floors 30 inches or higher, spindles no more than 4 inches apart","No broken windows or doors, no holes in walls, no exterior damage or leaking roof","Switch plates and outlet covers in place, GFI outlets within 3 feet of kitchen and bathroom sinks, no bare wires, secure covered breaker panel","Working range with anti-tip device and other appliances working","Hot and cold running water without leaks, flushing toilets and working heat","Bathroom window or exhaust fan vented outside; water heater relief valve extension within 6 inches of the floor","Electric service wire and meter sound; no double-cylinder deadbolts on exterior doors","All code violations abated and all open construction, electrical, plumbing or fire permits closed","No rubbish or debris inside or out; all utilities on at the inspection","No more than 2 occupants per bedroom","Also: Open permits closed: All open construction, electrical, plumbing or fire permits must be closed out and all code violations abated.","Also: Utilities on: All utilities must be on at the time of inspection."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Continuing Certificate of Occupancy inspection (paid in advance)","amount":"$40.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection (payable before or at the re-inspection)","amount":"$15.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://web.archive.org/web/20240630050032/https://www.pittsgrovetownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/Application-and-Requirements-for-Continuing-Certificate-of-Occupancy-PDF.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.pittsgrovetownship.com/departments/housing-zoning-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240630050032/https://www.pittsgrovetownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/Application-and-Requirements-for-Continuing-Certificate-of-Occupancy-PDF.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240521134214/https://www.pittsgrovetownship.com/departments/housing-zoning-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Township of Pittsgrove Housing/Zoning/Code Enforcement Office APPLICATION and CONTINUING CERTIFICATE OF OCCUPANCY ... Resale, Rental, Other, Settlement/Occupancy Date ... NON-TRANSFERABLE APPLICATION VOID AFTER 45 DAYS$t$, $t$b1074f376581862ba72f9e309be6a73e5fe6d0a5eacc3ee93bc20a1246c12dd4$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":9,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1711.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1711.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1711$t$, $t$Pittsgrove Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Pittsgrove Township Bureau of Fire Safety (smoke detector compliance through the Pittsgrove Township Zoning Office) (town fire bureau)","Contact: Charles Hughes, Bureau of Fire Safety contact and Construction Code Official (Township directory); Fire Official in the state fire… · 856-358-2300 · chughes@pittsgrovetownship.com","How to apply: No separate smoke/CO certificate application or fee was found. The Township Continuing Certificate of Occupancy application records smoke detectors, CO detectors and the fire extinguisher, and the state directory names the Pittsgrove Township Zoning Office for smoke detector compliance. Ask the Housing/Zoning/Code Enforcement Office whether the CCO inspection also serves as the smoke/CO certificate.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 5/18/2026: Charles Hughes · (856) 207-2434 · smke10@aol.com","Township CCO smoke sheet (effective January 1, 2019): battery smoke detectors must be 10-year sealed battery units","Smoke detectors in each bedroom as well as on each level (Township CCO list)","CO detectors within 10 feet of bedroom areas and kitchens, one per level (Township CCO list)","Township CCO list still asks for a 2A:10BC fire extinguisher, no more than 10 pounds, mounted in or within 10 feet of the kitchen","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.pittsgrovetownship.com/departments/housing-zoning-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240712232618/https://www.pittsgrovetownship.com/departments/administration/township-directory/","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220704215736/https://pittsgrovetownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/Smoke-Detector-CCO.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$M Pittsgrove Township$t$, $t$c69489eb66037bdb9d6e4bb0cb5524ef6e8902c5fd0dc21f443b81d24d75bd76$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":9,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1711.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1711.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1712$t$, $t$Quinton Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Continued Occupancy$t$, $j$["Issued by: Housing Office (Department of Housing)","Contact: Robert Schmid, Housing Officer · 856-935-2325 Ext. 5 · zoning@quintonnj.com","Apply: Applications can be turned in any time with the fee; call during office hours to schedule the first inspection. Inspections are on Wednesday evenings.","How to apply: Fill in the Quinton Township Certificate of Continued Occupancy Application (Department of Housing, PO Box 65, Quinton, NJ 08072) and turn it in with the fee (the form records payment by check). Then call the Housing Office during office hours (Wednesdays 4 pm to 5:30 pm) to schedule the first inspection; inspections are held Wednesday evenings. Have the water test, septic certification and chimney certification ready before the certificate can be issued.","Water test meeting NJDEP and federal EPA chemical, bacteriological and gross alpha limits (not needed on public water)","Septic certification (not needed on public sewer)","Chimney certification for all fossil fuel systems","Fire extinguisher (Township packet includes the 2005 state extinguisher memo)","Carbon monoxide alarms","Smoke detectors","Electrical panel box labeled; 100 amp service","Corrections and re-inspections must be done before occupancy","Also: Water test: Water test meeting NJDEP and federal EPA chemical, bacteriological and gross alpha limits, unless on a public water system.","Also: Septic certification: Septic certification unless on public sewer; the Township posts a septic certification guideline and a list of Salem County Department of Health recognized septic inspectors.","Also: Chimney certification: Chimney certification for all fossil fuel systems."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of Continued Occupancy, initial inspection","amount":"$40.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$40.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.quintonnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/668/Certificate-Of-Occupancy-Application-PDF$t$, $t$https://www.quintonnj.com/204/Housing-Office$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.quintonnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/668/Certificate-Of-Occupancy-Application-PDF","label":"Official source (quintonnj.com)"},{"url":"https://www.quintonnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/669/Certificate-Of-Occupancy-Guideline-PDF","label":"Official source (quintonnj.com)"},{"url":"https://www.quintonnj.com/204/Housing-Office","label":"Official source (quintonnj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$CERTIFICATE OF CONTINUED OCCUPANCY APPLICATION QUINTON TOWNSHIP DEPARTMENT OF HOUSING ... OWNER/SELLER (CIRCLE ONE) ... BUYER/TENANT (CIRCLE ONE) ... PLEASE NOTE: CORRECTIONS AND REINSPECTIONS MUST BE MADE BEFORE OCCUPANCY.$t$, $t$42eabc83f7402dcb97004dc2c9feadf5f9cc454097d56446ea1c8708e7eece72$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":11,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":5},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1712.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1712.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1712$t$, $t$Quinton Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Not confirmed. Likely the Quinton Township Housing Office, which checks smoke detectors, CO alarms and the fire extinguisher for the Certificate of Continued Occupancy","Contact: Robert Schmid, Housing Officer · 856-935-2325 Ext. 5 · zoning@quintonnj.com","How to apply: No separate smoke/CO certificate application or fee is published. The Township Certificate of Continued Occupancy guideline requires smoke detectors, CO alarms and a fire extinguisher before the certificate is issued. The NJ DCA online smoke certificate application does not offer Quinton (the DCA marks it smoke-certificate exempt), so ask the Housing Office who issues the smoke/CO certificate for a sale.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 4/6/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","Township CCO guideline requires smoke detectors, carbon monoxide alarms and a fire extinguisher before the certificate is issued; the extinguisher sheet in the Township packet is a 2005 state memo (2A:10B:C, no more than 10 pounds, within 10 feet of the kitchen, top no more than 5 feet above the floor)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.quintonnj.com/204/Housing-Office$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.quintonnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/669/Certificate-Of-Occupancy-Guideline-PDF","label":"Official source (quintonnj.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/_odata/firedistricts","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.quintonnj.com/204/Housing-Office","label":"Official source (quintonnj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The following must be provided before a certificate of continued occupancy will be issued: ... Fire Extinguisher Attachment enclosed Carbon Monoxide Alarms Attachment enclosed Smoke Detectors Attachment enclosed$t$, $t$6660ff894a51216f83f9e542b970882a7b0744b8b9a7636935bda280d0986634$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":11,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":5},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1712.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1712.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1713$t$, $t$Salem$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy (CO) for home sales$t$, $j$["Issued by: City of Salem Department of Inspections & Permits","Contact: Sean M. Brown, MPA, Director of Housing and Economic Development (Housing Office); the CO form names only the Department of Inspections &… · 856-935-0372 · sbrown@cityofsalemnj.gov","How to apply: Fill in the City of Salem Certificate of Occupancy & Landlord Rental Registration Application, mark \"Sell property\" as the purpose, and submit it with payment to the City of Salem Department of Inspections & Permits, 125 West Broadway, Salem. The Tax Collector signs off that taxes are paid, and the owner certifies there are no outstanding municipal charges. Applications are not processed without payment and complete documents.","Also: Taxes and municipal charges paid: The Tax Collector signs off on the CO application, and the owner certifies there are no outstanding municipal charges, including real estate taxes, water/sewer, court fees or other assessments."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of Occupancy, initial inspection","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Reinspection","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Certificate of Occupancy (2026 packet; one free with a paid rental registration each year)","amount":"$50"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://cityofsalemnj.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/certificate-of-occupancy-application-1.pdf$t$, $t$https://cityofsalemnj.gov/construction-office/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://cityofsalemnj.gov/construction-office/","label":"Official source (cityofsalemnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://cityofsalemnj.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/certificate-of-occupancy-application-1.pdf","label":"Official source (cityofsalemnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://cityofsalemnj.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/COO_RENTAL-REG-APPLICATION_2026_Optimized.pdf","label":"Official source (cityofsalemnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://cityofsalemnj.gov/housing-office/","label":"Official source (cityofsalemnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://cityofsalemnj.gov/code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (cityofsalemnj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$CO inspections for existing structures including rental unit occupancy change and home sales; existing housing code violations; tall grass and zoning issues are handled by the City's Department of Inspections & Permits, not the Construction Office$t$, $t$fbf25aa2bef98bd49a57a4b187c300e9c31ec79ad4613007898498a6cb887ff8$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":14,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1713.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1713.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1713$t$, $t$Salem$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: NJ DCA Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (NJ DCA, state)","Contact: Louis Kilmer, Bureau Chief, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement · 609-633-6106 · BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov","Apply: Fee depends on how many business days before closing you apply (more than 10, 4 to 10, under 4).","How to apply: Apply online through the NJ DCA Fire Safety portal (Certificate of Smoke Alarm, Carbon Monoxide Alarm, and Secondary Power Source Identification Label Compliance). Pay by e-check or credit card before submitting; a valid email address is required. The certificate is emailed once the application is submitted, the fee is paid and any required inspections are done. Homes heated by electricity with no CO alarm requirement should also email BFCE_CSDCMAC@dca.nj.gov.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 6/25/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609)633-6132","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"State smoke/CO certificate, applied more than 10 business days before closing","amount":"$45"},{"label":"State smoke/CO certificate, applied 4 to 10 business days before closing","amount":"$90"},{"label":"State smoke/CO certificate, closing less than 4 business days away","amount":"$161"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/$t$, $t$https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/_odata/firedistricts","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$S Salem City$t$, $t$1353b75a6a0634651d36d321028d88ed2d762de5b3735099ce1970c061d881ef$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":14,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1713.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1713.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1714$t$, $t$Upper Pittsgrove Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Compliance (COC), also called Certificate of Occupancy; Pre-Occupancy Inspection for sales$t$, $j$["Issued by: Zoning Office / Housing Office (Zoning & Housing Official)","Contact: Tanya Timberman, Zoning & Housing Official · 856-358-8500 · zoningofficer@upperpittsgrovenj.org","How to apply: Fill in the Upper Pittsgrove Township Pre-Occupancy Application, SALES Only (revised 03/30/2026) and mail it with a check payable to Upper Pittsgrove Township to the Township Housing Office, or leave it in the drop box at the Municipal Building, 431 Route 77, Elmer. The Smoke/CO certificate is a separate $25 application to the Bureau of Fire Prevention. Zoning Office hours are Tuesday 10 a.m. to 11:30 a.m.","House numbers 5 inches high and visible from the street","GFI protected outlets within 6 feet of a water source and on all exterior outlets","Fire extinguisher mounted in the kitchen","Appliances installed properly and working, no extension cords; exhaust fan over the stove (ductless hood allowed) and anti-tip bracket on the stove","Adequate electric, heating and plumbing service; two separate outlets in each habitable room","Bathroom vented or with a working window","Screened window in each room; all windows working with locks; exterior doors and hardware working","Handrails on steps with more than 3 risers; rails around landings or porches 30 inches or higher","Water heater relief valve piped to within 6 inches of the floor; emergency shut-off at the top of the stairs for a basement heater","Pools over 125 square feet and 3 feet or higher need a fence at least 4 feet high with a self-latching gate","House free of insect infestation","Smoke/CO inspection must pass (separate Bureau of Fire Prevention certificate)","Private well homes must comply with the Private Well Testing Act before sale; homes on a cesspool or privy cannot be sold until it is replaced with an approved system","Also: Private well testing: Under the Private Well Testing Act (N.J.S.A. 58:12A-26), a home on a private well cannot be sold without complying with the Act.","Also: Cesspool or privy: N.J.A.C. 7:9A-3.16 bars the sale of a property served by a cesspool, privy, outhouse or pit toilet until it is replaced with an approved system."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Pre-Occupancy Inspection, sales","amount":"$25"},{"label":"Re-inspection (if needed)","amount":"$25"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Pre-Occupancy-SALES-Application.pdf$t$, $t$https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/zoning-and-construction/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/zoning-and-construction/","label":"Official source (upperpittsgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Pre-Occupancy-SALES-Application.pdf","label":"Official source (upperpittsgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/CO-Inspection-Checklist.pdf","label":"Official source (upperpittsgrovenj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$UPT ordinance requires a COC (Certificate of Compliance) on residential or commercial rental properties whenever occupants change; therefore, a new COC is also required prior to the sale of a property.$t$, $t$0a657e213b2f6aab939daeb33ae096b1dec7fc346e08b5be2ddb98a4a572b9d7$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":13,"q_ok":13,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1714.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1714.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1714$t$, $t$Upper Pittsgrove Township$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Township of Upper Pittsgrove Bureau of Fire Prevention (town fire bureau)","Contact: Tim O'Donnell, Fire & Safety Official and Smoke Detectors Inspector (Fire Official in the state fire directory) · 856-358-8500 · upperpittsgrovefm@outlook.com","Apply: Payment must be received before the inspection.","How to apply: Fill in the Township Certificate of Smoke/Carbon Monoxide Detector Compliance application and pay $25.00 by check or money order payable to the Upper Pittsgrove Bureau of Fire Prevention before the inspection. Questions go to upperpittsgrovefm@outlook.com or 856-358-8500.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 4/7/2025: Timothy J O'Donnell · (856) 358-8500","10-year sealed battery smoke alarms on every level (or hardwired where required); basement alarm at the bottom of the stairwell at ceiling level","A 10-year sealed smoke alarm in every bedroom (Township rule); hardwired alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","Smoke and CO alarms must be less than 10 years old and working","CO alarm in the hallway within 10 feet of all bedrooms","A low-voltage fire alarm system must be tested and certified by an alarm contractor before the inspection; bring the certificate","House numbers at least 4 inches high, contrasting color, permanently fixed and visible from the street","Homes with solar, a generator or battery storage need a permanent printed label (for example \"Caution: Multiple Sources of Power\") at the main electrical panel and the electric meter","The Township CO checklist still lists a fire extinguisher mounted in the kitchen","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of Smoke/Carbon Monoxide Detector Compliance inspection","amount":"$25.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection for a failed or no-show inspection (same as the initial inspection fee)","amount":"$25.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Smoke-and-CO-Application-Guidelines.pdf$t$, $t$https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/zoning-and-construction/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Smoke-and-CO-Application-Guidelines.pdf","label":"Official source (upperpittsgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Pre-Occupancy-SALES-Application.pdf","label":"Official source (upperpittsgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/zoning-and-construction/","label":"Official source (upperpittsgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://upperpittsgrovenj.org/emergency-services/","label":"Official source (upperpittsgrovenj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$M Upper Pittsgrove Township$t$, $t$a7f7a692982c7e4455b2f5a2c3df21dbd96fb492e233e4122b361163ddcf5af1$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":13,"q_ok":13,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1714.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1714.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1715$t$, $t$Woodstown Borough$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Continuing Certificate of Occupancy (Residential CO)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Housing Official (Housing/Code Enforcement)","Contact: Ed Ramsay, Housing Official · 856-769-2200 ext. 112 · housing@historicwoodstown.org","Apply: Inspection fee is paid in advance. The application is void after 45 days.","How to apply: Fill in the Borough of Woodstown Application and Continuing Certificate of Occupancy (mark \"Resale\", give the settlement date and the number of smoke detectors, CO detectors and extinguishers) and pay the $100.00 inspection fee in advance by cash, check or money order at the Housing Office, 2nd floor, Borough Hall, 25 West Avenue. Housing Official hours are Mondays 9a to 12p and Thursdays 1p to 3p.","10-year sealed battery smoke detectors in each bedroom, within 10 feet of bedroom areas and the kitchen, and at least one per level including the basement and walk-up attic","CO detectors within 10 feet of bedroom areas and kitchens, at least one per level including basements and walk-up attics","Fire extinguisher rated 1A:10BC or 2A:10BC, no more than 10 pounds, visibly mounted in the kitchen or within 10 feet of it toward an exit","4-inch house letters and numbers visible from the street; tree limbs cut back at least 10 feet from the roof line","Handrails on stairways and stoops with 3 or more steps; guardrails on porches, balconies, raised floors and decks 30 inches or higher, spindles no more than 4 inches apart","No broken windows or doors, no holes in walls or ceilings, no structural or exterior damage, no leaking roof","Switch plates and outlet covers in place, GFI outlets within 3 feet of kitchen and bathroom sinks, light fixtures in place with no bare wires, secure covered breaker panel","Working range with anti-tip device and other appliances working; working heat (and air conditioning if present)","Hot and cold running water without leaks and flushing toilets; bathroom window or exhaust fan vented outside","Water heater relief valve extension within 6 inches of the floor (not closer than 2 inches); electric service wire and meter sound","No double-cylinder deadbolts on exterior doors; fire-rated door between an attached garage and the house","Sidewalks and driveways in good order without cracks or raised areas; pools, spas and hot tubs clean with proper security fencing","All code violations abated, all open construction permits closed, no rubbish or debris, all utilities on at the inspection","No more than 2 occupants per bedroom","Resale homes need a heater and chimney certification from a qualified contractor","Also: Heater and chimney certification: All resale properties must have a heater and chimney certification from a qualified contractor.","Also: Open permits closed: All open construction permits must be closed out and all code violations abated."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Continuing Certificate of Occupancy inspection (paid in advance by cash, check or money order)","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://historicwoodstown.org/vertical/sites/%7BE7F6D332-DC61-417D-8E31-6054B23067AE%7D/uploads/CO_App__Checklist.pdf$t$, $t$https://historicwoodstown.org/index.asp?SEC=B628895B-7233-4520-9082-7909784D2712&Type=B_BASIC$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://historicwoodstown.org/index.asp?SEC=B628895B-7233-4520-9082-7909784D2712&Type=B_BASIC","label":"Official source (historicwoodstown.org)"},{"url":"https://historicwoodstown.org/vertical/sites/%7BE7F6D332-DC61-417D-8E31-6054B23067AE%7D/uploads/CO_App__Checklist.pdf","label":"Official source (historicwoodstown.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The Housing Official is responsible for Residential Certificate of Occupancy (CO). If a home within the Borough sells, it is required that a new CO is completed and filed at Borough Hall.$t$, $t$fb7491bcc4b8a9ac3b68420c107667190c374f733fd6bd52c520acb4afda2cb1$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":1,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":1,"quotes":10,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":5},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1715.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1715.json$t$, true),
  ($t$1715$t$, $t$Woodstown Borough$t$, $t$SALEM$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Woodstown Borough Housing Office (Housing/Code Enforcement), listed by the state for smoke detector compliance","Contact: Ed Ramsay, Housing Official · 856-769-2200 ext. 112 · housing@historicwoodstown.org","How to apply: No separate smoke/CO certificate application or fee is published. The Borough Continuing Certificate of Occupancy inspection ($100.00) records and checks smoke detectors, CO detectors and the fire extinguisher. The NJ DCA online smoke certificate application does not offer Woodstown (the DCA marks it smoke-certificate exempt). Ask the Housing Official whether the CCO serves as the smoke/CO certificate.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 5/18/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609) 633-6132","Borough CCO list: 10-year sealed battery smoke detectors in each bedroom, within 10 feet of bedroom areas and the kitchen, and one per level including basement and walk-up attic","Borough CCO list: CO detectors within 10 feet of bedroom areas and kitchens, one per level","Borough CCO list (revised 12-18-25) still requires a 1A:10BC or 2A:10BC fire extinguisher, no more than 10 pounds, mounted in or within 10 feet of the kitchen","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://historicwoodstown.org/index.asp?SEC=B628895B-7233-4520-9082-7909784D2712&Type=B_BASIC$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/_odata/firedistricts","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/","label":"Official source (firesolutions.dca.nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://historicwoodstown.org/vertical/sites/%7BE7F6D332-DC61-417D-8E31-6054B23067AE%7D/uploads/CO_App__Checklist.pdf","label":"Official source (historicwoodstown.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$LEAID: 1715-999 Enf Auth. State Fire Official Louis Kilmer Phone (609) 633-6132 Addr: 25 West Avenue - PO Box 286 Woodstown NJ 08098 Phone (856) 769-1375 ... Woodstown Boro Housing$t$, $t$0ad699eccc87e15dbc90aae9134b0d3643d4278961753b01b33267596e36b8df$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-10-01","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":1,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":1,"quotes":10,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":5},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1715.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-10-01. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/1715.json$t$, true)
